SSC-CGL-2021-T1-GA-EN-11280,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-20,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"The difference between compound interest compounded annually and simple interest on a certain sum at a rate of 15% per annum for 2 years is ₹1,944. Find the compound interest compounded annually (in ₹) on the same sum for the same period at a rate of 10% per annum.","20,500","27,216","18,060","18,144",D,"18,144","For 2 years, CI − SI = P(r/100)². So P × (0.15)² = 1944 → P = 1944 ÷ 0.0225 = 86,400. CI at 10% for 2 years = 86,400 × (1.1² − 1) = 86,400 × 0.21 = 18,144. Answer: 18,144",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-20 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-20-s1
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-GA-EN-11281,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-20,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"The tops of two poles of heights 18 m and 30.5 m are connected by a wire. If the wire makes an angle of 30° with the horizontal, what is the length (in m) of the wire?",28,36,20,25,D,25,The vertical gap between the tops is 30.5 − 18 = 12.5 m. This gap is the side opposite the 30° angle in a right triangle whose hypotenuse is the wire. Wire = 12.5 ÷ sin 30° = 12.5 × 2 = 25 m. Answer: 25,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-20 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-20-s1
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-GA-EN-11282,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-20,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"A college hostel mess has provisions for 25 days for 350 boys. At the end of 10 days, when some boys were shifted to another hostel, it was found that now the provisions will last for 21 more days. How many boys were shifted to another hostel?",110,92,100,98,C,100,"After 10 days, the food left is enough for 350 boys for 15 days = 5,250 boy-days. It now lasts 21 days, so the boys remaining = 5,250 ÷ 21 = 250. Boys shifted = 350 − 250 = 100. Answer: 100",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-20 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-20-s1
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-GA-EN-11283,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-20,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"The following pie chart shows the distribution of percentage of a certain corporate office employees in various age-groups. Total number of employees of the corporate office = 2500 Study the chart carefully and answer the question that follows. (Data from the official pie chart “Percentage distribution of a certain corporate office employees by their ages”, shown as a table.) Age group Percentage of employees 19 to 28 years 20% 28+ to 38 years 25% 38+ to 48 years 30% 48+ to 58 years 15% 58+ years and above 10% The number of the corporate office employees of age group of 38+ years and above is how much percentage more than that of 28+ to 38 years?",150%,20%,120%,80%,C,120%,Employees aged 38+ and above = 30% + 15% + 10% = 55%; employees aged 28+ to 38 = 25%. 55% is (55 − 25)/25 × 100 = 120% more than 25%. (The total of 2500 is not needed.) Answer: 120%,Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-20 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-20-s1
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-GA-EN-11284,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-20,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"In a right triangle ABC, right angled at B, altitude BD is drawn to the hypotenuse AC of the triangle. If AD = 6 cm, CD = 5 cm, then find the value of AB 2 + BD 2 (in cm).",30,36,96,66,C,96,In a right triangle the altitude to the hypotenuse gives BD² = AD × CD = 6 × 5 = 30 and AB² = AD × AC = 6 × 11 = 66. AB² + BD² = 66 + 30 = 96. Answer: 96,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-20 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-20-s1
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-GA-EN-11285,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-20,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"The inner circumference of a circular path enclosed between two concentric circles is 264 m. The uniform width of the circular path is 3 m. What is the area (in m 2 , to the nearest whole number) of the path? (Take π = 22/7)",696,756,820,948,C,820,"Inner radius r = 264 ÷ (2 × 22/7) = 42 m, so outer radius R = 45 m. Area of path = (22/7)(R² − r²) = (22/7)(2025 − 1764) = (22/7) × 261 ≈ 820.3 → 820 m². Answer: 820",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-20 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-20-s1
