SSC-CGL-2021-T1-GA-EN-11575,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,A solid cone of radius 7 cm and height 7 cm was melted along with two solid spheres of radius 7 cm each to form a solid cylinder of radius 7 cm. What is the curved surface area (in cm 2 ) of the cylinder? (Use π = 22/7),2196,924,880,482,B,924,"Total volume = (1/3)π(7²)(7) + 2 × (4/3)π(7³) = π × 7³ × (1/3 + 8/3) = 3 × 343π = 1029π. Cylinder: π × 7² × h = 1029π, so h = 21 cm. Curved surface area = 2πrh = 2 × 22/7 × 7 × 21 = 924 cm². Answer: 924",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-GA-EN-11576,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"A tyre has two punctures. The first puncture alone would have made the tyre flat in 45 minutes, and the second puncture alone would have done it in 90 minutes. If air leaks out at a constant rate, then how long (in minutes) does it take for both the punctures together to make the tyre flat?",40,45,15,30,D,30,Per minute the two punctures let out 1/45 + 1/90 = 3/90 = 1/30 of the air. So together they take 30 minutes. Answer: 30,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-GA-EN-11577,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"A and B entered into a partnership with investments in the ratio 3 : 5. After a few months, A withdrew and collected back his money. At the end of the year, they received profit in the ratio 2 : 5. After how many months did A withdraw?",7,9,6,8,D,8,"If A stayed t months: (3 × t) : (5 × 12) = 2 : 5. 15t = 120, so t = 8 months. Answer: 8",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-GA-EN-11578,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"If (sin 2 θ − 3sinθ + 2)/cos 2 θ = 1, where 0° < θ < 90°, then what is the value of (cos2θ − sin3θ + cosec2θ)?",(−3 + 4√3)/6,(3 + 4√3)/6,(3 − 4√3)/6,(−3 − 4√3)/6,A,(−3 + 4√3)/6,"sin²θ − 3sinθ + 2 = cos²θ = 1 − sin²θ gives 2sin²θ − 3sinθ + 1 = 0, so sinθ = 1/2 or 1. As θ < 90°, θ = 30°. cos60° − sin90° + cosec60° = 1/2 − 1 + 2/√3 = −1/2 + 2√3/3 = (−3 + 4√3)/6. Answer: (−3 + 4√3)/6",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-GA-EN-11579,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"In the month of March, Dalip earned on an average ₹501 per day. For the first 18 days, his average earning was ₹495 and, for the last 15 days, his average earning was ₹505. On 18 th March, he earned ₹50 more than that earned on 17 th March. How much (in ₹) did he earn on 18 th March?",501,502,500,498,B,502,"March total = 31 × 501 = ₹15,531. First 18 days = 18 × 495 = ₹8,910; last 15 days (17th–31st) = 15 × 505 = ₹7,575. The 17th and 18th are counted twice: 8,910 + 7,575 − 15,531 = ₹954. If the 17th earned x, then x + (x + 50) = 954, so x = 452 and the 18th = ₹502. Answer: 502",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
