SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11609,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,"If a 2 + b 2 = 65 and ab = 8, a > b > 0, then find the value of a 2 − b 2 .",63,72,65,60,A,63,"(a + b)² = 65 + 16 = 81, so a + b = 9; (a − b)² = 65 − 16 = 49, so a − b = 7. a² − b² = (a + b)(a − b) = 63. Answer: 63",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11610,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"The given pie chart shows the percentage of students in five schools and the table shows the ratio of boys and girls in each school. Study the pie chart and table and answer the question that follows. (Data from the official pie chart, shown as a table.) School Percentage of students A 28% B 15% C 24% D 18% E 15% The below table shows the ratio of girls and boys in the given five schools. School Girls : Boys A 3 : 4 B 2 : 3 C 5 : 3 D 1 : 2 E 4 : 1 The number of girls in school D is what percentage less than the number of boys in school B (correct to the nearest integer)?",33%,27%,35%,19%,A,33%,Take the total as 100 units. Girls in D = 18 × 1/3 = 6; boys in B = 15 × 3/5 = 9. (9 − 6)/9 × 100 = 33.3% ≈ 33%. Answer: 33%,Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11611,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Algebra,English,"If x 4 − 79x 2 + 1 = 0, then a value of x + x −1 can be:",5,7,9,8,C,9,"Divide by x²: x² + 1/x² = 79. (x + 1/x)² = x² + 1/x² + 2 = 81, so x + 1/x = 9 (or −9). Answer: 9",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11612,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Algebra,English,"If a nine-digit number 485x3678y is divisible by 72, then for the smallest value of x, the value of (2y − 3x) is:",11,8,9,6,B,8,"Divisible by 8: the last three digits 78y must be divisible by 8, so y = 4 (784 = 8 × 98). Divisible by 9: the digit sum 4 + 8 + 5 + x + 3 + 6 + 7 + 8 + 4 = 45 + x must be a multiple of 9, so the smallest x is 0. 2y − 3x = 8 − 0 = 8. Answer: 8",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11613,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"The following bar graph shows the total number of youth (in lakhs) and the number of employed youth (in lakhs) in 5 states A, B, C, D and E. (Data from the official chart, shown as a table.) State Youth (lakhs) Employed youth (lakhs) A 12 10.5 B 8 7 C 11.5 10 D 10 7.5 E 9 8 How many youth (in lakhs) are unemployed in states B and D taken together?",3.5,3.25,4.25,4.5,A,3.5,Unemployed = youth − employed: B = 8 − 7 = 1 lakh; D = 10 − 7.5 = 2.5 lakh. Together = 3.5 lakh. Answer: 3.5,Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11614,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"What is the compound interest (in ₹) on a sum of ₹62,500 for 2 years at 12% p.a., if the interest is compounded 8-monthly?","18,342","13,428","16,548","16,232",D,"16,232","8 months is 2/3 of a year: rate per period = 12 × 2/3 = 8%, and 2 years = 3 periods. Amount = 62,500 × 1.08³ = 62,500 × 1.259712 = ₹78,732; CI = 78,732 − 62,500 = ₹16,232. Answer: 16,232",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11615,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Geometry,English,"AB is the diameter of a circle with centre O. C and D are two points on the circle on either side of AB, such that ∠CAB = 52° and ∠ABD = 47°. What is the difference (in degrees) between the measures of ∠CAD and ∠CBD?",20,10,25,15,B,10,"Angles in a semicircle: ∠ACB = ∠ADB = 90°, so ∠CBA = 38° and ∠DAB = 43°. ∠CAD = 52° + 43° = 95° and ∠CBD = 38° + 47° = 85°; the difference is 10°. Answer: 10",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11616,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Simple & Compound Interest,English,"Study the graph and answer the question that follows. (Data from the official histogram, shown as a table.) Daily wages (in ₹) Number of workers 400–450 30 450–500 45 500–550 65 550–600 60 600–650 55 650–700 35 What is the ratio of the total number of workers whose daily wages are less than ₹450 to the total number of workers whose daily wages are ₹650 and above?",6 : 7,3 : 5,5 : 7,1 : 4,A,6 : 7,Wages below ₹450: 30 workers. Wages ₹650 and above: 35 workers. 30 : 35 = 6 : 7. Answer: 6 : 7,Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11617,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"The breakup of the total number of employees of a company working in different offices (A to E), in degrees, is given in the pie chart. Total number of employees = 2400. (Data from the official pie chart, shown as a table.) Office Central angle A 126° B 18° C 54° D 90° E 72° If the percentage of male employees in office C is 20% and that of female employees in E is 40%, then what is the ratio of the numbers of female employees in E to that of female employees in C?",3 : 8,3 : 2,5 : 4,2 : 3,D,2 : 3,"C = 54/360 × 2400 = 360 employees, of whom 80% = 288 are female. E = 72/360 × 2400 = 480 employees, of whom 40% = 192 are female. 192 : 288 = 2 : 3. Answer: 2 : 3",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11618,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Geometry,English,"AB and CD are two chords in a circle with centre O and AD is the diameter. When produced, AB and CD meet at the point P. If ∠DAP = 27°, ∠APD = 35°, then what is the measure (in degrees) of ∠DBC?",28,32,30,26,A,28,"AD is a diameter, so ∠ACD = 90°, and hence ∠ACP = 90° (P lies on line DC). In ΔACP, ∠CAP = 90° − 35° = 55°, so ∠DAC = 55° − 27° = 28°. ∠DBC and ∠DAC stand on the same arc DC, so ∠DBC = 28°. Answer: 28",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11619,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A shopkeeper marks an article x % above the cost price and sells it by allowing 30% discount on the marked price. If there is a loss of 4.8%, then what is the value of x ?",36,40,30,35,A,36,"With CP = 100, SP = 95.2, and SP = 0.7 × MP, so MP = 95.2/0.7 = 136. So the mark-up is x = 36%. Answer: 36",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
SSC-CGL-2021-T1-QA-EN-11620,SSC CGL,2021,Tier 1,2022-04-21,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"Two trains are running on parallel tracks in the same direction at the speed of 80 km/h and 90 km/h, respectively. The trains crossed each other in 3 minutes. If the length of one train is 230 m, then what is the length (in m) of the other train?",230,270,250,300,B,270,"Relative speed = 10 km/h = 10,000/60 m per minute, so in 3 minutes the faster train gains 500 m. Sum of lengths = 500 m, so the other train is 500 − 230 = 270 m. Answer: 270",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2021 Tier 1 (2022-04-21 Shift 2),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2021-2022-04-21-s2
