SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-11958,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"A # B means ‘A is the sister of B’ A @ B means ‘A is the daughter of B’ A & B means ‘A is the husband of B’ A % B means ‘A is the father of B’ If A % B & C # D @ E, then how is B related to E?",Father,Son,Brother,Son-in-law,D,Son-in-law,"A % B: A is B’s father. B & C: B is C’s husband. C # D: C is D’s sister. D @ E: D is E’s daughter, so C is also E’s daughter. B is the husband of E’s daughter, i.e. E’s son-in-law. Answer: Son-in-law",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
