SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-11983,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"Two circles touch each other externally at P. AB is a direct common tangent to the two circles, A and B are points of contact, and ∠PAB = 40° . The measure of ∠ABP is:",45°,50°,40°,55°,B,50°,"For two circles touching externally, the direct common tangent subtends a right angle at the point of contact: ∠APB = 90°. So ∠ABP = 180° − 90° − 40° = 50°. Answer: 50°",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
