SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-11989,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Number System & Divisibility,English,The HCF of two numbers is 12. Which one of the following can never be their LCM?,72,84,60,90,D,90,"The LCM is always a multiple of the HCF. 72, 84 and 60 are multiples of 12, but 90 is not, so 90 can never be the LCM. Answer: 90",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-11990,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"In a right-angled triangle PQR, right-angled at Q, the length of the side PR is 17 units, length of the base QR is 8 units, and length of the side PQ is 15 units. If ∠RPQ = α, then sinα + cosα is:",18/17,21/17,15/17,23/17,D,23/17,"For angle α at P, the opposite side is QR = 8 and the adjacent side is PQ = 15, with hypotenuse PR = 17. sin α + cos α = 8/17 + 15/17 = 23/17. Answer: 23/17",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-11991,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Geometry,English,Radius of a circle is 10 cm. Angle made by chord AB at the centre of this circle is 60 degree. What is the length of this chord?,30 cm,20 cm,40 cm,10 cm,D,10 cm,"OA = OB = 10 cm and ∠AOB = 60°, so triangle AOB is equilateral. Hence AB = 10 cm. Answer: 10 cm",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-11992,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"₹2,500, when invested for 8 years at a given rate of simple interest per year, amounted to ₹3,725 on maturity. What was the rate of simple interest that was paid per annum?",6.25%,6%,5.875%,6.125%,D,6.125%,"SI = 3725 − 2500 = ₹1,225. Rate = (1225 × 100)/(2500 × 8) = 6.125%. Answer: 6.125%",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-11993,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Average & Statistics,English,"The batting average for 27 innings of a cricket player is 47 runs. His highest score in an innings exceeds his lowest score by 157 runs. If these two innings are excluded, the average score of the remaining 25 innings is 42 runs. Find his highest score in an innings.",174,186,188,176,C,188,Total of 27 innings = 27 × 47 = 1269; total of the other 25 = 25 × 42 = 1050. So highest + lowest = 219 and highest − lowest = 157. Highest = (219 + 157)/2 = 188. Answer: 188,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-11994,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"The pie chart given below shows the number of truck sold by 8 different companies. The total number of truck sold by all these 8 companies are 4000. Number of truck sold by a particular company is shown as a percent of total number of truck sold by all these 8 companies. (Data from the official chart, shown as a table.) Company Percentage of trucks sold A 13% B 27% C 18% D 12% E 3% F 7% G 6% H 14% The number of trucks sold by B, C, F and H is how much percent less than the number of trucks sold by all these 8 companies?",34 percent,14 percent,46 percent,22 percent,A,34 percent,B + C + F + H = 27% + 18% + 7% + 14% = 66% of the total. So these four sold 100 − 66 = 34 percent less than all eight companies together. Answer: 34 percent,Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-11995,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Geometry,English,The circumference of the two circles is 198 cm and 352 cm respectively. What is the difference between their radii?,16.5 cm,45 cm,24.5 cm,49.5 cm,C,24.5 cm,r = C/(2π). r₁ = 198 × 7/44 = 31.5 cm and r₂ = 352 × 7/44 = 56 cm. Difference = 56 − 31.5 = 24.5 cm. Answer: 24.5 cm,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-11996,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,The value of tan 2 θ + cot 2 θ − sec 2 θ cosec 2 θ is:,0,1/2,2,−2,D,−2,sec²θ cosec²θ = sec²θ + cosec²θ = (1 + tan²θ) + (1 + cot²θ). So tan²θ + cot²θ − sec²θ cosec²θ = −2. Answer: −2,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-11997,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Simple & Compound Interest,English,"Select the most appropriate option to fill in the blank. The angles are equal, consequently the sides are _____________.",smaller,larger,equal,unequal,C,equal,"“Consequently” shows a result: because the angles are equal, the sides are also equal. Answer: equal",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
