SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-11999,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Data Interpretation,English,Select the correct active form of the given sentence. Has the villa been occupied by them?,Had they occupied the villa?,Have they occupied the villa?,Do they occupied the villa?,Did they occupied the villa?,B,Have they occupied the villa?,"“Has … been occupied” is present perfect passive, so the active is present perfect: “Have they occupied the villa?” Answer: Have they occupied the villa?",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12000,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Time, Work & Pipes",English,"Select the correct indirect form of the given sentence. She said, “I am in no mood to work now.”",She said that she has been in no mood to work then.,She said that she was in no mood to work then.,She said that she was in no mood to work now.,She said that she has been in no mood to work now.,B,She said that she was in no mood to work then.,In indirect speech “I am” becomes “she was” (tense backshift) and “now” becomes “then”: “She said that she was in no mood to work then.” Answer: She said that she was in no mood to work then.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12001,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-01,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,"Sentences of a paragraph are given below in jumbled order. Arrange the sentences in the correct order to form a meaningful and coherent paragraph. A. When this extra water vapour condenses into precipitation, it results in heavier rain — or, if it’s cold enough, heavier snow. B. The atmosphere can store an additional 4% of water vapour for every additional 1°F of warming. C. More water evaporates from soils, plants, lakes and seas as the atmosphere warms. D. One of the most obvious indications of climate change is heavier rainfall.",BCAD,CBDA,ACDB,DCBA,D,DCBA,"D introduces the idea (heavier rainfall as a sign of climate change), C explains that warming increases evaporation, B adds how much extra vapour the air holds, and A says this vapour falls as heavier rain or snow: DCBA. Answer: DCBA",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-01 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-01-s1
