SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12371,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-08,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"If sec x – cos x = 4, then what will be the value of (1 + cos²x)/cos x?",2√5,9/4,√5,1/4,A,2√5,"sec x − cos x = 4. Required value = (1 + cos²x)/cos x = sec x + cos x. (sec x + cos x)² = (sec x − cos x)² + 4 sec x cos x = 16 + 4 = 20, so the value is √20 = 2√5. Answer: 2√5",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-08 Shift 3),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-08-s3
