SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12374,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-08,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,"If abc = 5, what is the value of (1/(1 + a + b⁻¹) + 1/(1 + b + 5c⁻¹) + 1/(1 + c/5 + a⁻¹))?",(a + b + c),1,1/5,5,B,1,Since abc = 5: 5c⁻¹ = ab and c/5 = 1/(ab). First term = b/(b + ab + 1); second = 1/(1 + b + ab); third (multiply by ab) = ab/(ab + 1 + b). Sum = (b + 1 + ab)/(1 + b + ab) = 1. Answer: 1,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-08 Shift 3),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-08-s3
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12375,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-08,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"Study the given graph and table and answer the following question. Data of different states regarding population of states in the year 1998 States Percentage of total population Arunachal Pradesh 25% Madhya Pradesh 20% Delhi 8% Goa 12% Bihar 11% Uttar Pradesh 15% Tamil Nadu 9% (Data from the official chart, shown as a table.) Total population of the given states = 32760000 Sex and literacy wise Population Ratio States Sex: M Sex: F Literate Illiterate Arunachal Pradesh 5 3 2 7 Madhya Pradesh 3 1 1 4 Delhi 2 3 2 1 Goa 3 5 3 2 Bihar 3 4 4 1 Uttar Pradesh 3 2 7 2 Tamil Nadu 3 4 9 4 What was the ratio of the number of females in Arunachal Pradesh to the number of females in Uttar Pradesh?",16 : 25,21 : 50,50 : 21,25 : 16,D,25 : 16,Females in Arunachal Pradesh = 25% × 3/8 of the total; in Uttar Pradesh = 15% × 2/5 of the total. Ratio = (25 × 3/8) : (15 × 2/5) = 75/8 : 6 = 75 : 48 = 25 : 16. Answer: 25 : 16,Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-08 Shift 3),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-08-s3
