SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GA-EN-12430,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"Arjun, Balaji and Charan are running in a 1000 m race. Arjun beat Balaji by 100 m and Balaji beat Charan by 100 m. In the next 1000 m race (speeds being the same as before), Balaji gives Charan a start of 100 m and Arjun gives Balaji a start of 100 m. Find the distance by which the winner is ahead of the person just behind him.",100 m,40 m,20 m,30 m,C,20 m,"From the first race, speeds A : B = 1000 : 900 = 10 : 9 and B : C = 10 : 9, so A : B : C = 100 : 90 : 81. SSC’s answer reads the start as extra distance for the giver: Arjun runs 1200 m, Balaji 1100 m and Charan 1000 m. Arjun finishes in 12 units; in that time Balaji covers 90 × 12 = 1080 m, i.e. he is 20 m behind (Charan covers 972 of 1000 m). If instead Balaji starts 100 m ahead of Arjun and Charan 100 m ahead of Balaji on a 1000 m course, Charan wins and Arjun and Balaji finish together about 11 m behind him. Answer: 20 m",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GA-EN-12431,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"Ramesh buys a table and a chair for Rs.3,900. He sells the table at a profit of 8% and the chair at a profit of 16%. He makes a profit of Rs.540. What is the difference between the original prices of the table and the chair?","Rs.2,000","Rs.1,800","Rs.1,700","Rs.1,900",B,"Rs.1,800","Let the table cost x; the chair costs 3900 − x. Profit: 0.08x + 0.16(3900 − x) = 540 → 624 − 0.08x = 540 → x = 1050. Table = Rs.1,050, chair = Rs.2,850; difference = Rs.1,800. Answer: Rs.1,800",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GA-EN-12432,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,The table given below shows the number of salesmen in 5 companies. Company Salesmen J 45 K 20 L 40 M 15 N 25 The number of salesmen in J is what percentage of the number of salesmen in K?,250 percent,125 percent,150 percent,225 percent,D,225 percent,J has 45 salesmen and K has 20. 45 ÷ 20 × 100 = 225%. Answer: 225 percent,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GA-EN-12433,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"The salaries of Rida and Riya are in the ratio 3 : 5 respectively. If the salary of each is increased by Rs.5,000, the new ratio becomes 5 : 7. What is Riya’s present salary?","Rs.7,500","Rs.12,500","Rs.10,000","Rs.2,500",B,"Rs.12,500","Let the salaries be 3x and 5x. (3x + 5000) : (5x + 5000) = 5 : 7 → 21x + 35000 = 25x + 25000 → x = 2500. Riya’s present salary = 5 × 2500 = Rs.12,500. Answer: Rs.12,500",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GA-EN-12434,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,The table given below shows the number of working days of a company in 5 years. Year Working days P 110 Q 310 R 160 S 60 T 210 What is the ratio of the number of working days in year R to the number of working days in year T?,21 : 17,16 : 21,21 : 16,15 : 22,B,16 : 21,"Working days: R = 160, T = 210. 160 : 210 = 16 : 21. Answer: 16 : 21",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12435,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,Three of the following four letter-clusters are alike in a certain way and thus form a group. Which letter-cluster does not belong to that group?,PONM,EDCB,SRQP,BYXW,D,BYXW,"PONM, EDCB and SRQP are four consecutive letters in reverse alphabetical order. BYXW breaks the pattern: B is followed by Y, not A. It is the odd one. Answer: BYXW",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12436,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,Select the option that is related to the fifth letter-cluster in exactly the same way as the second letter-cluster is related to the first letter-cluster and the fourth letter-cluster is related to the third letter-cluster. ACCUSED : UCCASDE :: FACTORY : TCAFOYR :: DYNAMIC : ?,ANYDMCI,DNYMACI,YNMICAD,DANYMIC,A,ANYDMCI,"ACCUSED → UCCASDE: the first four letters are reversed (ACCU → UCCA), the 5th stays (S) and the last two are reversed (ED → DE). FACTORY → TCAF + O + YR follows the same rule. DYNAMIC → DYNA reversed = ANYD, M stays, IC reversed = CI → ANYDMCI. Answer: ANYDMCI",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12437,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Select the set in which the numbers are related in the same way as are the numbers of the following sets. (NOTE: Operations should be performed on the whole numbers, without breaking down the numbers into their constituent digits. For example, 13 – operations on 13 such as adding/subtracting/multiplying etc. can be performed. Breaking down 13 into 1 and 3 and then performing mathematical operations on 1 and 3 is not allowed.) (16, 7, 81) (24, 16, 64)","(37, 25, 100)","(21, 19, 8)","(48, 39, 18)","(13, 7, 36)",D,"(13, 7, 36)","Rule: third number = (first − second)². (16 − 7)² = 81 and (24 − 16)² = 64. (13 − 7)² = 6² = 36 fits. The others fail: (37 − 25)² = 144, (21 − 19)² = 4, (48 − 39)² = 81. Answer: (13, 7, 36)",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
