SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12441,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Mathematical Operations,English,Which two numbers and which two signs need to be interchanged to balance the given equation? 28 + 7 × 10 ÷ 5 − 20 = 5,"7 and 28, × and ÷","5 and 20, − and ÷","5 and 10, + and ÷","10 and 20, × and +",C,"5 and 10, + and ÷","SSC’s option: interchange 5 and 10 and the signs + and ÷: 28 ÷ 7 × 5 + 10 − 20 = 4 × 5 + 10 − 20 = 10. This balances only if the 5 on the right-hand side is also read as 10 (i.e. every 5 and 10 interchanged). Checking the other options: (1) 7 + 28 ÷ 10 × 5 − 20 = 1, (2) 28 + 7 × 10 − 20 ÷ 5 = 94, (4) 28 × 7 + 20 ÷ 5 − 10 = 190 — none gives 5. Answer: 5 and 10, + and ÷",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
