SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12447,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Coding & Decoding,English,"In a certain code language, 'COMMUNITY' is written as 'YITUNMCOM' and 'AUTHORITY' is written as 'YITORHAUT'. How will 'ISOLATION' be written in that language?",NIOATLIOS,NIAOTLISO,NIOATLISO,NIOATILSO,C,NIOATLISO,"Split the word into three blocks: COM | MUN | ITY. The blocks are written in reverse order; the last block has its last letter moved to the front (ITY → YIT), the middle block has its first letter moved to the end (MUN → UNM), and the first block is unchanged: YIT UNM COM. AUTHORITY → YIT ORH AUT confirms it. ISOLATION = ISO | LAT | ION → NIO ATL ISO = NIOATLISO. Answer: NIOATLISO",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12448,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Syllogism & Statements,English,"Read the given statements and conclusions carefully. Assuming that the information given in the statements is true, even if it appears to be at variance with commonly known facts, decide which of the given conclusions logically follow(s) from the statement(s). Statements: Some pencils are rods. No rod is a door. All balls are rods. Conclusions: I. Some pencils are likely to be balls. II. No ball is a door. III. All rods are balls. IV. No pencil is a door.",Only conclusions II and III follow,"Only conclusions I, II and IV follow",Only conclusions I and II follow,Only conclusion I follows,C,Only conclusions I and II follow,"All balls are rods and no rod is a door, so no ball is a door: II follows. Pencils overlap rods, and balls lie inside rods, so pencils being balls is possible: I follows. Only some rods are known to be balls (III fails), and pencils that are not rods may be doors (IV fails). Answer: Only conclusions I and II follow",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
