SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12465,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Geometry,English,"ΔABC ~ ΔDEF and the perimeters of these triangles are 32 cm and 12 cm respectively. If DE = 6 cm, then what will be the length of AB?",12 cm,14 cm,18 cm,16 cm,D,16 cm,"In similar triangles, corresponding sides are in the ratio of the perimeters: AB : DE = 32 : 12. AB = 6 × 32/12 = 16 cm. Answer: 16 cm",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12466,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"The hour hand moves for 4 hours and its length is 6 cm. Find the area (in cm 2 , rounded off to two decimal places) of the sector covered by the hour hand.",32.69,37.71,35.75,30.67,B,37.71,"The hour hand turns 30° per hour, so in 4 hours it sweeps 120°. Area = (120/360) × (22/7) × 6² = 12 × 22/7 = 37.71 cm². Answer: 37.71",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12467,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Average & Statistics,English,"Ram, Shyam, Rohan, Rita and Mukesh are five members of a family who are weighed one after another, and their average weight is calculated after each member is weighed. If the average weight increases by 2 kg each time, then how much heavier is Mukesh than Ram?",14 kg,18 kg,12 kg,16 kg,D,16 kg,"Let Ram weigh r. Each new person raises the average by 2 kg, so the k-th person weighs (new average) + (k − 1) × 2 more than the old average: Shyam = r + 4, Rohan = r + 8, Rita = r + 12, Mukesh = r + 16. Mukesh is 16 kg heavier than Ram. Answer: 16 kg",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12468,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,"If twice the numerical value of the curved surface area of a right circular cylinder is equal to the numerical value of its volume, then find the numerical value of the radius of the base of the cylinder.",5,4,3,2,B,4,2 × CSA = volume → 2 × 2πrh = πr²h. So 4 = r; the radius is 4. Answer: 4,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12469,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"Study the given graph and answer the following question. Number of lecturers recruited in three different states in five different years (in hundreds) Year A B C 2017 10 14 22 2018 23 52 48 2019 52 22 56 2020 15 58 35 2021 75 55 38 (Data from the official chart, shown as a table.) The number of lecturers recruited in state B in the year 2019 was what percentage of the number of lecturers recruited in state C in the year 2021? (correct to 2 decimal places)",56.25%,48.62%,50.25%,57.89%,D,57.89%,From the chart: B in 2019 = 22 hundred; C in 2021 = 38 hundred. 22/38 × 100 = 57.89%. Answer: 57.89%,Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12470,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Number System & Divisibility,English,"When m 12 − 1 is divided by m + 1, what will be the remainder?",2,1,−1,0,D,0,"By the remainder theorem, the remainder on dividing by m + 1 is the value at m = −1. (−1)¹² − 1 = 1 − 1 = 0. Answer: 0",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12471,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Geometry,English,"In ∆PQR, ∠Q = 90°, PQ = 8 cm and ∠PRQ = 45°. Find the length of QR.",3 cm,5 cm,6 cm,8 cm,D,8 cm,"∠Q = 90° and ∠R = 45°, so ∠P = 45° and the triangle is isosceles: QR = PQ. Equivalently, tan 45° = PQ/QR = 1, so QR = 8 cm. Answer: 8 cm",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12472,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"Roy’s monthly income is Rs.18,000. He took a loan of Rs.30,000 on simple interest at the rate of 5% per annum for 3 years. The amount that he will pay as simple interest in 3 years is what percentage of his monthly salary?",20%,25%,35%,30%,B,25%,"SI = 30000 × 5 × 3/100 = Rs.4,500. 4500/18000 × 100 = 25%. Answer: 25%",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12473,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"If sec²A + tan²A = 3, then what will be the value of cot A?",0,√3,1/√3,1,D,1,"sec²A = 1 + tan²A, so 1 + 2tan²A = 3 → tan²A = 1 → tan A = 1 (taking A acute). cot A = 1/tan A = 1. Answer: 1",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12474,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,"If K + 1/K + 2 = 0 and K < 0, then what is the value of K 11 + 1/K 4 ?",0,−17,−1,−2,A,0,"K + 1/K + 2 = 0 → K² + 2K + 1 = 0 → (K + 1)² = 0 → K = −1 (which is negative, as given). K¹¹ + 1/K⁴ = −1 + 1 = 0. Answer: 0",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12475,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"The number of units manufactured by company A was 12500 units in 2019 and 10625 units in 2020, whereas in company B, production fell from 34000 units in 2019 to 30600 units in 2020. If X and Y are the percentage decreases in the number of units manufactured by companies A and B respectively from 2019 to 2020, then what will be the ratio of X and Y?",5 : 3,8 : 5,3 : 2,3 : 4,C,3 : 2,X = (12500 − 10625)/12500 × 100 = 1875/12500 × 100 = 15%. Y = (34000 − 30600)/34000 × 100 = 10%. X : Y = 15 : 10 = 3 : 2. Answer: 3 : 2,Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
