SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12478,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,Select the correct direct form of the given sentence. Shravan said that the prisoner had slept throughout the journey.,"Shravan said, ""The prisoner sleeps throughout the journey.""","Shravan said, ""The prisoner had been sleeping throughout the journey.""","Shravan said, ""The prisoner had slept throughout the journey.""","Shravan says, ""The prisoner has slept throughout the journey.""",C,"Shravan said, ""The prisoner had slept throughout the journey.""","The reporting verb “said” becomes “said,” with inverted commas. The past perfect “had slept” in reported speech stays “had slept” when converted back (it cannot be changed to the present “sleeps” or a continuous form). Option 4 wrongly changes “said” to “says”. Answer: Shravan said, ""The prisoner had slept throughout the journey.""",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 1),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s1
