SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GA-EN-12524,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 4,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"If x = 2 − 2 1/3 + 2 2/3 , then what is the value of x³ − 6x² + 18x?",22,33,40,45,A,22,"Let a = 2 1/3 , so a³ = 2 and x − 2 = a² − a. Cube: (x − 2)³ = a⁶ − 3a⁵ + 3a⁴ − a³ = 4 − 6a² + 6a − 2 = 2 − 6(x − 2). So x³ − 6x² + 12x − 8 = 14 − 6x, i.e. x³ − 6x² + 18x = 22. Answer: 22",Easy,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 4),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s4
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GA-EN-12525,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 4,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"In ∆PQR, right-angled at Q, the length of PQ is 5 cm and ∠PRQ = 30°. Find the length of side QR.",3√3 cm,5√3 cm,5/√3 cm,1/√3 cm,B,5√3 cm,"Opposite ∠R (30°) is PQ = 5 cm and QR is the side adjacent to it, so tan 30° = PQ/QR. QR = 5 ÷ (1/√3) = 5√3 cm. Answer: 5√3 cm",Easy,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 4),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s4
