SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12533,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 4,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Syllogism & Statements,English,"In the question below, some statements are given, followed by some conclusions based on those statements. Take the given statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts. Read all the conclusions and then decide which of the conclusions logically follow from the given statements. Statements: I. All O are C. II. All C are D. Conclusions: I. Some C are O. II. Some D are C. III. No O is D.",Both conclusions I and III follow,All the conclusions follow,Both conclusions II and III follow,Both conclusions I and II follow,D,Both conclusions I and II follow,"All O are inside C and all C are inside D. Since every O is a C, some C are O: I follows. Since every C is a D, some D are C: II follows. Every O is in fact a D, so “No O is D” is false: III does not follow. Answer: Both conclusions I and II follow",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 4),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s4
