SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12536,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 4,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"If A × B means A is the father of B, A – B means A is the mother of B, and A + B means A is the brother of B, then which of the following expressions represents that Q is the son of P?",Q × P + R,P × Q + R,P + R × Q,P × Q − R,B,P × Q + R,"P × Q: P is the father of Q. Q + R: Q is the brother of R, so Q is male. Hence Q is the son of P. (In option 4, Q – R makes Q a mother, i.e. female.) Answer: P × Q + R",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 4),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s4
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12537,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 4,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Select the set in which the numbers are related in the same way as are the numbers of the following sets. (NOTE: Operations should be performed on the whole numbers, without breaking down the numbers into their constituent digits. For example, 13 – operations on 13 such as adding/subtracting/multiplying etc. can be performed. Breaking down 13 into 1 and 3 and then performing mathematical operations on 1 and 3 is not allowed.) (60, 17, 13) (62, 14, 17)","(56, 15, 13)","(55, 18, 9)","(43, 9, 12)","(57, 15, 14)",A,"(56, 15, 13)","Rule: first number = 2 × (second + third). 2 × (17 + 13) = 60 and 2 × (14 + 17) = 62. (56, 15, 13): 2 × (15 + 13) = 56. ✔ The others fail: 2 × 27 = 54 ≠ 55, 2 × 21 = 42 ≠ 43, 2 × 29 = 58 ≠ 57. Answer: (56, 15, 13)",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 4),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s4
