SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12544,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 4,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Syllogism & Statements,English,"Three statements are given, followed by three conclusions numbered I, II and III. Assuming the statements to be true, even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts, decide which of the conclusions logically follow(s) from the statements. Statements: Some chips are cakes. All cakes are ice creams. All ice creams are sweets. Conclusions: (I) Some sweets are cakes. (II) Some ice creams are cakes. (III) All cakes are sweets.",Either conclusion I or conclusion III follows,"Conclusions I, II and III all follow",Only conclusion I follows,Only conclusion II follows,B,"Conclusions I, II and III all follow","All cakes are ice creams and all ice creams are sweets, so all cakes are sweets: III follows. Hence some sweets are cakes (I) and some ice creams are cakes (II) also follow. All three conclusions follow. Answer: Conclusions I, II and III all follow",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 4),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s4
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12545,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 4,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,Three of the following four letter-clusters are alike in a certain way and thus form a group. Which letter-cluster does not belong to that group?,MEKF,WPUQ,BXCY,ZLXM,C,BXCY,"In MEKF, WPUQ and ZLXM: 1st letter − 2 = 3rd letter and 2nd letter + 1 = 4th letter (M→K, E→F; W→U, P→Q; Z→X, L→M). In BXCY the 1st letter goes +1 (B→C), so it is the odd one. Answer: BXCY",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 4),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s4
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12546,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 4,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,Select the option that is related to the fifth letter-cluster in the same way as the second letter-cluster is related to the first letter-cluster and the fourth letter-cluster is related to the third letter-cluster. LAMP : RQGT :: GAME : GQGO :: GOAT : ?,ACDF,EVUO,OUEV,VEUO,D,VEUO,"LAMP → RQGT: 1st output = 4th letter + 2 (P→R), 2nd = 2nd letter + 16 (A→Q), 3rd = 3rd letter − 6 (M→G), 4th = 1st letter + 8 (L→T). GAME → G, Q, G, O fits the same rule (E+2, A+16, M−6, G+8). GOAT → T+2 = V, O+16 = E, A−6 = U, G+8 = O → VEUO. Answer: VEUO",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 4),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s4
SSC-CGL-2022-T1-GI-EN-12547,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 4,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Select the set in which the numbers are related in the same way as are the numbers of the following sets. (NOTE: Operations should be performed on the whole numbers, without breaking down the numbers into their constituent digits. For example, 13 – operations on 13 such as adding/subtracting/multiplying etc. can be performed. Breaking down 13 into 1 and 3 and then performing mathematical operations on 1 and 3 is not allowed.) (4, 6, 9) (25, 10, 4)","(23, 3, 32)","(45, 20, 19)","(6, 36, 216)","(98, 7, 89)",C,"(6, 36, 216)","Rule: first × third = (second)². 4 × 9 = 36 = 6² and 25 × 4 = 100 = 10². (6, 36, 216): 6 × 216 = 1296 = 36². ✔ Answer: (6, 36, 216)",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 4),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s4
