SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12553,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 4,Quantitative Aptitude,Simple & Compound Interest,English,"If the nine-digit number 3422213AB is divisible by 99, then what is the value of 2A + B?",10,12,11,13,C,11,"99 = 9 × 11. Divisibility by 9: 3 + 4 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 1 + 3 + A + B = 17 + A + B, so A + B = 1 or 10. For 99, add two-digit groups from the right: AB + 13 + 22 + 42 + 3 = AB + 80 must be a multiple of 99, so AB = 19 (A = 1, B = 9). 2A + B = 2 + 9 = 11. Answer: 11",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 4),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s4
