SSC-CGL-2022-T1-QA-EN-12559,SSC CGL,2022,Tier 1,2022-12-13,Shift 4,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"Two stations R and S are 400 km apart. A train leaves R for S and at the same time another train leaves S for R. The two trains meet after 10 hours. If the speed of the first train is 4 km/h more than that of the second train, then what is the speed of the slower train?",16 km/h,22 km/h,18 km/h,26 km/h,C,18 km/h,"The trains approach each other, so their speeds add: 400 km ÷ 10 h = 40 km/h. Speeds x + 4 and x with 2x + 4 = 40 → x = 18 km/h (slower train). Answer: 18 km/h",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2022 Tier 1 (2022-12-13 Shift 4),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2022-12-13-s4
