SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14413,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,Which of the following awards was won by Lata Mangeshkar in the year 2001?,Dadasaheb Phalke Award,Padma Vibhushan,Bharat Ratna,Filmfare Lifetime Achievement Award,C,Bharat Ratna,"Option (3) is correct. Lata Mangeshkar won Bharat Ratna in 2001. Lata Mangeshkar was an Indian playback singer who was considered one of the greatest singers ever. She is also called ‘Nightingale of India’, ‘Voice of the Millennium’, and ‘Queen of Melody.’ Bharat Ratna is the highest civilian award given by the Government of India. It was given for the first time in 1954 to C. Rajagopalachari, Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan, and C. V. Raman.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1 (Morning)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14414,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"Details about Sudarshana lake is given in a rock inscription at Girnar (Junagarh), which was composed to record the achievements of the Shaka ruler.",Chashtana,Rudradaman I,Rudrasimha III,Maues,B,Rudradaman I,"Option (2) is correct. The details about Sudarshana Lake are given on a rock inscription at Girnar (Junagarh) to record the achievements of Rudradaman I. Sudarshan Lake is located in mid-Girnar Hill in Saurashtra, Gujarat, and it was built as an artificial reservoir to prevent flooding. The lake was constructed on the order of Chandragupta Maurya. The rock inscription is also known as the Girnar Rock inscription of Rudradaman.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1 (Morning)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14415,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,History,English,_____is an industry association and self-regulatory organisation (SRO) whose primary objective is to work towards the robust development of the microfinance sector.,NABARD,Self-help Group Association,Microfinance and Investments Regulatory Authority,Microfinance Institutions Network 31. Which article has a similar provision to that of Article 32 and deals with writ jurisdiction? 1. Article 228 2. Article 227 3. Article 226 4. Article 225 SOLVED PAPER (9th September 2024 Shift-1) 31,D,Microfinance Institutions Network 31. Which article has a similar provision to that of Article 32 and deals with writ jurisdiction? 1. Article 228 2. Article 227 3. Article 226 4. Article 225 SOLVED PAPER (9th September 2024 Shift-1) 31,"Option (4) is correct. The Microfinance Institutions Network (MFIN) is an industry association and self-regulatory organisation (SRO) whose primary objective is to work towards the robust development of the microfinance sector. It was established in 2009 as an industry association for Non-Bank Finance Company Micro Finance Institutions (NBFC-MFIs). In 2014, RBI was recognised it as India’s first SRO for NBFC-MFIs. As of October 2024, Dr. Alok Mishra is the CEO and Director of MFIN.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14416,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,Indian Polity & Constitution,English,Which of the following is NOT a condition for the President’s office in India?,He shall not hold any office of profit,The allowances shall not be diminished during his term of office.,"He shall not be entitled, without payment of rent, to use his official residence.",He shall not be a member of either House of the Parliament.,C,"He shall not be entitled, without payment of rent, to use his official residence.","Option (3) is correct. The conditions for the President of India are covered under Part IV, Article 59 of the Indian Constitution. They are as follows: • The President cannot be a member of either House of Parliament or of a House of the Legislature of any State. In case the person is a member, the person needs to vacate their seat in that House on the date on which he enters his office as President. • The President shall not hold any other office of profit. • The President is entitled to use their official residences without payment of rent • The emoluments and allowances of the President shall not be diminished during his term of office.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1 (Morning)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14417,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Which of the following statements best defines the monoecious?,A flower with gynoecium only,A flower with androecium only,A flower with both androecium and gynoecium,"A flower with dithecous 34. Mohan Veena player, Pandit Vishwa Mohan Bhatt won the____________ Award in the year 1994. 1. Grammy 2. Sangita Kalanidhi 3. Oscar 4. Sangeet Natak Akademi",C,A flower with both androecium and gynoecium,"Option (3) is correct. ‘Monoecious’ plants are the ones that have both male (androecium) and female (gynoecium) reproductive organs in the same plant. Some of the examples are Magnolias, Squash, coconuts etc. ‘Dioecious plants’ have male and female reproductive parts of different plants. e.g., red, cedars and ginkgos.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14418,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,Who is the Union Minister of State (Independent Charge) for Science and Technology as of July 2023?,Dharmendra Pradhan,Jitendra Singh,Ashwini Vaishnaw,Ramesh Pokhriyal,B,Jitendra Singh,"Option (2) is correct. As of June 2023, the Union Minister of State (Independent Charge) for Science and Technology was Dr. Jitendra Singh.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14419,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,Chemistry,English,Which of the following decomposition reactions is NOT a redox reaction?,Decomposition of sodium hydride,Decomposition of calcium carbonate,Decomposition of potassium chlorate,Decomposition of dihydrogen monoxide 37. Who among the following has authored the play ‘Nil Darpan’? 1. Chittaranjan Das 2. Motilal Nehru 3. Dinabandhu Mitra 4. Sarojini Naidu,B,Decomposition of calcium carbonate,"Option (2) is correct. A redox reaction is a chemical reaction in which the transfer of electrons takes place between the reactants. In these reactions, Oxidation (loss of electrons) and reduction (gain of electrons) take place at the same time. The decomposition of calcium carbonate is a decomposition reaction in which the compound breaks down into two or more components. In case of the calcium carbonate, it breaks down into Calcium Oxide and Carbon dioxide.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14420,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Who among the following formed the Bihar Provincial Kisan Sabha in 1929?,Jayprakash Narayan,JM Sengupta,Kunwar Singh,Swami Sahajanand Saraswati 39. Which plateau is very fertile because they are rich in black soil that is very good for farming? 1. Deccan lava plateau 2. African plateau 3. Ethiopian plateau 4. Katanga plateau,D,Swami Sahajanand Saraswati 39. Which plateau is very fertile because they are rich in black soil that is very good for farming? 1. Deccan lava plateau 2. African plateau 3. Ethiopian plateau 4. Katanga plateau,"Option (4) is correct. The Bihar Provincial Kisan Sabha (BPKS) was formed in 1929 by Swami Sahajanand Saraswati to address the grievances of peasants against the zamindars. Its first meeting was conceived at Sonepur Mela in Saran district, Bihar.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14421,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Which of the following is a correct order of basicity?,LiOH>NaOH>KOH>CsOH,KOH>CsOH>NaOH>LiOH,LiOH>KOH>CsOH>NaOH,CsOH>KOH>NaOH>LiOH,D,CsOH>KOH>NaOH>LiOH,"Option (4) is correct. Basicity is the measure of a base’s ability to accept hydrogen ions, or protons, in water to form a stable product. The correct order is CsOH> KOH>NaOH>LiOH.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1 (Morning)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14422,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,Biology,English,Which of the following pairs is INCORRECT regarding the grade of organisation and its example?,Cell-tissue grade organisation - Jellyfish,Cellular grade organisation - Sycon,Protoplasmic grade organisation - Paramecium,Tissue-organ grade organisation - Euplectella 42. The head office of Board of Control for Cricket in India (BCCI) is located in ............. . 1. Kolkata 2. Chennai 3. Mumbai 4. New Delhi,D,Tissue-organ grade organisation - Euplectella 42. The head office of Board of Control for Cricket in India (BCCI) is located in ............. . 1. Kolkata 2. Chennai 3. Mumbai 4. New Delhi,"Option (4) is correct. The grade of organisation means how cells are arranged in an organism’s body. An organism can have different grades of organisation- cellular, tissue, organ and the organ system. Euplectella has a cellular-level organisation. They are also known as glass sponges as they lack tissues.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14423,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"When the analysis of population density is done by calculating it through net cultivated area, then the measure is termed as:",Net density,Gross density,Agricultural density,Physiological density 44. Mahendravarman I was the ruler of which of the following dynasties? 1. Pallava 2. Pandya 3. Chalukya 4. Chola,D,Physiological density 44. Mahendravarman I was the ruler of which of the following dynasties? 1. Pallava 2. Pandya 3. Chalukya 4. Chola,"Option (4) is correct. When the analysis of population density is done by calculating it through net cultivated area, then the measure is termed Physiological density. It measures how many people live per unit of arable land in a region. Arable land is suitable for growing crops and raising animals for food. Agriculture density is the number of farmers per unit of arable land.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-14424,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,What challenge does foreign investment often face in India?,Excessive foreign competition,Lack of skilled labour,Lack of consumer base,Inconsistent regulatory environment 46. Which of the following states is the biggest producer of Pulses? 1. Bihar 2. Madhya Pradesh 3. Punjab 4. Haryana 47. Who founded the Prarthana Samaj in Mumbai in 1867? 1. Gopal Krishna Gokhale 2. Shri Ram Bajpai 3. Atmaram Pandurang 4. Raja Ram Mohan Roy 48. Who is the Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu as of July 2023? 1. KN Nehru 2. Pinarayi Vijayan 3. M Yediyurappa 4. MK Stalin 49. In which city was the first golf club of India situated? 1. Kolkata 2. Mysore 3. Shimla 4. Gulmarg,D,Inconsistent regulatory environment 46. Which of the following states is the biggest producer of Pulses? 1. Bihar 2. Madhya Pradesh 3. Punjab 4. Haryana 47. Who founded the Prarthana Samaj in Mumbai in 1867? 1. Gopal Krishna Gokhale 2. Shri Ram Bajpai 3. Atmaram Pandurang 4. Raja Ram Mohan Roy 48. Who is the Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu as of July 2023? 1. KN Nehru 2. Pinarayi Vijayan 3. M Yediyurappa 4. MK Stalin 49. In which city was the first golf club of India situated? 1. Kolkata 2. Mysore 3. Shimla 4. Gulmarg,"Option (4) is correct. Due to an inconsistent regulatory environment, it becomes challenging for foreign investors.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
