SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-14465,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Non-Verbal & Spatial Reasoning,English,"Six numbers 21, 22, 23, 24, 25 and 26 are written on different faces of a dice. Three positions of this dice are shown in the figure. Find the number on the face opposite to 24. 21 23 25 21 25 22 25 24 22",26,25,22,21 19. How many triangles are there in the given figure? 1. 21 2. 20 3. 18 4. 19,D,21 19. How many triangles are there in the given figure? 1. 21 2. 20 3. 18 4. 19,"Option (4) is the correct. The numbers an opposite faces are. (26, 25); (21, 24) and (23, 22)",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-14466,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Coding & Decoding,English,"In a certain code language, ‘what where how’ is written as ‘aa dd ff ’; ‘where there that’ is written as ‘dd zz pp’ and ‘which what here’ is written as ‘ff kk ll’. How is ‘how’ written in that language?",aa,kk,zz,ff,A,aa,"Option (1) is the correct. Hence, What where how → aa dd ff ...(i) Where there that → dd zz pp ...(ii) Which what here → ff kk ll ...(iii) From (i) and (iii) what → ff ...(iv) From (i) and (ii) where → dd ...(v) So, from (i), (iv) and (v) how → aa",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1 (Morning)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-14467,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Syllogism & Statements,English,"Three statements are given followed by three conclusions numbered I, II and III. Assuming the statements to be true, even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts, decide which of the conclusions logically follow(s) from the statements. Statements: Some tears are drops. Some drops are streams. All streams are rivers. Conclusions: I. All tears can never be rivers. II. Some drops are rivers. III. All tears being streams is a possibility.",Only conclusion I follows,Both II and III conclusion follow,Only conclusion III follows,"Both I and II conclusion follow 22. Which of the following terms will replace the question mark (?) in the given series? YZUW, ?, QTQU, MQOT, INMS 1. UWSV 2. UWVS 3. USWV 4. WUSV",B,Both II and III conclusion follow,"Option (2) is the correct. Tears Dropes Stream Rivers or Dropes Stream Rivers Tears So, both conclusions II and III follows",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-14468,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"In a certain code language, ‘A + B’ means ‘A is the mother of B’, ‘A – B’ means ‘A is the father of B’, ‘A $ B’ means ‘A is the son of B’, ‘A % B’ means ‘A is the sister of B’, ‘A / B’ means ‘A is the wife of B’ and ‘A = B’ means ‘A is the brother of B’. Which of the following means A is the daughter of K? i. A + K / J – P = D ii. J % P = K + A = D iii. K + A / P – D % J iv. D + K = A / P – J",i,iii,ii,iv,D,iv,"Option (4) is the correct. (i) A K J P D So, A is the mother of K. (ii) J P K A D So, A is the son of K. (iii) K A P D J So, A is the son of K. (iv) D K A P J So, A is the daughter of K.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1 (Morning)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-14469,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"19 is related to 209 following a certain logic. Following the same logic, 27 is related to 297. To which of the following is 61 related, following the same logic? (NOTE: Operations should be performed on the whole numbers, without breaking down the numbers into its constituent digits. e.g., 13 – Operations on 13 such as adding /deleting /multiplying etc. to 13 can be performed. Breaking down 13 into 1 and 3 and then performing mathematical operations on 1 and 3 is not allowed)",653,600,571,"671 25. Which of the following numbers will replace the question mark (?) in the given series? 1, 3, 10, 41, ?, 1237 1. 202 2. 210 3. 200 4. 206 General Awareness 26. In which year was Project Tiger launched in India? 1. 1973 2. 1970 3. 1972 4. 1985 27. Lathmar Holi is primarily celebrated in the state of: 1. Karnataka 2. Himachal Pradesh 3. Arunachal Pradesh 4. Uttar Pradesh",D,"671 25. Which of the following numbers will replace the question mark (?) in the given series? 1, 3, 10, 41, ?, 1237 1. 202 2. 210 3. 200 4. 206 General Awareness 26. In which year was Project Tiger launched in India? 1. 1973 2. 1970 3. 1972 4. 1985 27. Lathmar Holi is primarily celebrated in the state of: 1. Karnataka 2. Himachal Pradesh 3. Arunachal Pradesh 4. Uttar Pradesh","Option (4) is the correct. As, 19 × 11 = 209 and 27 × 11 = 297 So, 61 × 11 = 671",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
