SSC-CGL-2024-T1-QA-EN-14493,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"The given table shows the percentage of marks obtained by three students in three different subjects in an institute. (maximum marks are given in brackets) Subject→ Student¯ History (175) Geography (200) Botany (125) Ram 54 87 71 Mohan 51 79 78 Shyam 75 49 76 If in order to pass the exam, the minimum of 105 marks are neededs in History, how many students pass in the exam?",2,3,1,0,C,1,"Option (3) is correct. Required percentage to pass in history = 105 175 100 × = 60% So, only 1 student passed in history.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-QA-EN-14494,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Simple & Compound Interest,English,"Fill pipe P is 21 times faster than fill pipe Q. If Q can fill a cistern in 110 minutes, find the time it takes to fill the cistern when both fill pipes are opened together.",3 minutes,5 minutes,4 minutes,6 minutes,B,5 minutes,"Option (2) is correct. Since, pipe Q fill in 110 min. So, part of cistern filled per minute by pipe Q = 1 110 So, part of cistern filled per minute by pipe P = 21 110 \ Part of cistern filled by pipe P and Q together = 21 110 1 110 + = 22 110 = 1 5 \ Required time = 5 minutes",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1 (Morning)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-QA-EN-14495,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,The following tables shows the marks (out of 100) obtained by five students in five different subjects. Student ¯ Subject → Maths Physics Chemistry English Physical Education Tarun 65 80 75 85 90 Rohit 69 76 80 88 94 Mohit 76 84 77 90 95 Shobhit 76 85 76 86 78 Sumit 90 88 78 82 68 Who obtained 79 % marks in all the subject taken together?,Rohit,Tarun,Mohit,Sumit,B,Tarun,"Option (2) is correct. Total marks obtained by Tarun = 65 + 80 + 75 + 85 + 90 = 395 So, required percentage = 395 500 100 × = 79%",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-QA-EN-14496,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,"R pays ` 100 to P with ` 5, ` 2 and ` 1 coins. The total number of coins used for paying are 40. What is the number of coins of denomination ` 5 in the payment?",13,17,16,18,A,13,"Option (1) is correct. Let the number of coins of ` 5, ` 2 and ` 1 be x, y and z respectively So, 5x + 2y + z = 100 ...(i) and x + y + z = 40 ...(ii) On subtracting, we get 4x + y = 60 ⇒ y = 60 – 4x Now, from (ii), z = 40 – y – x = 40 – (60 – 4x) – x = 3x – 20 As, 60 – 4x ³ 0 ⇒ x £ 15 and 3x – 20 ³ 7, 0 ⇒ x ³ 20 3 So, from the options x could be 13.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1 (Morning)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
