SSC-CGL-2024-T1-QA-EN-14502,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-09,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"The average marks (out of 100) of boys and girls in an examination are 75 and 80, respectively. If the average marks of all the students in that examination are 78. Find the ratio of the number of boys to the number of girls.",1 : 3,2 : 3,1 : 2,3 : 4,B,2 : 3,"Option (2) is correct. Let the number of boys and girls be b and g respectively. \ Sum of marks of boys = 75 b and sum of marks of girls = 80 g Now, 75 80 b g b g + + = 78 ⇒ 75 b + 80 g = 78 b + 78 g ⇒ 3 b = 2 g ⇒ b g = 2 3 SOLVED PAPER (9th September 2024 Shift-1) 39",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-09 Shift 1 (Morning)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/9%20Sep%202024%20S1.pdf
