SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-15660,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-11,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Classification (Odd One Out),English,"Three of the following numbers are alike in a certain way and one is different. Pick the odd one out. (NOTE : Operations should be performed on the whole numbers, without breaking down the numbers into its constituent digits. E.g. 13 – Operations on 13 such as adding /deleting /multiplying etc., to 13 can be performed. Breaking down 13 into 1 and 3 and then performing mathematical operations on 1 and 3 is not allowed.)",75 – 120,90 – 144,65 – 104,45 – 70,D,45 – 70,"In 75–120, 90–144 and 65–104 the second number is 1.6 times the first (75×1.6=120, 90×1.6=144, 65×1.6=104). 45×1.6 = 72, not 70, so 45–70 is the odd one. Answer: 45 – 70",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-11 Shift 2) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-11 Shift 2 (Afternoon)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-11-s2
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-15661,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-11,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Select the set in which the numbers are related in the same way as are the numbers of the following set. (34, 15, 64) (29, 17, 63) (NOTE: Operations should be performed on the whole numbers, without breaking down the numbers into its constituent digits. E.g. 13 – Operations on 13 such as adding/deleting/multiplying etc. to 13 can be performed. Breaking down 13 into 1 and 3 and then performing mathematical operations on 1 and 3 is not allowed.)","(24, 28, 76)","(31, 23, 54)","(25, 14, 53)","(44, 32, 98)",C,"(25, 14, 53)","Rule: first number + 2 × second number = third number. 34 + 2×15 = 64; 29 + 2×17 = 63. Check: 25 + 2×14 = 53. The others fail (24+56=80, 31+46=77, 44+64=108). Answer: (25, 14, 53)",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-11 Shift 2) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-11 Shift 2 (Afternoon)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-11-s2
