SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-15664,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-11,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Syllogism & Statements,English,"Three statements are followed by three conclusions numbered I, II and III. You have to consider these statements to be true, even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts. Decide which of the given conclusions logically follow/s from the given statements. Statements: All pens are pages. Some pages are pins. Some pins are boards. Conclusions: (I) Some pins are pens. (II) Some boards are pages. (III) Some pens are boards.",Either conclusion I or conclusion III follows.,Only conclusion I follows.,Only conclusion II follows.,None of the conclusions follow.,D,None of the conclusions follow.,"All pens are pages, but the pages that are pins need not be pens, so I does not follow. The boards linked to some pins need not be pages or pens, so II and III do not follow either. I and III do not form a complementary pair, so ""either I or III"" is also invalid. Answer: None of the conclusions follow.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-11 Shift 2) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-11 Shift 2 (Afternoon)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-11-s2
