SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-18867,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-24,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood relations / coded relations,English,"Symbols are defined as follows: A + B means A is B's mother; A − B means A is B's brother; A × B means A is B's wife; A ÷ B means A is B's father. Given M + Q − R + K − Y, how is M related to Y?",Mother,Father's mother,Mother's mother,Brother's wife,C,Mother's mother,"M is Q's mother. Q is R's brother, so M is also R's mother. R is K's mother, and K is Y's brother; therefore R is Y's mother. M is R's mother, making M Y's maternal grandmother.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Cross-Checked PYQ Archive),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-24 Shift 2),https://wikistudy.in/exams/ssc-cgl/pyq-paper-2024-pdf/24-sep-12-30-pm
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-18868,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-24,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Mathematical operations / sign interchange,English,Which two signs must be swapped to make 29 × 145 + 5 − 640 ÷ 15 = 216 correct?,− and ×,÷ and +,− and +,÷ and ×,B,÷ and +,"After swapping ÷ and +, the expression becomes 29 × 145 ÷ 5 − 640 + 15. Since 145 ÷ 5 = 29, this is 29 × 29 − 640 + 15 = 841 − 640 + 15 = 216.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Cross-Checked PYQ Archive),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-24 Shift 2),https://wikistudy.in/exams/ssc-cgl/pyq-paper-2024-pdf/24-sep-12-30-pm
