SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19722,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,"At the 36th National Games, Hashika Ramchandra won six gold medals in which of the following sports?",Swimming,Boxing,Wrestling,Badminton 27. Which state in India was the most transformed by the Green Revolution? 1. Kerala 2. Maharashtra 3. Punjab 4. West Bengal,A,Swimming,"Option (1) is correct. Hashika Ramchandra won six gold medals in swimming at the 36th National Games. She won a total of seven medals, of which one was bronze. She was also crowned the best female athlete at the National Games. She is the first athlete from Karnataka to win this title.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19723,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Which of the following ports was developed as a Satellite port to relieve the pressure at the Mumbai port?,Marmagao Port,New Mangalore Port,Deendayal Port Authority,Jawaharlal Nehru Port SOLVED PAPER (26th September 2024 Shift-2) 19 29. Who among the following was the shortest-serving Prime Minister of India? 1. Atal Bihari Vajpayee 2. Gulzarilal Nanda 3. Chandra Shekhar 4. Charan Singh,D,Jawaharlal Nehru Port SOLVED PAPER (26th September 2024 Shift-2) 19 29. Who among the following was the shortest-serving Prime Minister of India? 1. Atal Bihari Vajpayee 2. Gulzarilal Nanda 3. Chandra Shekhar 4. Charan Singh,"Option (4) is correct. Jawaharlal Nehru Port, located in Navi Mumbai, was established in 1989 to handle container traffic and ease congestion at the Mumbai port. It has since become one of the largest container ports in India, designed to accommodate the growing trade and shipping needs of the region, thereby supporting economic development while reducing the burden on the older Mumbai port.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19724,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"In the context of Mathura school of Art, during which of the following periods were a number of sculptures of Brahmanical deities, such as Kartikeya, Vishnu and Kubera carved?",Satavahana,Shaka,Parthian,Kushana,D,Kushana,"Option (4) is correct. In the context of the Mathura school of Art, a number of sculptures of Brahmanical deities, such as Kartikeya, Vishnu, and Kubera, were carved during the Kushana period.The Kushana period (approximately 1 st to 3rd centuries CE) is known for its flourishing art and culture, particularly in Mathura. During this time, the Mathura school of art produced numerous sculptures depicting various Brahmanical deities, reflecting the religious and cultural dynamics of the era. The Kushanas played a significant role in promoting and patronizing the arts, leading to the development of distinctive styles in sculpture that emphasized naturalism and intricate detailing.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2 (Afternoon)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19725,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,Indian Economy,English,In which of the following situations does the government run a deficit budget?,When the government expenditure and revenue both are zero.,When the government revenue exceeds expenditure.,When the government expenditure equals revenue.,When the government expenditure exceeds revenue. 32. Tsang Po and Jamuna are other names of which river? 1. Narmada 2. Indus 3. Ganga 4. Brahmaputra,D,When the government expenditure exceeds revenue. 32. Tsang Po and Jamuna are other names of which river? 1. Narmada 2. Indus 3. Ganga 4. Brahmaputra,"Option (4) is correct. A deficit budget arises when the government expenditures surpass its revenues, such as those from taxes and fees. This situation typically necessitates borrowing to make up the difference, signifying that the government is financing its activities through debt.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19726,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,Physics,English,"Which of the following groups/parties was started in San Francisco, United States of America during the Indian National Movement?",Khilafat Committee,Ghadar Party,Swaraj Party,Hindustan Socialist Republican Association,B,Ghadar Party,"Option (2) is correct. The Ghadar Party was established in 1913 by Indian expatriates in the United States, specifically in San Francisco. Its main objective was to achieve India’s independence from British rule through revolutionary action. The party focused on mobilising Indians living abroad and supporting an armed struggle against colonial oppression in India. It became an important player in the nationalist movement, particularly among the Indian diaspora in North America.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2 (Afternoon)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19727,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,Biology,English,"Which of the following organisations is NOT a winner of the $100,000 cash prize as ‘Best Small Business: Good Food for All’, announced by the United Nations for providing inspiring, diverse and impactful solutions in improving access to healthy and sustainable food?",Edible Routes Private Limited,Oorja Development Solutions India Private Limited,Taru Naturals,Patanjali 35. ‘Castling’ is related to which of the following sports? 1. Chess 2. Billiards 3. Tennis 4. Table tennis,D,Patanjali 35. ‘Castling’ is related to which of the following sports? 1. Chess 2. Billiards 3. Tennis 4. Table tennis,"Option (4) is correct. The award recognises small businesses that contribute to improving access to healthy and sustainable food. While Edible Routes, Oorja Development Solutions and Taru Naturals have been acknowledged for their impactful solutions in this area, Patanjali, although a well-known brand, has not been listed among the winners of this specific prize.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19728,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,What is the cost of the ‘Nand Baba Milk Mission’ scheme launched by the Uttar Pradesh state government in 2023 to provide milk producers the facility of selling their milk at a reasonable price in villages through dairy co- operative societies?,"` 2,000 crore","` 1,500 crore",` 500 crore,"` 1,000 crore",D,"` 1,000 crore","Option (4) is correct. The Nand Baba Milk Mission is designed to assist milk producers by enabling them to sell milk at fair prices through dairy co-operative societies in rural areas. The ` 1,000 crore allocation aims to strengthen the dairy sector, improve the livelihoods of milk producers and encourage milk consumption within the state.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2 (Afternoon)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19729,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"In the context of vernier calliper, an internal jaw is used to measure:",the depth of a beaker,the length correct up to 1 mm,the length of a rod and diameter of a sphere,the internal diameter of a hollow cylinder and pipes,D,the internal diameter of a hollow cylinder and pipes,"Option (4) is correct. The internal jaws of a vernier caliper are specifically designed to measure the dimensions of objects from the inside. This allows for accurate measurement of the internal diameter of hollow objects, such as cylinders and pipes. The external jaws, on the other hand, are used for measuring external dimensions like the length of rods.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2 (Afternoon)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19730,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,Biology,English,Match the terms in column A with their respective properties in column B. Column-A Column-B i. Glucose a. Intermediate substance in breakdown of glucose ii. Yeast b. Glucose is converted into pyruvic iii. Glycolysis c. Uses nutrients for fermentation process iv. Pyruvic acid d. Best organic substrate fro respiration,"i-d, ii-c, iii-b, iv-a","i-b, ii-d, iii-a, iv-c","i-a, ii-b, iii-c, iv-d","i-b, ii-a, iii-d, iv-c 39. If a bar magnet is hung from a string, in which direction does its north pole point? 1. North 2. South 3. East 4. West",A,"i-d, ii-c, iii-b, iv-a",Option (1) is correct. Glucose – Best organic substrate for respiration Yeast – Uses nutrients for fermentation process Glycolysis – Glucose is converted into pyruvic acid Pyruvic acid – Intermediate substance in breakdown of glucose,Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19731,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Match the points under Column A with those under Column B. Column-A Column-B i. Hexapoda a. Daphnia ii. Crustacea b. Mosquito iii. Myriapoda c. Limulus iv. Chelicerata d. Julus,"i-b, ii-a, iii-d, iv-c","i-d, ii-c, iii-b, iv-a","i-a, ii-b, iii-c, iv-d","i-b, ii-c, iii-a, iv-d 41. Fugdi dance is associated with which of the following states? 1. Uttar Pradesh 2. Goa 3. Kerala 4. Uttarakhand 42. The concept of ‘Independence of judiciary’ in the Indian Constitution is taken from the Constitution of: 1. France 2. Britain 3. Ireland 4. The USA",A,"i-b, ii-a, iii-d, iv-c",Option (1) is correct. Hexapoda–Mosquito Crustacea – Daphnia Myriapoda – Julus Chelicerata - Limulus,Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19732,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,Umayalpuram K Sivaraman is an eminent musician associated with which of the following musical instruments?,Dhol,Sitar,Mridangam,Guitar 44. Rottela Panduga or the Roti Festival is celebrated in which Indian state? 1. Maharashtra 2. Andhra Pradesh 3. Tamil Nadu 4. Karnataka 45. Belur Math was founded by which of the following social reformers in British India? 1. KT Telang 2. Swami Vivekanand 3. VN Mandlik 4. RG Bhandarkar 46. Which of the following parts of the mountain will receive the most rainfall from moisture-laden winds? 1. Leeward side 2. Relief side 3. Upward side 4. Windward side 47. Which singer from Assam was posthumously awarded the Bharat Ratna in 2019? 1. Rameshwar Pathak 2. Padmanav Bordoloi 3. Archana Mahanta 4. Bhupen Hazarika,C,Mridangam,"Option (3) is correct. Umayalpuram K. Sivaraman is a renowned Indian musician known for his mastery of the mridangam, a traditional percussion instrument used in Carnatic music. He has made significant contributions to the field, both as a performer and as a teacher.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19733,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,History,English,"Medini Rai of Chanderi, Hasan Khan of Mewat and Mahmud Lodi joined Rana Sanga with their forces to fight against which of the following Mughal rulers?",Aurangzeb,Humayun,Babur,Akbar,C,Babur,"Option (3) is correct. Medini Rai of Chanderi, Hasan Khan of Mewat, and Mahmud Lodi allied with Rana Sanga to oppose Babur, the founder of the Mughal Empire.This alliance was formed to resist Babur’s expansion into northern India, particularly after his victory at the First Battle of Panipat in 1526. Ultimately, they confronted Babur at the Battle of Khanwa in 1527, where Babur achieved victory.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2 (Afternoon)),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
