SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GA-EN-19735,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 2,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,"As per the UNDP, the rank of Sri Lanka in the Human Development Index (2022) is:",72 189,74 189,75 189,73 189 Quantitative Aptitude,D,73 189 Quantitative Aptitude,"Option (4) is correct. According to the 2022 Human Development Report by the UNDP, Sri Lanka ranks 73 rd out of 189 countries with a score of 0.782. This indicates that Sri Lanka has made significant strides in human development, but there is still room for improvement in areas such as health, education, and income levels. Quantitative Aptitude",Easy,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 2),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2024/26%20Sep%202024%20S2.pdf
