SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-19960,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Mathematical Operations,English,What will come in the place of the question mark (?) in the following equation if ‘+’ and ‘×‘ are interchanged and ‘−’ and ‘÷’ are interchanged? 95 − 19 × 4 + 6 ÷ 16 = ?,14,11,12,13,D,13,After the swaps the expression becomes 95 ÷ 19 + 4 × 6 − 16. = 5 + 24 − 16 = 13. Answer: 13,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3 (Evening)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-26-s3
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-19961,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"In the following number-pairs, the second number is obtained by applying certain mathematical operations to the first number. Select the set in which the numbers are related in the same way as are the numbers of the following sets. (NOTE : Operations should be performed on the whole numbers, without breaking down the numbers into its constituent digits. E.g. 13 – Operations on 13 such as adding /deleting /multiplying etc., to 13 can be performed. Breaking down 13 into 1 and 3 and then performing mathematical operations on 1 and 3 is not allowed.) (96, 29) (112, 33)","(204, 55)","(188, 52)","(176, 45)","(108, 30)",B,"(188, 52)","Rule: divide the first number by 4 and add 5 — 96 ÷ 4 + 5 = 29 and 112 ÷ 4 + 5 = 33. Only 188 fits: 188 ÷ 4 + 5 = 47 + 5 = 52. (204 gives 56, 176 gives 49, 108 gives 32.) Answer: (188, 52)",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3 (Evening)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-26-s3
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-19962,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"Select the number from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series. 672, 677, 686, 699, 716, ?",747,737,749,757,B,737,"Differences: +5, +9, +13, +17 — each grows by 4. Next difference is +21, so 716 + 21 = 737. Answer: 737",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3 (Evening)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-26-s3
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-19963,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"Four letter-clusters have been given, out of which three are alike in some manner and one is different. Select the letter-cluster that is different. Note: The odd one out is not based on the number of consonants/vowels or their position in the letter cluster.",YWA,LJO,JHL,OMQ,B,LJO,"Use letter positions. YWA: Y −2 → W, then W +4 → A (wrapping round). JHL and OMQ follow the same −2, +4 pattern. LJO is −2 then +5 (J → O), so it is the odd one. Answer: LJO",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3 (Evening)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-26-s3
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-19964,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Which of the following terms will replace the question mark (?) in the given series? FHVQ, IJSO, LLPM, ONMK, ?",ROJI,RPKJ,QPJI,RPJI,D,RPJI,"Track each position: 1st letter F, I, L, O → +3 → R; 2nd H, J, L, N → +2 → P. 3rd V, S, P, M → −3 → J; 4th Q, O, M, K → −2 → I. The term is RPJI. Answer: RPJI",Easy,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3 (Evening)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-26-s3
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-19965,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,Select the option that is related to the fifth letter cluster in the same way as the second letter cluster is related to the first letter cluster and the fourth letter cluster is related to the third letter cluster. IMPROVE : RPMIEVO :: HISTORY : TSIHYRO :: JOURNEY : ?,RUOJYEN,NEYJOUR,JOURYEN,YENRUOJ,A,RUOJYEN,IMPROVE is split as IMPR | OVE and each part is reversed: RPMI + EVO. HISTORY → HIST | ORY → TSIH + YRO. JOURNEY → JOUR | NEY → RUOJ + YEN = RUOJYEN. Answer: RUOJYEN,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3 (Evening)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-26-s3
