SSC-CGL-2024-T1-GI-EN-19973,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Classification (Odd One Out),English,"Three of the following number-pairs are alike in some manner and hence form a group. Which number-pair does not belong to that group? (NOTE: Operations should be performed on the whole numbers, without breaking down the numbers into its constituent digits. E.g. 13 – Operations on 13 such as adding/subtracting/multiplying etc. to 13 can be performed. Breaking down 13 into 1 and 3 and then performing mathematical operations on 1 and 3 is not allowed.)",6 – 64,9 – 121,12 – 225,8 – 100,C,12 – 225,"Pattern: second number = (first + 2)². 6 → 64, 9 → 121, 8 → 100. For 12 it should be 14² = 196, not 225, so 12 – 225 is the odd pair. Answer: 12 – 225",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3 (Evening)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-26-s3
