SSC-CGL-2024-T1-QA-EN-19998,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Algebra,English,Find the value of the unknowns: x + 1.5y + 2z = 5.5 x + 5y + 7z = 15 3x + 11y + 13z = 25,"x = -3,y = 2,z = 4","x = 4,y = -3,z = 2","x = 2,y = 4,z = -3","x = 2,y = -3,z = 4",D,"x = 2,y = -3,z = 4","Check x = 2, y = −3, z = 4: 2 − 4.5 + 8 = 5.5; 2 − 15 + 28 = 15; 6 − 33 + 52 = 25. All three equations hold; every other option fails the first equation. Answer: x = 2,y = -3,z = 4",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3 (Evening)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-26-s3
SSC-CGL-2024-T1-QA-EN-19999,SSC CGL,2024,Tier 1,2024-09-26,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"In a circular race of 1600 m in length, Bhaskar and Vinay start with speeds of 27 km/h and 45 km/h starting at the same time from the same point. When will they meet for the first time on the track when running in the opposite directions and the same direction, respectively?",2 minutes 20 seconds and 4 minutes 20 seconds,1 minute 20 seconds and 5 minutes 20 seconds,1 minute 40 seconds and 5 minutes 20 seconds,2 minutes 40 seconds and 5 minutes 40 seconds,B,1 minute 20 seconds and 5 minutes 20 seconds,Speeds: 27 km/h = 7.5 m/s and 45 km/h = 12.5 m/s. Opposite directions: 1600 ÷ 20 = 80 s = 1 min 20 s. Same direction: 1600 ÷ 5 = 320 s = 5 min 20 s. Answer: 1 minute 20 seconds and 5 minutes 20 seconds,Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3) | 2024 Tier 1 (2024-09-26 Shift 3 (Evening)),https://www.nextgenpsc.com/ssc/cgl/previous-year-papers/cgl-2024-09-26-s3
