SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20413,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Seating Arrangement & Direction,English,"A is facing North, B is seated second to the right of A. Who is sitting immediately to the left of B?",The person seated to the immediate right of A,The person seated to the opposite to A,The person seated to the immediate left of A,Cannot be determined,A,The person seated to the immediate right of A,"Option (1) is correct. The correct sitting arrangement is: A ______ B So, the person who is sitting to the right of A is seated to the left of B.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2025/12%20Sep%20S1%202025.pdf
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20414,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,"In each of the following questions, the first word is coded to form the second word using a specific rearrangement and/or substitution rule. Apply the same rule to the third word to determine the correct corresponding word from the given alternatives. AYRRJC : CATTLE :: NCPDCAR : ?",SUBJECTS,NEGLECT,PERFECT,"OPERATE 17. Identify the odd one: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 20 1. 17 2. 13 3. 20 4. 11 18. Which of the following is the odd one out? 1. 2, 3, 5 2. 11, 13, 17 3. 4, 6, 8 4. 17, 19, 23 19. Rani said, “The man in the photo is my mother's son-in- law.” Who is the man to Rani? 1. Husband 2. Father 3. Uncle 4. Cousin Time Allotted: 1 hour Max Marks: 200 STAFF SELECTION COMMISSION COMBINED GRADUATE LEVEL (TIER-I) SOLVED PAPER (12th September 2025: Shift-1)",C,PERFECT,"Option (3) is correct. From the first word to the second, all letters move forward 2 letters. Hence, the required word will be PERFECT.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2025/12%20Sep%20S1%202025.pdf
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20415,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"Pointing to a man, a woman said, “His mother is the only daughter of my father.” How is the man related to the woman?",Son,Nephew,Cousin,"Grandson 23. Pointing to a woman, John says, “She is the wife of my uncle's only son.” How is the woman related to John? 1. Sister 2. Cousin 3. Sister-in law 4. Niece",A,Son,"Option (1) is correct. The only daughter of the woman’s father is the woman herself. So, the man is the son of the woman.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2025/12%20Sep%20S1%202025.pdf
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20416,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"A man said, “My mother's husband's only son is the father of your sister's brother”. How is the man related to you?",Uncle,Father,Grandfather,"Brother 25. If # = ×, @ = –, $ = +, then evaluate: 9 # 2 @ 3 $ 1 1. 18 2. 14 3. 16 4. 17 General Awareness",B,Father,"Option (2) is correct. The man’s mother’s husband is his father. And the father of my sister’s brother is my father. So, my father is the son of the man’s father, i.e, the man is my father.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2025/12%20Sep%20S1%202025.pdf
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20417,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,"Arrange the fractions 5/9, 4/7, 3/5, and, 2/3 in ascending order.","3/5, 4/7, 2/3, 5/9","5/9, 4/7, 3/5, 2/3","2/3, 3/5, 4/7, 5/9","4/7, 5/9, 2/3, 3/5",B,"5/9, 4/7, 3/5, 2/3","Decimal values: 5/9 = 0.556, 4/7 = 0.571, 3/5 = 0.600, 2/3 = 0.667. Ascending order: 5/9, 4/7, 3/5, 2/3.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20418,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,Simplify: (2½ + 3.6) − 1.9,4.2,5.2,6.2,7.2,A,4.2,2½ = 2.5. (2.5 + 3.6) − 1.9 = 6.1 − 1.9 = 4.2.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20419,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,Evaluate: 7¼ − [5/6 ÷ {1/3 − (1/2 × (3/4 − 1/4))}],−3¼,3¼,−2¾,2¾,C,−2¾,Innermost: 3/4 − 1/4 = 1/2. Then 1/2 × 1/2 = 1/4. Next 1/3 − 1/4 = 1/12. Then 5/6 ÷ 1/12 = 10. Finally 7¼ − 10 = −2¾.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20420,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"From a sample of 200 software engineers, determine the ratio of those proficient in Python to those proficient in Java using the given information: Category | Number Proficient in Python and Java | 50 Proficient in Python only | 70 Proficient in Java only | 60 Proficient in neither language | 20",11:12,12:11,7:6,6:7,B,12:11,Python: 50 (both) + 70 (only Python) = 120. Java: 50 + 60 = 110. Ratio 120 : 110 = 12 : 11.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20421,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"Arvind started a business by investing ₹80,000. After 4 months, Bhavin joined with ₹1,20,000. At the end of 8 months from the start, Chandan joined with ₹1,60,000. If the total profit is ₹1,05,000 at the end of the year, find the share of Chandan.","₹26,500","₹26,000","₹26,200","₹26,250",D,"₹26,250","Capital × months: Arvind 80,000 × 12 = 9,60,000; Bhavin 1,20,000 × 8 = 9,60,000; Chandan 1,60,000 × 4 = 6,40,000. Ratio 3 : 3 : 2. Chandan’s share = 2/8 × 1,05,000 = ₹26,250.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20422,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A and B start a business. A invests ₹80,000 for 9 months, B invests ₹1,20,000 for 6 months. What is B’s share of a ₹45,000 profit?","₹26,500","₹28,000","₹36,000","₹22,500",D,"₹22,500","A: 80,000 × 9 = 7,20,000. B: 1,20,000 × 6 = 7,20,000. Ratio 1 : 1, so B gets half of ₹45,000 = ₹22,500.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20423,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Simple & Compound Interest,English,What is the average of all integers between 100 and 250 that are exactly divisible by 11?,176,186,196,146,A,176,"Multiples of 11 between 100 and 250 run from 110 to 242 (13 terms, an arithmetic progression). Average = (110 + 242)/2 = 176.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20424,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"The average of 15 numbers is 80. The average of the first 6 numbers is 72. The average of the next 6 numbers is 25% more than the average of the first 6 numbers. The 13th number is 8 more than the 15th number, and the 14th number is 10 less than the 15th number. What is the average of the 13th and 14th numbers?",70.89,85,75.67,80.65,C,75.67,"Total = 15 × 80 = 1200. First 6 = 6 × 72 = 432. Next 6 average = 72 × 1.25 = 90, sum 540. Last three sum = 1200 − 432 − 540 = 228. With the 15th number = x: (x + 8) + (x − 10) + x = 228, so x = 230/3. 13th + 14th = 2x − 2 = 454/3, average = 227/3 ≈ 75.67.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20425,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"A landlord bought a flat for ₹8,00,000. He wants to earn a 9% annual return on his investment after paying ₹2,000 per month for maintenance. What should be the monthly rent he charges?","₹7,000","₹7,500","₹8,000","₹8,500",C,"₹8,000","Required yearly return = 9% of 8,00,000 = ₹72,000. Add yearly maintenance 2,000 × 12 = ₹24,000. Rent per year = ₹96,000, so monthly rent = ₹8,000.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20426,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,An amount is said to double in 5 years with compound interest. How many years will it take for the amount to grow to 8 times its original value?,15,16,17,18,A,15,"It doubles every 5 years at compound interest. 8 times = 2 × 2 × 2, three doublings, so 3 × 5 = 15 years.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20427,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A sum becomes ₹6,600 in 2 years and ₹7,920 in 3 years at compound interest. What is the original principal?","₹4,000.33","₹5,583.33","₹4,583.33","₹6,583.33",C,"₹4,583.33","One year’s growth: 7920/6600 = 1.2, so the rate is 20%. Principal = 6600 ÷ 1.2² = 6600 ÷ 1.44 = ₹4,583.33.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20428,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,Suman purchased 25 liters of milk at ₹45 per liter and another 15 liters of milk at ₹50 per liter. She combined both quantities and then sold the entire mixture at ₹48 per liter. What was her total profit or loss?,Loss of ₹45,Profit of ₹45,Profit of ₹90,Loss of ₹90,B,Profit of ₹45,"Cost = 25 × 45 + 15 × 50 = 1125 + 750 = ₹1,875. Sale = 40 × 48 = ₹1,920. Profit = ₹45.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20429,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A toy manufacturer produced 1200 toy cars at a total cost of ₹90,000. He donated 200 cars to a charity event. For the rest, he announced a 10% discount on the market price of ₹120 per car. He also offered 2 toy cars free for every 8 toy cars purchased. If all 1200 toy cars were distributed, what is his overall gain or loss percentage?",4% loss,4% profit,5% loss,5% profit,A,4% loss,"After donating 200 cars, 1000 cars go out under the offer. With 2 free for every 8 bought, only 800 are paid for. Price per car = 120 × 0.9 = ₹108. Revenue = 800 × 108 = ₹86,400 against cost ₹90,000. Loss = 3,600, which is 4% of 90,000.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20430,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A retailer marks an air conditioner 80% above its cost price. He offers a first discount of 25% on the marked price. During a festive offer, an additional discount of 10% is applied on the already discounted price. If the final selling price is ₹15,552, what is the approximate cost price of the air conditioner?","₹9,000","₹9,200","₹12,800","₹10,000",C,"₹12,800","SP = CP × 1.8 × 0.75 × 0.9 = 1.215 × CP. CP = 15,552 ÷ 1.215 = ₹12,800.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20431,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Ratio & Proportion,English,A 40-liter mixture contains juice and water in the ratio 5:3. How much water (in liters) must be added to this mixture to change the ratio of juice to water to 2:3?,15.5 litres,22.5 litres,25 litres,30 litres,B,22.5 litres,"Juice = 5/8 × 40 = 25 L, water = 15 L. For juice : water = 2 : 3, water must be 25 × 3/2 = 37.5 L. Water to add = 37.5 − 15 = 22.5 litres.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20432,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A is able to complete a task in 15 days, while B takes 20 days to finish the same task. If they collaborate and work together for 4 days, what fraction of the work will still remain?",1/4,7/15,8/15,11/15,C,8/15,One day together: 1/15 + 1/20 = 7/60. In 4 days: 28/60 = 7/15. Work left = 1 − 7/15 = 8/15.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20433,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"Two oils priced at ₹90 per kg and ₹150 per kg are blended and sold at ₹144 per kg, achieving a profit margin of 20%. What is the ratio of the two oils in the mixture?",1 : 1,2 : 1,3 : 2,4 : 1,A,1 : 1,"Cost price of the mixture = 144 ÷ 1.2 = ₹120 per kg. By alligation, (150 − 120) : (120 − 90) = 30 : 30 = 1 : 1.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20434,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"Three pipes, A, B, and C are capable of filling a tank in 6, 8, and 12 hours, respectively. When all three pipes are opened together, they operate for 2 hours before pipe C is closed. How much additional time will it take to completely fill the tank after that?",6/7 hours,2/6 hours,3/5 hours,9/2 hours,A,6/7 hours,"All three together fill 1/6 + 1/8 + 1/12 = 9/24 = 3/8 per hour, so in 2 hours 3/4 is full. A and B then fill 1/6 + 1/8 = 7/24 per hour. Time for the remaining 1/4 = (1/4) ÷ (7/24) = 6/7 hour.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20435,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A bullet train covers a fixed distance in 30 minutes at an average speed of 240 km/h. Due to track maintenance, it needs to be diverted, increasing the distance by 20%. If the train needs to arrive at its destination on time (i.e., in 30 minutes), what should its new average speed be in km/h?",280 km/h,300 km/h,288 km/h,320 km/h,C,288 km/h,Distance = 240 × 1/2 = 120 km. New distance = 120 × 1.2 = 144 km. Speed needed for 30 minutes = 144 ÷ 0.5 = 288 km/h.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20436,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"Two cars, X and Y, start from points 360 km apart and travel at constant speeds. If they move towards each other, they meet in 4 hours. If they move in the same direction, they meet in 12 hours. What is the speed of car X? (Assume X is the faster car).",60 km/h,75 km/h,45 km/h,90 km/h,A,60 km/h,Towards each other: sum of speeds = 360/4 = 90 km/h. Same direction: difference = 360/12 = 30 km/h. Faster car X = (90 + 30)/2 = 60 km/h.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20437,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,"A circular pizza having a radius of 21 cm. If 75% of it is eaten, what is the area of pizza remaining?",173.25 cm²,346.36 cm²,432.25 cm²,115.5 cm²,B,346.36 cm²,"Remaining = 25% of πr² = 0.25 × π × 441. With π = 3.1416 this is about 346.36 cm², the marked option. (With π = 22/7 it is 346.5 cm², which is still closest to this option.)",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20438,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Geometry,English,A ring-shaped disc has outer radius 10 cm and inner radius 7 cm. What is the approximate ratio of the ring’s area to the whole outer circle?,1:2,2:3,3:4,4:5,A,1:2,"Ring area / outer circle = π(10² − 7²) / π(10²) = 51/100, which is about 1 : 2.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20439,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,A bicycle wheel having a radius of 35 cm. What percentage of its circumference is covered in a quarter turn? (Use π = 22/7),15%,25%,30%,35%,B,25%,"A full turn covers the whole circumference, so a quarter turn covers 1/4 of it, which is 25%. The radius is not needed.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20440,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,"The line y = mx + 5 passes through (1,8). Find m.",5,4,3,2,C,3,"Put (1, 8) into y = mx + 5: 8 = m + 5, so m = 3.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20441,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,31³ + 18³−37³ + 210 is equal to:,−36810,−14820,−45670,−23450,B,−14820,"31³ = 29,791, 18³ = 5,832, 37³ = 50,653. So 29,791 + 5,832 − 50,653 + 210 = −14,820.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20442,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,Evaluate: 7 1 4 5 6 1 3 1 2 3 4 1 4                           ,−3 1 4,3 1 4,−2 3 4,2 3 4,C,−2 3 4,Option (3) is correct. 7 1 4 5 6 1 3 1 2 3 4 1 4                            = 29 4 5 6 1 3 1 2 1 2                           = 29 4 5 6 1 3 1 4                    = 29 4 5 6 1 12               = 29 4 5 6 12 29 4 10          = = 29 40 4 11 4 2 3 4 − − − = =,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2025/12%20Sep%20S1%202025.pdf
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20443,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A and B start a business. A invests ` 80,000 for 9 months, B invests ` 1,20,000 for 6 months. What is B's share of a ` 45,000 profit?","` 26,500","` 28,000","` 36,000","` 22,500 57. What is the average of all integers between 100 and 250 that are exactly divisible by 11? 1. 176 2. 186 3. 196 4. 146",D,"` 22,500 57. What is the average of all integers between 100 and 250 that are exactly divisible by 11? 1. 176 2. 186 3. 196 4. 146","Option (4) is correct. Total profit = ` 45000 According to the question, the ratio of their shares is: 9 × ` 80000 : 6 × ` 120000 = ` 720000 : ` 720000 = 1 : 1 So, share of B = 1 1 1 + × 45000 = 1 2 × 45000 = ` 22500",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2025/12%20Sep%20S1%202025.pdf
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20444,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,Suman purchased 25 litres of milk at ` 45 per litres and another 15 litres of milk at ` 50 per litres. She combined both quantities and then sold the entire mixture at ` 48 per litres. What was her total profit or loss?,Loss of ` 45,Profit of ` 45,Profit of ` 90,Loss of ` 90,B,Profit of ` 45,Option (2) is correct. Given: 25 litres of milk at ` 45/litre; 15 litres of milk at ` 50/litre Total = 25 + 15 = 40 litres Selling price = ` 48/litre Cost price of 25 litres at ` 45/litre = 25 × 45 = ` 1125 Cost price of 15 litres at ` 50/litre = 15 × 50 = ` 750 Total cost price = ` (1125 + 750) = ` 1875 Total selling price = ` 40 × 48 = ` 1920 Profit = SP – CP = ` 1920 – ` 1875 = ` 45,Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2025/12%20Sep%20S1%202025.pdf
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20445,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Ratio & Proportion,English,A 40-litres mixture contains juice and water in the ratio 5:3. How much water (in litres) must be added to this mixture to change the ratio of juice to water to 2:3?,15.5litres,22.5 litres,25 litres,30 litres,B,22.5 litres,"Option (2) is correct. Total mixture = 40 litre; Ratio = Juice : Water = 5 : 3 So, juice = 5 8 × 40 = 25 litres And, water = 3 8 × 40 = 15 litres Let x litres of water be added, then 25 15 + x = 2 3 25 × 3 = 2(15 + x) 75 = 30 + 2x x = 22.5",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2025/12%20Sep%20S1%202025.pdf
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20446,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,"A circular pizza having a radius of 21 cm. If 75% of it is eaten, what is the area of pizza remaining?",173.25 cm2,346.36 cm2,432.25 cm2,115.5 cm2,B,346.36 cm2,"Option (2) is correct. Radius of circular pizza = 21 cm Since, 75% of pizza is eaten, so 25% of pizza is remaining. Hence, required area = 25 100 × p × 21 × 21 = 1 4 × 3.141 × 21 × 21 = 346.3 cm2",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2025/12%20Sep%20S1%202025.pdf
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20447,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Geometry,English,A ring-shaped disc has an outer radius of 10 cm and an inner radius of 7 cm. What is the approximate ratio of the ring's area to the whole outer circle?,1 : 2,2 : 3,3 : 4,4 : 5,A,1 : 2,"Option (1) is correct. Outer radius = 10 cm, inner radius = 7 cm Area of outer circle = 100p cm2 Area of inner circle = 49p cm2 Hence, area of ring = 100p – 49p = 51p ≈ 50p cm2 So, ratio = 50p : 100p = 1 : 2",Medium,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2025/12%20Sep%20S1%202025.pdf
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20448,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,A bicycle wheel has a radius of 35 cm. What percentage of its circumference is covered in a quarter turn? (Use p = 22 7 ),15%,25%,30%,"35% 74. The line y = mx + 5 passes through (1,8). Find m. 1. 5 2. 4 3. 3 4. 2 75. 313 + 183 – 373 + 210 is equal to: 1. –36810 2. –14820 3. 45670 4. –23450 English Comprehension 76. Choose the correct one-word substitute for: 'An official reprimand or strong criticism'. 1. Accusation 2. Denunciation 3. Censure 4. Indictment",B,25%,"Option (2) is correct. Radius of wheel = 35 cm Circumference of wheel = 2pr = 2 × 22 7 × 35 = 220 cm Distance covered in a quarter turn = 220 4 = 55 cm So, required percentage = 55 220 100 × = 25%",Hard,Verified,Verified (Archived Official Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 1),https://www.oswaal360.com/pluginfile.php/10939/mod_folder/content/0/SSC/SSC%20CGL/2025/12%20Sep%20S1%202025.pdf
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20449,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Synonyms,English,Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: ABNEGATE,Demand,Accept,Renounce,Support,C,Renounce,"Abnegate means to renounce or give up (a right, a pleasure, a belief). Demand, accept and support do not carry this meaning.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20450,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Idioms & Phrases,English,Choose the correct meaning of idiom: Move heaven and earth,To relocate frequently,To work tirelessly to achieve something,To stay silent in protest,To follow blindly,B,To work tirelessly to achieve something,To move heaven and earth means to make every possible effort to get something done.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20451,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Antonyms,English,Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. Puissant,Feeble,Robust,Powerful,Strong,A,Feeble,"Puissant means powerful or mighty. Its opposite is feeble; robust, powerful and strong are near-synonyms.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20452,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Spelling Correction,English,Identify the misspelt word,Supersede,Perseverance,Priviledge,Assassinate,C,Priviledge,"The correct spelling is privilege (no d). Supersede, perseverance and assassinate are spelt correctly.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20453,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Spelling Correction,English,Spot the correct spelling of a drug-effect psychology field.,Psychopharmacology,Psychopharmacholog,Psychopharmeocology,Psychopharmocology,A,Psychopharmacology,Psychopharmacology is the study of how drugs affect the mind and behaviour. The other options misspell -pharmacology.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20454,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,One Word Substitution,English,Choose the correct one-word substitute for: 'A person who abstains from all forms of indulgence'.,Ascetic,Agnostic,Mystic,Skeptic,A,Ascetic,"An ascetic avoids all forms of indulgence, especially for spiritual reasons. An agnostic is unsure whether God exists, a mystic seeks union with the divine, and a skeptic doubts accepted claims.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20455,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Reading Comprehension,English,Select the correct option: Neither the principal investigator ___ the co-authors anticipated the backlash.,nor,or,and,nor did,A,nor,"Neither is always paired with nor: Neither the principal investigator nor the co-authors anticipated the backlash. The verb anticipated is already present, so nor did would add a second verb.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20456,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,"Select the correct option: The board will convene next Friday, ___ final approval is expected.",at which,on which,when,whereupon,C,when,"The blank links a clause to the time next Friday, so when fits: The board will convene next Friday, when final approval is expected. SSC’s key is when; whereupon would mean as a result of which.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20457,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Select the correct option: Nothing short of a paradigm shift will ___ the entrenched bureaucratic inertia.,persuade,dislodge,dissuasion,disillusion,B,dislodge,"Inertia is shaken loose or dislodged. Persuade needs a person as object, dissuasion is a noun, and disillusion means to disappoint.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20458,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Error Spotting,English,"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error: Much of what appears to be coordination (1)/ among the regulatory bodies and private stakeholders (2)/ are, in fact, coincidental overlaps (3)/ caused by differing mandates. (4)",(1),(2),(3),(4),C,(3),"The subject is Much of what appears to be coordination, an uncountable noun phrase that takes a singular verb. Part (3) should read is, in fact, coincidental overlaps, not are.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20459,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Error Spotting,English,"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error: That the framework lacks provisions for backward compatibility (1)/ is less problematic than the assumption (2)/ that all peripheral institutions will, without coercion, (3)/ adheres to the central directive as framed. (4)",(1),(2),(3),(4),D,(4),"After the modal will the base form of the verb is needed: that all peripheral institutions will, without coercion, adhere to the central directive. So part (4), adheres, contains the error.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20460,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Change the following from active to passive: People can seldom access archived manuscripts without clearance.,Archived manuscripts can seldom being accessed without clearance.,Archived manuscripts could seldom be accessed without clearance.,Archived manuscripts can seldom be accessed without clearance.,Archived manuscripts are seldom able to be accessed without clearance.,C,Archived manuscripts can seldom be accessed without clearance.,Active: People can seldom access archived manuscripts. In the passive the modal stays and is followed by be + past participle: Archived manuscripts can seldom be accessed without clearance. Could changes the tense and can being is ungrammatical.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20461,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word: The prince’s ‘gules’ dominated the family coat of arms. (Highlighted word shown in quotes.),The tapestry featured gules and argent prominently.,The chef prepared a sauce of deep gules and cumin.,The gules border signified martial lineage.,The herald explained the symbolism of gules to visitors.,B,The chef prepared a sauce of deep gules and cumin.,"Gules is the heraldic word for red. Sentences (a), (c) and (d) use it in that heraldic sense. SSC’s key marks (b), where gules is used outside heraldry as a colour of a sauce. Note: dictionaries record no separate culinary meaning for gules, so (b) is not a true homonym; we keep SSC’s answer because it is the only option that moves the word out of heraldry.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20462,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Active & Passive Voice,English,Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure: The package is delivered to the office every morning.,The office delivers the package every morning.,Someone delivers the package to the office every morning.,The office has delivered the package every morning.,The package delivers itself to the office every morning.,B,Someone delivers the package to the office every morning.,Passive: The package is delivered to the office every morning (no agent given). In the active a general subject is supplied and the tense stays simple present: Someone delivers the package to the office every morning.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20463,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,"What primary democratic function does social media serve, as per the paragraph?",Promoting entertainment,Replacing newspapers,Facilitating free flow of information,Organizing trade unions,C,Facilitating free flow of information,The passage says democracy thrives on the free flow of information and that social media democratises this process by dismantling gatekeeping. So its main democratic function is facilitating the free flow of information.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20464,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,What makes social media a double-edged tool in democratic societies?,Its affordability,Its visual design,Its ability to spread both truth and misinformation,Its international reach,C,Its ability to spread both truth and misinformation,The passage calls social media double-edged because the same platforms that disseminate truth can also propagate misinformation.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20465,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,"According to the paragraph, which element amplifies marginalized voices through social media?",Editorial boards,Gatekeeping journalism,Viral reach and grassroots mobilization,Institutional press,C,Viral reach and grassroots mobilization,"It says grassroots movements harness virality to amplify marginalised voices, so viral reach and grassroots mobilisation do this.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20466,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Reading Comprehension,English,What does the author suggest as a critical solution to social media misuse in democracies?,Enhanced meme culture,Legalizing all content,Algorithmic transparency and media literacy,Global censorship policies,C,Algorithmic transparency and media literacy,"The passage lists regulatory oversight, media literacy and algorithmic transparency as essential to harness social media’s democratic potential. The matching option is algorithmic transparency and media literacy.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20467,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Reading Comprehension,English,"In the author’s view, what determines whether social media supports or undermines democracy?",Political advertisements,How platforms are funded,Societal intent and ethical usage,Popularity of influencers,C,Societal intent and ethical usage,"The author calls social media a mirror of societal intent, and says its role depends on the ethical frameworks governing its use and on how it is wielded. That is societal intent and ethical usage.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20468,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence: No sooner had I reached the station ‘when the train departed’. (Highlighted part shown in quotes.),than the train departed,then the train departed,when the train had departed,than did the train depart,A,than the train departed,No sooner is always followed by than: No sooner had I reached the station than the train departed. Option (d) wrongly adds a second inversion.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20469,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence: The manager ‘asked to the clerk to submit the report’. (Highlighted part shown in quotes.),asked the clerk that submit the report,requested the clerk to submit report,asked the clerk to submit the report,told to the clerk submit report,C,asked the clerk to submit the report,Ask takes a direct object without to: The manager asked the clerk to submit the report.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20470,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Direct & Indirect Speech,English,"A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech. She said, “I saw him last night.”",She said she had seen him the previous night.,She said she has seen him last night.,She said she was seeing him last night.,She said she had saw him the previous night.,A,She said she had seen him the previous night.,"In reported speech after said, the past simple saw becomes past perfect had seen, I becomes she, and last night becomes the previous night: She said she had seen him the previous night.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20471,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Direct & Indirect Speech,English,"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech. The librarian said that silence must be maintained in the library.","“Silence should be maintained in the library,” said the librarian.","“You will maintain silence in the library,” the librarian said.","“Maintain silence in the library,” said the librarian.",“Must you maintain silence in the library?” asked the librarian.,C,"“Maintain silence in the library,” said the librarian.","The reported sentence gives an order: silence must be maintained. In direct speech an order is usually an imperative: Maintain silence in the library, said the librarian. SSC’s key is this option; (a) weakens must to should, and (b) and (d) change the meaning.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20472,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles),English,"Rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph: 1. Consequently, effective communication hinges on more than just the words we choose. 2. Non-verbal cues, such as tone of voice, facial expressions, and body language, can convey more meaning than the verbal message itself. 3. Communication is a complex process involving the exchange of information, ideas, and feelings between individuals. 4. It's often the subtle signals that tell us how a message is truly being received or intended.","3, 2, 1, 4","2, 4, 1, 3","1, 4, 3, 2","3, 4, 2, 1",A,"3, 2, 1, 4","Sentence 3 introduces communication as a complex process. Sentence 2 says non-verbal cues carry much of the meaning. Sentence 1 (Consequently) concludes that words alone are not enough, and sentence 4 adds that subtle signals show how a message is received. Order: 3, 2, 1, 4.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20473,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles),English,"Rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph: 1. A key strategy is to diversify energy sources, transitioning from fossil fuels to renewable alternatives like solar, wind, and geothermal power.2. To mitigate the worst effects of climate change, the global community must drastically reduce its reliance on carbon-intensive energy production.3. This shift not only decreases greenhouse gas emissions but also improves air quality and creates new economic opportunities.4. Additionally, policies that promote energy efficiency in buildings and transportation can further lower overall energy consumption.","2, 1, 3, 4","1, 2, 3, 4","4, 1, 2, 3","2, 3, 1, 4",A,"2, 1, 3, 4","Sentence 2 states the goal of cutting dependence on carbon-intensive energy. Sentence 1 gives a key strategy (renewables). Sentence 3 (This shift) explains its benefits, and sentence 4 (Additionally) adds energy efficiency. Order: 2, 1, 3, 4.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20474,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,History,English,Read the below statements marked as Assertion (A) and Reason (R). Mark the correct options: Assertion (A): Humayun’s Tomb was the first major Mughal garden tomb and directly inspired the design of the Taj Mahal. Reason (R): It introduced the charbagh garden layout and double-domed mausoleum style that became characteristic of later Mughal architecture.,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A.","Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A.","A is true, but R is false.","A is false, but R is true",A,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A.",Humayun’s Tomb in Delhi (1560s-70s) was the first garden tomb on the Indian subcontinent and a model for the Taj Mahal. It brought in the char-bagh (four-part garden) setting and the tall double dome that later Mughal tombs used. So both are true and R explains A.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20475,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,History,English,Which ancient ruler’s administration is noted for its highly centralized structure?,Harshavardhana,Samudragupta,Chandragupta Maurya,Pulakeshin II,C,Chandragupta Maurya,"The Mauryan state of Chandragupta Maurya (with Chanakya, as described in the Arthashastra and by Megasthenes) had a highly centralised administration: a powerful king, a council of ministers, many departments, spies and royal officials down to the village. Later rulers such as Harsha and the Guptas relied more on feudatories.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20476,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Which of the following correctly reflects the evolution of Indian classical music?,Jatis evolved from ragas as per ancient texts,72-mela system was given by Bharata in 13th century,Folk music originally used mela and grama scales,Ragas evolved from jatis; 72-mela was by Venkatamakhi,D,Ragas evolved from jatis; 72-mela was by Venkatamakhi,"Ancient texts (Natyashastra, Brihaddeshi) describe jatis as the forerunners of ragas, so ragas evolved from jatis, not the other way round. The 72-melakarta scheme was set out by Venkatamakhi in the Chaturdandi Prakashika (17th century), not by Bharata. Only option 4 is correct.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20477,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"Consider the following statements about the phases of long jump: 1) The athlete attains maximum momentum by running on the runway before take-off. 2) During take-off, the athlete pushes off with the weaker foot to maintain balance. Which of the statements given above are correct?",Only 1 is Correct,Only 2 is Correct,1 and 2 are correct,Neither 1 nor 2 are Correct,A,Only 1 is Correct,Statement 1 is correct: the approach run builds maximum horizontal speed before take-off. Statement 2 is wrong: the jumper takes off from the stronger foot to get the most powerful push. So only 1 is correct.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20478,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Mary Kom’s most recent international gold medal was won at which tournament?,"Asian Games, Hangzhou","President’s Cup, Indonesia","Commonwealth Games, Birmingham","Olympic Games, Tokyo",B,"President’s Cup, Indonesia","M.C. Mary Kom won her last international gold at the 23rd President’s Cup in Labuan Bajo, Indonesia, in July 2019 (51 kg, beating April Franks 5-0). Later she won bronze at the 2019 World Championships and lost in the Tokyo 2020 pre-quarterfinal.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20479,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,The Regulating Act of 1773 primarily introduced changes in the Company's administration in which two distinct areas?,Company's Judicial system and revenue collection.,Company's Military strategy and trade regulations.,Company's constitution at home and territorial control in India.,Company's relations with princely states and foreign policy.,C,Company's constitution at home and territorial control in India.,"The Regulating Act of 1773 changed the Company’s constitution at home (rules for the Court of Directors and Court of Proprietors) and its government in India (a Governor-General of Bengal with a council, control over Bombay and Madras, and a Supreme Court at Calcutta).",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20480,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,History,English,Consider the following statements regarding India’s water-sharing treaties with its neighbours: 1) The Mahakali Treaty signed with Nepal in 1996 includes provisions for integrated development of the Mahakali River and the Pancheshwar Project. 2) The Ganga Water Treaty signed with Bangladesh in 1996 allows for the sharing of Ganga waters at Farakka throughout the entire year. Which of the statements above is/are correct?,Only 1 is Correct,Only 2 is Correct,Both 1 and 2 are Correct,Neither 1 nor 2 are Correct,A,Only 1 is Correct,"Statement 1 is correct: the 1996 Mahakali Treaty with Nepal covers integrated development of the Mahakali river, including the Pancheshwar project. Statement 2 is wrong: the 1996 Ganga Waters Treaty sets sharing at Farakka for the lean season (1 January to 31 May), not the whole year.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20481,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"Fill in the blank: Under the SLKIC vertical of Khelo India, ____ Kendriya Vidyalayas have been adopted in partnership with KVS.",3,4,5,6,B,4,"Under the State Level Khelo India Centres (SLKIC) vertical, four Kendriya Vidyalayas (Gwalior, Ghaziabad, Delhi Cantt. and Sidhi) have been adopted as SLKICs in partnership with the Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan (Khelo India website; PIB).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20482,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,"Consider the following statements about “The Adventures of Kakababu, Volume 1” by Sunil Gangopadhyaya: 1) A pioneering Bengali adventure novel featuring detective Kakababu with mystery and cultural themes. 2) A political satire on post-independence Indian governance. 3) An autobiography of the author’s freedom fighter experiences in Bengal. Which of the above statements is/are correct?",Only statement 1 is correct,Only statement 2 is correct,Statements 2 and 3 are correct,"1, 2 and 3 are correct",A,Only statement 1 is correct,"Sunil Gangopadhyay’s Kakababu stories are Bengali adventure-mystery novels featuring Kakababu (Raja Roy Chowdhury), so statement 1 is correct. The book is neither a political satire nor an autobiography.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20483,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,"Which indian political leader addressed a special session in 2025 on “Environment, COP-30, and Global Health”?",Piyush Goyal,Hardeep Puri,Narendra Modi,S. Jaishankar,C,Narendra Modi,"Prime Minister Narendra Modi addressed the session on Environment, COP-30 and Global Health at the 17th BRICS Summit in Rio de Janeiro on 7 July 2025 (PIB, 7 July 2025).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20484,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Which of the following types of landslides involves backward rotation of the slipping material?,Rockslide,Rock fall,Slump,Debris fall,C,Slump,"A slump is a slide in which a block of earth or rock moves down along a curved surface and rotates backwards as it slips. A rockslide moves along a flat plane, and rock falls and debris falls drop freely.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20485,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,What is meant by population density?,Population per household,People per square kilometre,People per region,People per district,B,People per square kilometre,"Population density is the number of people living per unit area, usually stated as persons per square kilometre.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20486,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are given below. Choose the correct option: Assertion (A): Population explosion occurs when death rates decline rapidly but birth rates remain high. Reason (R): Societal reproductive behavior changes instantly with improvements in healthcare.,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation","A is true, but R is false","A is false, but R is true",C,"A is true, but R is false","A is true: a population explosion happens when death rates fall fast (better health care, food) while birth rates stay high. R is false: reproductive behaviour changes slowly, over a generation or more; that time lag is exactly why the explosion occurs.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20487,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,Geography,English,Which of the following best reflects the fundamental objective of applying generative design in aerospace systems engineering?,Facilitating seamless integration of multi-payload platforms in shared bus structures,Optimizing mechanical configurations for minimum mass and maximum structural resilience,Enhancing life-support redundancies to meet crew safety protocols in deep-space missions,Designing adaptive thrust mechanisms to dynamically control orbital corrections,B,Optimizing mechanical configurations for minimum mass and maximum structural resilience,Generative design uses algorithms to explore many shapes and pick structures that meet load and strength limits with the least material. In aerospace the aim is parts with minimum mass and maximum structural strength.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20488,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,Biology,English,The function of lysosomes in cells is:,Protein synthesis,Intracellular digestion,Energy production,Genetic information storage,B,Intracellular digestion,"Lysosomes contain digestive (hydrolytic) enzymes and break down food particles, worn-out organelles and microbes inside the cell, i.e. intracellular digestion. They are called the suicide bags of the cell.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20489,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,Indian Polity & Constitution,English,"Which of the following statements regarding Article 270 are correct? 1) Article 270 governs the sharing of taxes between the Union and States, including proceeds from GST. 2) After the 101st Constitutional Amendment, Article 270 includes provisions for distributing revenue from Union taxes and GST. 3) The GST Compensation Cess is also shared between the Union and States under Article 270.",1 and 3 only,1 Only,1 & 2 only,2 & 3 only,C,1 & 2 only,"Article 270, as amended by the 101st Amendment (2016), governs how Union taxes, including GST collected by the Union, are distributed between the Union and the States, so 1 and 2 are correct. The GST Compensation Cess was levied under a separate law and paid to States as compensation; it is not part of the divisible pool shared under Article 270, so 3 is wrong.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20490,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"If Earth's radius were reduced by 1% while its mass remained unchanged, what would be the effect on the gravitational acceleration at its surface?",Increase by approximately 1%,Decrease by approximately 2%,Increase by approximately 2%,Decrease by approximately 1%,C,Increase by approximately 2%,"g = GM/R². With M fixed, g is proportional to 1/R². If R becomes 0.99R, g becomes g/0.9801 ≈ 1.0203g, an increase of about 2%.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20491,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,Chemistry,English,"Under Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita(BNSS), what is the maximum period for which a person can be held in police custody in total, even if remanded periodically by a magistrate?",30 days,60 days,90 days,"15 days (for initial remand, extendable)",D,"15 days (for initial remand, extendable)","Under Section 187(2) of the BNSS, police custody can total at most 15 days. These can be taken in one stretch or in parts during the first 40 or 60 days of the 60- or 90-day detention period. The keyed option, 15 days, is that cap. Note: its wording (extendable) is loose, because the total of 15 days cannot be exceeded; only the window in which it is used is wider.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20492,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,What is the age range for farmers to enrol in the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maandhan Yojana (PM-KMY)?,18–30 years,18–40 years,21–45 years,25–50 years,B,18–40 years,"The Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maandhan Yojana (2019), a pension scheme for small and marginal farmers, is open to farmers aged 18 to 40 years. It pays a pension of ₹3,000 a month from age 60.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20493,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,Read the below statements marked as Assertion (A) and Reason (R). Mark the correct options: Assertion (A): UDAN Scheme improves regional air connectivity. Reason (R): It provides financial viability gap funding to airlines.,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A","A is true, but R is false","A is false, but R is true",A,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","UDAN (Ude Desh ka Aam Nagrik, 2016) improves regional air connectivity, and a key tool for that is viability gap funding to airlines on under-served routes, along with concessions from the Centre, states and airports. So both are true and R explains A.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20494,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,"According to the Global Cities Index 2025 by Oxford Economics, which two cities retained their top positions?",Tokyo and Beijing,London and New York,Paris and Rome,Berlin and Moscow,B,London and New York,"In Oxford Economics’ Global Cities Index 2025, New York stayed 1st and London 2nd, the same top two as in 2024 (Oxford Economics, May 2025).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20495,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,History,English,Which of the following statements about light industries is correct?,They process heavy ores and minerals.,They produce large-scale industrial machinery.,They require bulky and heavy raw materials.,Use light materials to make consumer goods,D,Use light materials to make consumer goods,"Light industries use light raw materials and make consumer goods such as garments, electronics and food products. Processing heavy ores, bulky raw materials and big machinery are features of heavy industry.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20496,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,Indian Polity & Constitution,English,Schedule VII of the Constitution contains ______.,Election guidelines,Three legislative lists,Emergency powers,Judicial provisions,B,Three legislative lists,"The Seventh Schedule divides legislative subjects into three lists: the Union List, the State List and the Concurrent List.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20497,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,Geography,English,A coastal city implements a plan to build sea walls and elevate buildings in response to rising sea levels. This action primarily falls under which category of climate change response?,Climate Change Mitigation.,Carbon Sequestration.,Geoengineering.,Climate Change Adaptation.,D,Climate Change Adaptation.,Building sea walls and raising buildings protects people from the effects of climate change that are already happening. That is adaptation. Mitigation means cutting greenhouse gas emissions; carbon sequestration and geoengineering are ways of reducing or offsetting warming.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20498,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Awareness,Indian Economy,English,What specific physical quantity ensures a satellite maintains its orbit without continuous propulsion?,Mass,Gravitational pull,Orbital velocity,Atmospheric drag,C,Orbital velocity,"A satellite stays in orbit because it moves sideways at its orbital velocity: gravity keeps pulling it inward, and this speed makes it keep falling around the Earth instead of into it. Without that velocity gravity alone would bring it down, and atmospheric drag only slows it.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20499,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,"In the following question, select the related word from the given alternatives Liberty : Autonomy :: Equality : ?",Legitimacy,Neutrality,Fairness,Diversity,C,Fairness,"Pairs of near-synonyms from political ideas. Liberty is close in meaning to autonomy (self-rule); equality is closest to fairness, i.e. equal and just treatment. Legitimacy, neutrality and diversity are different concepts.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20500,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,"Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series. BGL, GLQ, LQV, QVA, ?",ZAS,OKS,VAF,AVG,C,VAF,"Every letter moves 5 places forward: B→G→L→Q→V, G→L→Q→V→A, L→Q→V→A→F (wrapping after Z). So QVA is followed by VAF.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20501,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,"Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series. DAG, FCI, ? , JGM, LIO",GDJ,IFL,HKE,HEK,D,HEK,Each letter moves 2 places forward from one term to the next: DAG → FCI → HEK → JGM → LIO. The missing term is HEK.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20502,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Which of the following alternatives will replace the question mark? Atom, Molecule, Cell, ?",Tissue,Proton,System,Gene,A,Tissue,"The series climbs the levels of biological organisation: atom → molecule → cell → tissue (then organ, system). Proton is smaller than an atom and gene is part of a cell, so Tissue comes next.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20503,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"Complete the series: __________, 150, 183, 219, 258",120,148,361,247,A,120,"The differences are 183 − 150 = 33, 219 − 183 = 36, 258 − 219 = 39, rising by 3. The difference before 33 is 30, so the first term is 150 − 30 = 120.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20504,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"What will come at the place of question mark? 2, 12, 30, 56, 90, ?",132,140,142,150,A,132,"Each term is n(n + 1) for odd n: 1×2 = 2, 3×4 = 12, 5×6 = 30, 7×8 = 56, 9×10 = 90, so the next is 11×12 = 132. (Differences 10, 18, 26, 34, 42 also rise by 8.)",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20505,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Syllogism & Statements,English,Read the following statement carefully and identify the conclusion that follows. Statement: Most farmers in the region depend on monsoon rains for irrigation. Conclusions: I. The region does not have proper irrigation infrastructure. II. A weak monsoon may reduce agricultural output.,Only Conclusion I follows,Only Conclusion II follows,Both I and II follow,Neither I nor II follows,B,Only Conclusion II follows,"If farmers depend on rain, a weak monsoon will hurt crops, so II follows. Dependence on rain does not prove there is no irrigation infrastructure at all; it may simply be insufficient, so I does not follow.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20506,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Instruction: Identify the assumptions that must hold for the statement to be valid, then choose the correct option. Statement: The discovery of exoplanets in habitable zones around distant stars has provided exciting prospects for the search for extraterrestrial life, yet the vast distances and technological limitations pose significant obstacles to direct exploration. Assumptions: I. Exoplanets located in habitable zones may have the potential to support life. II. Current technology is insufficient to directly explore exoplanets in habitable zones. III. Direct exploration of exoplanets will be unnecessary if we detect signs of life remotely.",Only I and II are implicit,Only II and III are implicit,Only I is implicit,All assumptions are implicit,A,Only I and II are implicit,"Calling the search for life on these planets exciting assumes they may support life (I). Saying distance and technology block direct exploration assumes present technology is not enough (II). Nothing in the statement says direct exploration would become unnecessary, so III is not implicit.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20507,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"How many meaningful four-letter English words can be formed using the first, second, third, and sixth letters of the word “PROVIDE” (when counted from left to right), using each letter only once in each word?",One,Three,Two,Five,B,Three,"The letters are P, R, O and D (1st, 2nd, 3rd and 6th letters of PROVIDE). Common words: DROP and PROD; the third word counted in SSC’s key is DORP (a hamlet or village, valid in standard word lists). SSC’s key is Three. Note: DORP is rare, so many candidates counted only two; we keep SSC’s official answer.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20508,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Which of the following addresses are identical to each other: 1. Rajeev Chauhan 3/5, Lotus Enclave, Kanpur, 208012 2. Rajeev Chauhan 3-5, Lotus Enclave, Kanpur , 208012 3. Rajeev Chauhan 3-5, Lotus Enclave, Kanpur , 208012 4. Rajeev Chauhan 3-5, Lotus Enclave, Kanpur , 208002",1 and 2,2 and 3,2 and 4,3 and 4,B,2 and 3,"Address 1 writes the house number as 3/5 while the others write 3-5, and address 4 has PIN 208002 instead of 208012. Addresses 2 and 3 match exactly.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20509,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,Each of the letters in the word STAMINA is arranged in alphabetical order. How many letters are there in the English alphabetical series between the letter that is first from the left and the one that is fourth from the right in the new letter-cluster formed?,11,12,13,14,A,11,STAMINA in alphabetical order: A A I M N S T. First from the left is A (1st letter of the alphabet); fourth from the right is M (13th). Letters between A and M: 13 − 1 − 1 = 11.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20510,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,Find the best option that best completes the analogy. NPR : OQS :: XYZ : ?,YZA,ZAB,YAC,YAZ,A,YZA,"Each letter moves one place forward: N→O, P→Q, R→S. So X→Y, Y→Z, Z→A (wrapping after Z), giving YZA.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20511,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"In a row of 50 books, Book A is 15th from left and Book B is 20th from right. How many books lie between them?",17,15,12,10,B,15,"Book B is 20th from the right in a row of 50, so it is 50 − 20 + 1 = 31st from the left. Books between the 15th and the 31st: 31 − 15 − 1 = 15.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20512,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,"In each of the following questions, the second word is formed by rearranging the letters of the first word according to a specific pattern. Identify that pattern and apply the same to the third word to find the correct answer from the given alternatives. NUMERAL : UEALRMN :: ALGEBRA : ?",LRBAGEA,BARLAGE,LERAGBA,LERABGA,D,LERABGA,"NUMERAL has letters at positions 1-7. UEALRMN takes them in the order 2, 4, 6, 7, 5, 3, 1. Applying the same order to ALGEBRA (A L G E B R A) gives L, E, R, A, B, G, A = LERABGA.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20513,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Classification (Odd One Out),English,Find the odd one out from the given alternatives:,TDS,GST,VAT,DNA,D,DNA,"TDS (tax deducted at source), GST (goods and services tax) and VAT (value added tax) are all taxes. DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is a biological molecule, so it is the odd one.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20514,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"If A is the son of B, and B is the brother of C, how is C related to A?",Father,Uncle,Brother,Cousin,B,Uncle,B is A’s parent (A is B’s son) and C is B’s sibling. A parent’s sibling is an uncle or aunt; among the options only Uncle fits.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20515,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"One number is not like the others: 1331, 2197, 3375, 4096",1331,3375,4096,2197,C,4096,"1331 = 11³, 2197 = 13³ and 3375 = 15³ are cubes of odd numbers (and are odd). 4096 = 16³ is the cube of an even number, so it is the odd one out.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20516,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Find the number that breaks the pattern: 2, 5, 10, 17, 28, 40, 58",10,17,40,28,C,40,"The differences should be consecutive primes: 2 (+3) 5 (+5) 10 (+7) 17 (+11) 28 (+13) 41 (+17) 58. The series shows 40 instead of 41, so 40 breaks the pattern.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20517,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Coding & Decoding,English,"In a certain code language, each letter is assigned a unique digit. Based on the given codes for specific words, determine the code for the target word using the same logic. If MOUSE is coded as 45291 and RAT as 786, how is STORE coded?",96571,97653,98345,96278,A,96571,"From MOUSE = 45291: M=4, O=5, U=2, S=9, E=1. From RAT = 786: R=7, A=8, T=6. STORE = S T O R E = 9 6 5 7 1 = 96571.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20518,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"If 7 ＄ 3 = 58 and 6 ＄ 2 = 40, what is 5 ＄ 1?",26,24,28,22,A,26,a ＄ b = a² + b²: 7² + 3² = 49 + 9 = 58 and 6² + 2² = 36 + 4 = 40. So 5 ＄ 1 = 25 + 1 = 26.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20519,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"Pointing to a girl, a woman says, 'She is the daughter of my mother’s only daughter.’ How is the girl related to the woman?",Daughter,Daughter-in-law,Cousin,Sister,A,Daughter,The only daughter of the woman’s mother is the woman herself. So the girl is the daughter of the woman.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20520,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"A woman says, “This man's son's sister is my daughter.” How is the woman related to the man?",Wife,Sister,Mother,Daughter-in-law,A,Wife,"The man’s son’s sister is the man’s daughter, and she is also the woman’s daughter. The two are her parents, so the woman is the man’s wife.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20521,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Two numbers are in ratio 7:9, and their sum is 128. Find the numbers.","49, 79","56, 72","62, 66","70, 58",B,"56, 72","Let the numbers be 7x and 9x. Then 16x = 128, so x = 8 and the numbers are 56 and 72.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20522,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Mathematical Operations,English,"If 16+11=A and 1/9=B, and A % B=(A×B)−1, then what is A % B?",0,−3,2,5,C,2,A = 16 + 11 = 27 and B = 1/9. A % B = (A × B) − 1 = 27 × 1/9 − 1 = 3 − 1 = 2.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20523,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"If the sum of 28 and 22 is multiplied by 8, what is the result?",384,400,415,416,B,400,28 + 22 = 50 and 50 × 8 = 400.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20524,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Algebra,English,Let x = √3 + √5 and y = √8 + √2. Which is greater?,x = y,x > y,x < y,Cannot be determined,C,x < y,"x = √3 + √5 ≈ 1.732 + 2.236 = 3.968 and y = √8 + √2 ≈ 2.828 + 1.414 = 4.243. So x < y. (Squaring: x² = 8 + 2√15 ≈ 15.75, y² = 10 + 2√16 = 18.)",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20525,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Ratio & Proportion,English,"The number of red, blue, and green marbles in a bag is in the ratio 3 : 4 : 6. If 20 red marbles, 15 blue marbles, and an unknown number of green marbles are added to the bag, the ratio of red, blue, and green marbles becomes 4 : 5 : 7. Determine the number of green marbles added.",3,5,7,9,B,5,"Let the counts be 3k, 4k, 6k. After adding: (3k + 20) : (4k + 15) = 4 : 5, so 15k + 100 = 16k + 60 and k = 40. Red = 140, blue = 175, so one ratio unit is 35 and green must become 7 × 35 = 245. Green was 6 × 40 = 240, so 5 were added.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20526,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,Evaluate the continued fraction: x = 2 + 1/(3 + 1/(4 + 1/2)),67/29,41/17,45/19,47/20,A,67/29,Work from the inside: 4 + 1/2 = 9/2; 3 + 2/9 = 29/9; 1 ÷ 29/9 = 9/29; x = 2 + 9/29 = 67/29.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20527,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A and B invest ₹40,000 and ₹60,000 respectively in a business. What is A's share in a profit of ₹50,000?","₹15,000","₹20,000","₹25,000","₹30,000",B,"₹20,000","Profit is shared in the ratio of capital, 40,000 : 60,000 = 2 : 3. A’s share = 2/5 × 50,000 = ₹20,000.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20528,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A and B contribute to a business investment in the ratio 3:5. They earn a profit of ₹64,000. A is a working partner and receives 10% of the profit extra. What is A’s total share?","₹26,500","₹28,000","₹38,500","₹36,000",B,"₹28,000","A first gets 10% of ₹64,000 = ₹6,400 as working partner. The remaining ₹57,600 is split 3 : 5, so A gets 3/8 × 57,600 = ₹21,600. Total = 6,400 + 21,600 = ₹28,000.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20529,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"In a team of 75 employees, the average monthly sales per employee is ₹ 1.8 lakh. If 30 junior employees average ₹ 1.2 lakh each, what is the average monthly sales figure (in ₹ lakh) for the senior employees?",₹4.2 lakh,₹2.2 lakh,₹2.8 lakh,₹2.7 lakh,B,₹2.2 lakh,"Total sales = 75 × 1.8 = 135 lakh. Juniors = 30 × 1.2 = 36 lakh. The other 45 seniors make 135 − 36 = 99 lakh, an average of 99/45 = ₹2.2 lakh.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20530,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"The price of petrol shot up by 5%. Before the hike, the price was Rs. 82 per litre. A man travels 3045 km every month and his car gives a mileage of 15 km per litre. What is the increase in the monthly expenditure (to the nearest Rs.) on the man's travel due to the hike in the petrol prices?",₹820,₹832,₹845,₹850,B,₹832,Petrol used = 3045/15 = 203 litres a month. A 5% rise on ₹82 is ₹4.10 per litre. Extra cost = 203 × 4.10 = ₹832.30 ≈ ₹832.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20531,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A company placed an order for 20 high-end laptops and some quantity of standard desktops. The price of a high-end laptop was 5 times that of a standard desktop. Due to a mistake, the number of laptops and desktops was interchanged in the delivery. This caused the total bill to increase by 80%. What was the ratio of the number of high-end laptops to standard desktops in the original order?",1:2,2:1,5:2,2:5,D,2:5,"Let a desktop cost d and a laptop 5d, with D desktops ordered. Ordered bill = 100d + Dd; delivered bill = 5Dd + 20d. Then 5D + 20 = 1.8(100 + D), so 3.2D = 160 and D = 50. Laptops : desktops = 20 : 50 = 2 : 5.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20532,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"Find the compound interest on ₹8,000 at 12% per annum for 3 years 4 months, compounded annually.","₹3,000","₹4,000","₹3,689","₹3,600",C,"₹3,689","For 3 years: 8000 × 1.12³ = ₹11,239.42. For the extra 4 months (1/3 year) interest is 12% × 1/3 = 4%: 11,239.42 × 1.04 = ₹11,688.99. CI = 11,689 − 8,000 ≈ ₹3,689.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20533,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A candy shop owner buys three kinds of candies: red, blue, and green. Red candies are purchased at 3 for ₹15, blue candies at 4 for ₹18, and green candies at 5 for ₹22. He mixes them in the ratio 1 : 1 : 2. He sells all the mixed candies at 2 for ₹10. What is his approximate gain or loss percentage?",Loss of 9.2%,Profit of 9.29%,Profit of 10%,Loss of 10%,B,Profit of 9.29%,"Cost per candy: red ₹5, blue ₹4.50, green ₹4.40. Mixed 1 : 1 : 2, the average cost is (5 + 4.5 + 2 × 4.4)/4 = ₹4.575. Selling price is ₹5 each. Profit % = 0.425/4.575 × 100 ≈ 9.29%.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20534,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Ratio & Proportion,English,"The ratio of boys to girls in a school is 7:5. If 20 more girls join the school, the new ratio of boys to girls becomes 7:6. What is the total number of students in the school initially?",200,240,300,360,B,240,"Boys 7x, girls 5x. 7x : (5x + 20) = 7 : 6 gives 42x = 35x + 140, so x = 20. Initial total = 12x = 240.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20535,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A, B, and C are capable of completing a job in 30, 45, and 90 days, respectively. A works every day, while B and C join A every fifth day. How long will it take to finish the task?",25 days,18 days,16 days,12 days,A,25 days,A does 1/30 a day. Every 5th day B and C join: 1/30 + 1/45 + 1/90 = 6/90 = 1/15. Work in each 5-day block = 4/30 + 1/15 = 6/30 = 1/5. Five such blocks finish the job: 25 days.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20536,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Simple & Compound Interest,English,"A 100-litre solution contains acid and water in the ratio 3:2. Some quantity of this solution is removed and replaced with pure acid. If the final ratio of acid to water becomes 7:3, how many litres of solution were replaced?",35 litres,25 litres,50 litres,20 litres,B,25 litres,"The 100 litres hold 60 L acid and 40 L water. Removing x litres of mixture removes water in proportion, and the acid added has no water. Water left = 40(1 − x/100), which must be 30% of 100 = 30 L. So x = 25 litres.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20537,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"The ratio of the efficiencies of two workers, P and Q, is 5 : 2. If P can complete a project in 12 days, how many days will Q take to complete the same project alone?",24 days,30 days,35 days,40 days,B,30 days,"Time is inversely proportional to efficiency. Q is 2/5 as efficient as P, so Q takes 12 × 5/2 = 30 days.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20538,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A car starts from point P on a circular track and an SUV starts from point Q, which is 600 meters ahead of P in the direction of motion. The car's speed is 15 m/s, and the SUV's speed is 10 m/s. The circumference of the track is 1.5 km. How much distance will the car have traveled when it first overtakes the SUV?",900 m,1200 m,1500 m,1800 m,D,1800 m,"The car gains 15 − 10 = 5 m/s on the SUV, which is 600 m ahead. It catches up after 600/5 = 120 s, by which time the car has gone 15 × 120 = 1800 m.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20539,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,"A circular park having a radius of 14 m. If a 1.5 m wide path is built around it, what is the approximate area of the path?",139 m²,135 m²,142 m²,150 m²,A,139 m²,Outer radius = 14 + 1.5 = 15.5 m. Path area = π(15.5² − 14²) = 22/7 × (240.25 − 196) = 22/7 × 44.25 ≈ 139 m².,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20540,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,What is 5π/4 radians in degrees?,225°,180°,240°,360°,A,225°,Multiply by 180/π: 5π/4 × 180/π = 225°.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20541,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Algebra,English,The line y = −x + 4 passes through which of the following points?,"(2, 2)","(5, 4)","(1, 2)","(3, 6)",A,"(2, 2)","Substitute each point in y = −x + 4. For (2, 2): −2 + 4 = 2. It works. (5, 4) gives −1, (1, 2) gives 3, and (3, 6) gives 1, so they do not lie on the line.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20542,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,What is the central angle of a sector with an arc length of 10 cm in a circle of radius 5 cm?,6 radians,3 radians,2 radians,4 radians,C,2 radians,"Arc length = rθ, so θ = 10/5 = 2 radians.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20543,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"If tan(90° − A) = √3, what is sin A?",1/2,√3/2,√2/2,3/4,A,1/2,"tan(90° − A) = cot A = √3, so A = 30° and sin A = 1/2.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20544,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Algebra,English,"If x = √7, determine the value of x + 1/x.",8√7/7,7√7/8,7√7/9,9√7/7,A,8√7/7,x + 1/x = √7 + 1/√7 = (7 + 1)/√7 = 8/√7 = 8√7/7.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20545,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Geometry,English,Two triangles are similar with sides in the ratio 3:5. What is the ratio of their areas?,3:5,5:3,9:25,25:9,C,9:25,For similar triangles the ratio of areas is the square of the ratio of sides: 3² : 5² = 9 : 25.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20546,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Algebra,English,"If x = √((2 + √3)/(2 − √3)), then determine the value of x² + x − 9?",3√3,5√3,7√3,9√3,B,5√3,"Rationalise: (2 + √3)/(2 − √3) = (2 + √3)²/(4 − 3) = (2 + √3)², so x = 2 + √3. Then x² = 7 + 4√3 and x² + x − 9 = 7 + 4√3 + 2 + √3 − 9 = 5√3.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20547,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Geometry,English,The angles of a cyclic quadrilateral are in the ratio 1:2:3:4. What is the measure of the smallest angle?,36°,72°,108°,144°,A,36°,"The four angles of any quadrilateral add to 360°. With ratio 1:2:3:4 there are 10 parts, so the smallest is 36° (the others 72°, 108°, 144°, and opposite angles do add to 180° as a cyclic quadrilateral needs).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20548,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"If secA = 13/5 and A is acute, find sinA.",5/13,12/13,13/12,13/5,B,12/13,sec A = 13/5 means cos A = 5/13. Then sin A = √(1 − 25/169) = √(144/169) = 12/13.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20549,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Synonyms,English,Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: NEBULOUS,Vague,Precise,Obvious,Clear,A,Vague,"Nebulous means vague or unclear. Precise, obvious and clear are opposites.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20550,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Antonyms,English,Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. Erudite,Scholarly,Uninformed,Learned,Intellectual,B,Uninformed,"Erudite means learned or scholarly. Its opposite is uninformed; scholarly, learned and intellectual are synonyms.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20551,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Idioms & Phrases,English,Choose the correct meaning of idiom: Fly off the handle,To escape quietly,To disappear quickly,To become suddenly angry,To handle a situation smartly,C,To become suddenly angry,To fly off the handle means to lose one’s temper suddenly.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20552,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Antonyms,English,Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. Encomium,Panegyric,Praise,Castigation,Tribute,C,Castigation,"Encomium is high praise. Its opposite is castigation (severe criticism); panegyric, praise and tribute are synonyms.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20553,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Spelling Correction,English,Spot the correct spelling of a chromosomal “three copies” term.,Trisomie,Trissomy,Trisomy,Trissomie,C,Trisomy,"Trisomy is the condition of having three copies of a chromosome, e.g. trisomy 21 in Down syndrome.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20554,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,One Word Substitution,English,Choose the correct one-word substitute for: 'A state of disuse or inactivity'.,Hiatus,Oblivion,Interregnum,Desuetude,D,Desuetude,"Desuetude means a state of disuse. A hiatus is a pause, oblivion is being forgotten, and an interregnum is a gap between two reigns or governments.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20555,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Select the correct option: So delicate ___ the negotiations that a single leak could derail them.,are,were,is,was,B,were,"In the inverted structure ‘So delicate ___ the negotiations that…’, the subject is the plural noun ‘the negotiations’ (also picked up by ‘derail them’), so the verb must be plural; with ‘could’ in the second clause, the past form fits: ‘So delicate were the negotiations that a single leak could derail them.’ Answer: were. Note: SSC’s official answer key printed ‘was’ in error; a singular verb cannot agree with ‘the negotiations’, so we show the correct answer, ‘were’.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20556,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Select the correct option: Her interpretation was ___ than insightful; it bordered on the revelatory.,less,more,other,rather,B,more,"More … than fits the comparison: her interpretation was more than insightful; it bordered on the revelatory. Less would contradict the second clause, and other/rather do not fit before than here.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20557,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,"Select the correct option: The reforms, while ostensibly motivated by economic exigencies, were in effect a veiled attempt to ___ dissent under the guise of austerity.",quell,swell,rebut,impugn,A,quell,"To quell dissent is to suppress it, which matches a veiled attempt under the guise of austerity. Swell means increase, rebut means argue against, and impugn means call into question.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20558,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Error Spotting,English,"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error: The more senior the position was (1)/ the more urgent became the need (2)/ for discretion, decorum, and (3)/ refraining from premature disclosure. (4)",(1),(2),(3),(4),D,(4),"Parts (3) and (4) form a list after the need for: discretion, decorum, and …. The first two items are nouns, so the third should be a noun too (e.g. restraint from premature disclosure), not the gerund phrase refraining from premature disclosure. SSC’s key marks part (4).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20559,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Error Spotting,English,"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error: The report’s emphasis on techno-optimism, while commendable, (1)/ overlook the structural inequities (2)/ that persist in data accessibility and digital literacy (3)/ across demographic and regional divides. (4)",(1),(2),(3),(4),B,(2),"The subject is The report’s emphasis (singular), so the verb must be overlooks, not overlook. The error is in part (2).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20560,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Change the following from active to passive: Why did the editor overlook the substantial stylistic anomalies?,Why have the substantial stylistic anomalies been overlooked by the editor?,Why are the substantial stylistic anomalies being overlooked by the editor?,Why did the substantial stylistic anomalies be overlooked by the editor?,Why were the substantial stylistic anomalies overlooked by the editor?,D,Why were the substantial stylistic anomalies overlooked by the editor?,"The active question is in the past simple (did overlook), so the passive uses were + past participle: Why were the substantial stylistic anomalies overlooked by the editor?",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20561,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word: The historian referenced a ‘bailey’ in Norman military architecture. (Highlighted word shown in quotes.),The shepherd gathered his sheep in the bailey.,The bailey was reinforced with wooden palisades.,The outer bailey surrounded the motte.,The king’s guard patrolled the lower bailey.,A,The shepherd gathered his sheep in the bailey.,"A bailey is the courtyard of a castle, enclosed by a wall. SSC’s key marks (a), the only sentence with no castle setting, where the bailey is a place for keeping sheep. Note: dictionaries do not list a separate farmyard meaning for bailey, so no option contains a true homonym; we keep SSC’s answer.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20562,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Active & Passive Voice,English,Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure: It has been alleged that confidential data was being leaked by insiders within the firm.,Insiders were leaking confidential data within the firm.,"Confidential data had been leaked by insiders, it is alleged.",Insiders have allegedly been leaking confidential data within the firm.,The firm was allegedly leaking insider data.,C,Insiders have allegedly been leaking confidential data within the firm.,The passive says it is alleged that insiders were leaking data. The active version keeps the allegation and the continuous sense: Insiders have allegedly been leaking confidential data within the firm.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20563,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Reading Comprehension,English,What is the central idea of groupthink as discussed in the passage?,Collaborative brainstorming,Valuing consensus over critique,Trusting only experts,Promoting decentralization,B,Valuing consensus over critique,"The passage defines groupthink as the desire for unanimity overriding critical appraisal of alternatives, i.e. valuing consensus over critique.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20564,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Reading Comprehension,English,"According to the passage, what evolutionary trait contributes to social conformity?",Hunger for dominance,Need for speed,Instinct for tribal survival,Desire for luxury,C,Instinct for tribal survival,"It traces conformity to our evolutionary inclination toward tribal belonging, when deviation meant survival risk, i.e. an instinct for tribal survival.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20565,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Which event is cited as a real-world consequence of groupthink?,Cold War treaty signing,Challenger disaster,Brexit vote,The Dot-com crash,B,Challenger disaster,"The passage cites the Bay of Pigs invasion and the Challenger space shuttle disaster as examples of groupthink. Of the options, only Challenger disaster appears.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20566,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Reading Comprehension,English,"How does digital media reinforce conformity, according to the passage?",By removing controversial content,By presenting data in charts,Through curated echo chambers,By enabling anonymous posts,C,Through curated echo chambers,"Algorithms reinforce conformity by curating information bubbles that validate existing biases, i.e. curated echo chambers.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20567,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,What is suggested as a solution to groupthink and conformity?,Hiring more senior leaders,Mandating compliance,Encouraging constructive dissent,Expanding digital networks,C,Encouraging constructive dissent,The remedy given is institutionalising dissent: constructive disagreement acts as a safeguard against tunnel vision.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20568,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence: She insisted ‘me to take the medicine’. (Highlighted part shown in quotes.),that I take the medicine,me that I take medicine,me taking the medicine,to take medicine by me,A,that I take the medicine,"Insist is followed by on + gerund or by a that-clause, not by an object + to-infinitive: She insisted that I take the medicine.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20569,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence: No one knows ‘where is he hiding’. (Highlighted part shown in quotes.),where is he hide,where he is hiding at,where he is hiding,where he has hidden is,C,where he is hiding,In an indirect (embedded) question the normal statement order is used: No one knows where he is hiding.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20570,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Direct & Indirect Speech,English,"A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech. He said, “I am not feeling well.”",He said that he is not feeling well.,He said that he was not feeling well.,He said that he didn’t felt well.,He said he not feeling well.,B,He said that he was not feeling well.,"After said, present continuous am not feeling becomes past continuous was not feeling, and I becomes he: He said that he was not feeling well.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20571,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Direct & Indirect Speech,English,"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech. The manager told the staff that deadlines must be followed strictly.","“Deadlines must be followed strictly,” said the manager.","“You should follow deadlines strictly,” said the manager.","“Follow deadlines strictly,” the manager said.","“Deadlines are to be followed,” said the manager.",A,"“Deadlines must be followed strictly,” said the manager.","The reported sentence keeps must for obligation and the passive form. The direct version is: Deadlines must be followed strictly, said the manager.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20572,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles),English,Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a logical passage: 1. The team analyzed the survey data. 2. Insights were used to improve the customer experience. 3. A targeted marketing campaign was created. 4. The data was collected through various channels.,1-4-3-2,3-1-2-4,4-3-1-2,4-1-3-2,D,4-1-3-2,"The data was first collected (4), then analysed (1), a targeted campaign was created from it (3), and the insights were used to improve customer experience (2). Order: 4-1-3-2.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20573,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,English Comprehension,Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles),English,"Rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph: 1. These factors include the amount of sunlight received, the composition of the atmosphere, and the Earth's orbit. 2. The long-term variations in Earth's climate are influenced by a complex interplay of natural and anthropogenic factors. 3. The most significant anthropogenic factor is the emission of greenhouse gases from industrial activities. 4. Together, these elements determine the planet's overall energy balance and, consequently, its average temperature.","2, 1, 4, 3","1, 2, 3, 4","3, 4, 1, 2","4, 2, 3, 1",A,"2, 1, 4, 3","Sentence 2 introduces long-term climate variation and its natural and human factors. Sentence 1 (These factors include…) lists natural ones, and sentence 4 (Together, these elements…) sums up their effect on energy balance. Sentence 3 names the main human factor. SSC’s key order is 2, 1, 4, 3.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20574,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,Arrange the following classical dances in chronological order of earliest historical references (oldest to newest): 1. Bharatanatyam 2. Mohiniyattam 3. Kathak 4. Manipuri,1 - 3 - 2 - 4,1 - 2 - 4 - 3,1 - 3 - 4 - 2,1 - 4 - 3 - 2,C,1 - 3 - 4 - 2,"SSC’s order: Bharatanatyam (roots in the Natyashastra and Tamil Sangam-era texts), Kathak (the kathakars, story-tellers of north Indian temples), Manipuri, then Mohiniyattam (associated with 18th-19th century Travancore). Note: earliest references are debated; the term Mohiniyattam appears in a 16th-17th century text, which some place before Manipuri’s earliest dated texts, so option (a) can also be argued. We keep SSC’s key.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20575,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Which of the following pairs is correctly matched with the shape of its roof?,"Latina — rectangular, wagon-shaped","Phamsana — slabs rising to a point, straight incline","Valabhi — tall, curving inward sharply",Latina — low and broad with stepped roofing,B,"Phamsana — slabs rising to a point, straight incline","In north Indian temple architecture, phamsana roofs are made of slabs that rise to a single point in a straight incline, without the inward curve of the tall latina shikhara. Valabhi roofs are rectangular and wagon-vaulted, so options (a), (c) and (d) mismatch the names.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20576,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,"The Pongtu Festival, celebrated by the Tutsa tribe of Arunachal Pradesh, is primarily observed to seek blessings from which deity before millet harvesting?",Donyi-Polo,Rangkhothak,Rangfraa,Nyegi-Nyapa,B,Rangkhothak,"The Tutsa of Changlang and Tirap celebrate Pongtu (Pongtu Kuh) in April, before the millet harvest, offering prayers to the supreme god Rangkhothak for a good harvest and protection from calamities (Changlang district administration).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20577,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,History,English,"Fill in the blanks: In Teen Taal of Hindustani Classical Music, the Khali is marked on the _____ matra.",1,5,9,13,C,9,"Teentaal has 16 beats in four divisions of 4. The sam (1st beat) and the 5th and 13th beats are tali (claps), and the 9th beat is the khali (wave).",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20578,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Why is the weight and circumference of a cricket ball strictly regulated in official matches?,"Heavier balls suit bowlers, lighter ones suit batsmen, so balance is needed","Variations affect bounce, swing, and fairness on standard pitches",ICC mandates it to cut costs and simplify logistics,Only red balls follow this; white balls have separate norms,B,"Variations affect bounce, swing, and fairness on standard pitches","The size and weight of the ball (155.9-163 g for men’s cricket) are fixed by the Laws of Cricket because they change bounce, swing and seam movement. Fixed standards keep matches fair and comparable everywhere.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20579,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,Which Indian athlete won the first-ever Paralympic gold in archery at the Paris 2024 Paralympics?,Sheetal Devi,Harvinder Singh,Rakesh Kumar,Preethi Pal,B,Harvinder Singh,Harvinder Singh won India’s first-ever Paralympic gold in archery in the men’s individual recurve open at Paris 2024. Sheetal Devi won bronze in the mixed compound team event there.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20580,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,Which city hosted the Meeting of the BRICS Ministers of Foreign Affairs on 4 June 2018?,"Pretoria, South Africa","Brasilia, Brazil","Beijing, China","New Delhi, India",A,"Pretoria, South Africa","The BRICS Ministers of Foreign Affairs met in Pretoria, South Africa, on 4 June 2018, when South Africa held the BRICS chair ahead of the Johannesburg summit.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20581,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,Which of the following best describes the theme of the book 'Hot Stage'?,A collection of modern Indian plays on social issues,A historical account of India’s independence movement,A novel about ancient Indian mythology,A travelogue about the Himalayas,A,A collection of modern Indian plays on social issues,"SSC’s key describes Hot Stage as a collection of modern Indian plays on social issues. Note: the book published under this title is Anita Nair’s Hot Stage (2023-24), a crime novel in her Inspector Gowda series that deals with social themes. None of the options describes it accurately, so the question is arguable; we keep SSC’s answer.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20582,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Chemistry,English,Which of the following is not typically considered a weather element?,Temperature,Humidity,Soil pH,Wind,C,Soil pH,"Weather elements are atmospheric conditions such as temperature, humidity, pressure, wind, cloud and rainfall. Soil pH is a property of soil, not of the atmosphere.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20583,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Which of the following about the 61st National Chess Championship is/are correct? 1.) GM Karthik Venkataraman won in Gurgaon and got ₹6 lakh. 2.) IM Neelash Saha finished 2nd but lost due to a tiebreak game vs Ganguly.,Only 1,Only 2,Both 1 and 2 are correct,Neither 1 nor 2 is correct,A,Only 1,"Statement 1 is correct: GM Karthik Venkataraman won the 61st National Chess Championship at Gurugram (August 2024) and got ₹6 lakh. Statement 2 is wrong: Karthik, Surya Shekhar Ganguly and Neelash Saha all scored 9/11; on Buchholz tie-break Ganguly was 2nd and Saha 3rd, with no tiebreak game played (AICF; FIDE).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20584,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,"What was launched on Electrical Safety Day 2025 by MoS Power and New & Renewable Energy, Shri Shripad Naik?",National Fire Safety Code,Suraksha Shakti safety mascot,Smart Meter Adoption Program,Digital Grid Optimization Tool,B,Suraksha Shakti safety mascot,"On Electrical Safety Day, 26 June 2025, MoS for Power and New & Renewable Energy Shripad Naik launched the safety mascot Suraksha Shakti and released an Electrical Safety Handbook (PIB, 28 June 2025).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20585,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Geography,English,Read the following Assertion (A) and Reason (R) carefully and choose the correct option: Assertion (A): The Chotanagpur Plateau is considered an eastern extension of the Central Highlands. Reason (R): The Chotanagpur Plateau is drained primarily by the Chambal and Betwa rivers.,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A","A is true, but R is false","A is false, but R is true",C,"A is true, but R is false",A is true: NCERT describes the Chotanagpur plateau as the further eastward extension of the Central Highlands. R is false: the Chotanagpur plateau is drained mainly by the Damodar; the Chambal and Betwa drain the Malwa and Bundelkhand region.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20586,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,In which year is the first module of the Bharatiya Antariksh Station (BAS) scheduled for launch?,2028,2030,2035,2040,A,2028,"ISRO plans to launch the first module of the Bharatiya Antariksh Station (BAS-1) in 2028, with the full station by 2035.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20587,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Chemistry,English,Which statement best reflects the role of non-metallic minerals in India?,India lacks enough reserves for industrial use.,"Mostly used as gems, with minimal industrial use.",India has rich reserves vital for major industries.,Only metallic minerals drive industrial growth.,C,India has rich reserves vital for major industries.,"India has large reserves of non-metallic minerals such as limestone, mica, gypsum and dolomite. They are vital for cement, electrical, fertiliser and steel industries.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20588,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,A Proclamation of National Emergency must be approved by each House within how many months?,1,3,6,9,A,1,"Under Article 352, as amended by the 44th Amendment (1978), a proclamation of National Emergency must be approved by both Houses of Parliament within one month.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20589,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Indian Economy,English,"Read the following statements marked as Assertion (A) and Reason (R). Choose the correct option: Assertion (A): The Polar Satellite Launch Vehicle (PSLV) is widely recognized as the workhorse launch vehicle of ISRO. Reason (R): PSLV is highly versatile, capable of launching a diverse range of payloads into various Earth orbits (including Earth Observation, small Geosynchronous, and Navigation satellites), and boasts an exceptionally high mission success rate across its different variants.","Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A","A is true, but R is false","A is false, but R is true",A,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","PSLV is called ISRO’s workhorse because it is versatile (polar, sun-synchronous, GTO and other orbits, e.g. IRNSS, Chandrayaan-1, Mars Orbiter Mission) and has a long record of successful launches. That versatility and reliability are the reason, so R explains A.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20590,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Which of the following is true regarding the Anglo-Indian representation in State Assemblies?,The Governor still nominates one Anglo-Indian member to the Assembly.,The provision was abolished by the 42nd Constitutional Amendment.,The provision was abolished by the 104th Constitutional Amendment.,Anglo-Indian members are elected through proportional representation.,C,The provision was abolished by the 104th Constitutional Amendment.,"Nomination of Anglo-Indians to the Lok Sabha (Art. 331) and to State Assemblies (Art. 333) was ended by the 104th Constitutional Amendment Act, 2019, with effect from January 2020.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20591,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Which of the following changes has Bharatiya Nagarik suraksha Samhita(BNSS) brought to criminal procedure?,Replaced all IPC sections,Video-recorded confessions,Presumption of guilt,Scrapping of all bail rights,B,Video-recorded confessions,"The BNSS allows statements and confessions to be recorded by audio-video electronic means (Section 183) and requires videography of searches and seizures. Of the options, video-recorded confessions is the real change; the BNSS did not replace IPC sections (that was the BNS), presume guilt or scrap bail.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20592,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,Which scheme supports financial services through postmen?,NSAP,IPPB,PMJAY,PRAGATI,B,IPPB,"India Post Payments Bank (IPPB), owned by the Department of Posts, provides banking and financial services at the doorstep through postmen and Gramin Dak Sevaks.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20593,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,Fill in the Blank: Kalbelia dance represents the movement of _____.,Camels,Snakes,Birds,Horses,B,Snakes,"Kalbelia is a folk dance of Rajasthan’s Kalbelia snake-charmer community. Its swirling movements imitate a serpent, and it is on UNESCO’s intangible heritage list.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20594,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,"According to the IMD World Competitiveness Ranking 2025, which dimension does the country Switzerland hold 1st position in for both 2024 and 2025?",Business Efficiency,Infrastructure,Economic Performance,Employment,B,Infrastructure,"In the IMD World Competitiveness Ranking 2025, Switzerland was 1st overall and kept 1st place in both Government Efficiency and Infrastructure from 2024. Of the options, only Infrastructure fits (IMD booklet 2025).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20595,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Biology,English,The 'Mangrove Cell' initiative in 2025 is primarily linked to which Indian state?,Odisha,Andhra Pradesh,Maharashtra,West Bengal,C,Maharashtra,The Mangrove Cell is a dedicated unit of the Maharashtra Forest Department (set up in 2012) for protecting and restoring the state’s mangroves.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20596,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,History,English,Read the following statements carefully and choose the correct option: Assertion (A): Iron and steel is considered a heavy industry. Reason (R): It requires lightweight raw materials like cotton and rubber.,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A","A is true, but R is false","A is false, but R is true",C,"A is true, but R is false","A is true: iron and steel is a heavy industry. R is false: it uses heavy, bulky raw materials such as iron ore, coking coal and limestone, not cotton and rubber.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20597,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Indian Economy,English,Consider the following statements about the MISHTI Scheme: 1. It aims at mangrove plantation using scientific methods. 2. It was announced under Budget 2023-24. 3. It includes commercial leasing of mangrove forests.,Only 1 and 2 are correct,Only 2 and 3 are correct,Only 1 and 3 are correct,"All 1, 2 and 3 are correct",A,Only 1 and 2 are correct,"MISHTI (Mangrove Initiative for Shoreline Habitats and Tangible Incomes) was announced in the Union Budget 2023-24 to plant mangroves along the coast using scientific methods, so 1 and 2 are correct. It does not involve commercial leasing of mangrove forests.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20598,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Awareness,Indian Polity & Constitution,English,"Article 370, which granted special status to Jammu and Kashmir, was abrogated by which constitutional mechanism?",Presidential Order under Article 370(3),Amendment by Parliament under Article 368,Ordinance by the President,Order under Article 356,A,Presidential Order under Article 370(3),"In August 2019 the President issued orders under Article 370 (C.O. 272 and the declaration under Article 370(3)), after which Article 370’s special provisions stopped applying. The Supreme Court upheld this in December 2023.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20599,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,"Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series. AEI, EIM, IMQ, MQU, ?",QUY,QKS,LMX,KJS,A,QUY,"Every letter moves 4 places forward: A→E→I→M→Q, E→I→M→Q→U, I→M→Q→U→Y. So MQU is followed by QUY.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20600,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,"Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series. ACE, EIM, IOU, MUC, ?",QSA,UHG,QAK,CGD,C,QAK,"1st letters: A, E, I, M, Q (+4). 2nd letters: C, I, O, U, A (+6, wrapping after Z). 3rd letters: E, M, U, C, K (+8, wrapping). Next term: QAK.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20601,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"What comes next: 12, 30, 56, 90, 132, ?",182,250,190,293,A,182,"Each term is n(n + 1) for odd n: 3×4 = 12, 5×6 = 30, 7×8 = 56, 9×10 = 90, 11×12 = 132, so next is 13×14 = 182. (Differences 18, 26, 34, 42, 50 rise by 8.)",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20602,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"What will be come at the place of question mark? 1, 2, 5, 26, 677, ?",458330,456976,453625,458329,A,458330,"Each term is the square of the previous term plus 1: 1² + 1 = 2, 2² + 1 = 5, 5² + 1 = 26, 26² + 1 = 677. Next: 677² + 1 = 458329 + 1 = 458330.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20603,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"Find the number that fits: 2, 5, 10, 17, ?",26,24,21,20,A,26,"The terms are n² + 1: 1 + 1 = 2, 4 + 1 = 5, 9 + 1 = 10, 16 + 1 = 17, so next is 25 + 1 = 26. (Differences 3, 5, 7, 9.)",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20604,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Instruction: Identify the assumptions that must hold for the statement to be valid, then choose the correct option. Statement: While the world is moving towards automation, it is essential to ensure that ethical frameworks evolve alongside technological advancements to prevent misuse. Assumptions: I. Automation can lead to ethical dilemmas. II. Ethical frameworks must be updated to keep pace with technological advancements. III. Automation will eventually replace human labor in all sectors.",Only I and II are implicit,Only I and III are implicit,All are implicit,Only I is implicit,A,Only I and II are implicit,"Saying ethics must keep pace to prevent misuse assumes automation can raise ethical problems (I) and that ethical frameworks need updating as technology advances (II). The statement says nothing about automation replacing human labour in every sector, so III is not implicit.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20605,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,The position of how many letters will remain unchanged if each of the letters in the word DEVELOP is arranged in alphabetical order?,Two,Four,Three,Five,A,Two,"DEVELOP in alphabetical order is D E E L O P V. Comparing with D E V E L O P position by position, only D (1st) and E (2nd) stay in place. Answer: two.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20606,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Identify the similar address: No. 45, First Avenue, Raja Annamalaipuram, Chennai, Tamil Nadu – 600028","No. 45, 1st Avenue, R.A. Puram, Chennai, TN 600028","No. 45, First Avenue, Raja Annamalaipuram, Chennai, Tamil Nadu – 600028","45, First Avenue, Raja Annamalai Puram, Chennai, Tamil Nadu – 600028","No. 45/1, First Avenue, R. Annamalaipuram, Chennai, Tamil Nadu – 600028",B,"No. 45, First Avenue, Raja Annamalaipuram, Chennai, Tamil Nadu – 600028","Option 2 matches the given address character for character. The others change the wording: 1st Avenue / R.A. Puram / TN, a missing No. and a split Raja Annamalai Puram, or No. 45/1 and R. Annamalaipuram.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20607,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"From the given options, find the word which cannot be formed using the letters of the given word: INTELLIGENCE",CANCEL,NEGLECT,GENTLE,INCITE,A,CANCEL,"INTELLIGENCE has the letters I, N, T, E, L, G and C but no A, so CANCEL cannot be formed. NEGLECT, GENTLE and INCITE can be made from its letters.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20608,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"Eight persons A, B, C, D, E, F, G, and H are sitting around a circle facing the center. C is second to the right of A. E is opposite C. F is to the immediate left of E. B is to the immediate right of A. G is to the immediate left of D. Who is sitting to the right of D?",H,U,B,F,D,F,"Place A anywhere. B is to A’s immediate right and C second to A’s right, so B sits between A and C. E sits opposite C, and F is to E’s immediate left. Of the three seats left, G must be to D’s immediate left, which fixes D, G and then H. The person to D’s right is F. (Option 2 reads U on SSC’s sheet; there is no person U.)",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20609,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,"In each of the following questions, a specific alphabetic coding pattern has been applied to the first word to form the second word. Identify the same coding logic and apply it to the third word to determine the correct answer from the given options. COUNTRY : FRXQWUB :: EXAMINE : ?",HAPDLQH,HADPLQH,HAHPLDQ,GBQDVWB,B,HADPLQH,"Each letter moves 3 places forward: C→F, O→R, U→X, N→Q, T→W, R→U, Y→B. EXAMINE becomes E→H, X→A, A→D, M→P, I→L, N→Q, E→H = HADPLQH.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20610,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,"In each of the following questions, the second word is formed by rearranging the letters of the first word using a specific transformation, such as reversal or block shifting. Identify that transformation and apply it to the third word to choose the correct option. KITCAT : CATTIK :: PENTOP : ?",TOPPEN,TOPNEP,POPTEN,POPNET,B,TOPNEP,KITCAT splits into KIT + CAT. The result CATTIK is the second half (CAT) followed by the first half reversed (TIK). For PENTOP: TOP + reversed PEN (NEP) = TOPNEP.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20611,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"In each of the following questions, a group of three numbers/symbols is given in each option. Identify the group that does NOT follow the same pattern as the others.",Z1# : Y2@ : X3＄,W4% : V5^ : U6&,T7* : S8( : R9),Q10_ : P9@ : O8＄,D,Q10_ : P9@ : O8＄,"In the first three groups the letter goes back one step and the number goes up one step each time (Z1, Y2, X3; W4, V5, U6; T7, S8, R9), and the numbers run on from group to group. In Q10_ : P9@ : O8＄ the numbers fall (10, 9, 8), so it is the odd one.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20612,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Coding & Decoding,English,"Instruction: In a certain coding system: ‘dream focus build skill’ is coded as ‘trq, xnz, hmd, clv’ ‘focus logic dream’ is coded as ‘trq, jkp, xnz’ ‘trust logic build dream’ is coded as ‘xnj, clv, jkp, trq’ Question: What is the code for ‘build skill logic trust’?","clv, hmd, jkp, xnj","clv, xnj, jkp, trq","hmd, xnz, jkp, xnj","hmd, clv, xnj, xnz",A,"clv, hmd, jkp, xnj","dream appears in all three sentences and trq in all three codes, so dream = trq. focus is in sentences 1 and 2, so it is xnz (the other common code). logic is in 2 and 3, so it is jkp; build is in 1 and 3, so it is clv. Then skill = hmd and trust = xnj. build skill logic trust = clv, hmd, jkp, xnj.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20613,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Mathematical Operations,English,"If x+2y=14 and x−y=5, find x.",6,4,8,10,C,8,"Subtract the second equation from the first: (x + 2y) − (x − y) = 14 − 5, so 3y = 9 and y = 3. Then x = 5 + 3 = 8.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20614,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"If 6 ＄ 2 = 20 and 4 ＄ 3 = 19, then 5 ＄ 2 = ?",18,17,16,15,B,17,a ＄ b = ab + a + b: 6×2 + 6 + 2 = 20 and 4×3 + 4 + 3 = 19. So 5 ＄ 2 = 10 + 5 + 2 = 17.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20615,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Coding & Decoding,English,"If ‘SAVE’ is coded as ‘★3#5’, and ‘VASE’ as ‘#3★5’, then what is the code for ‘EVAS’?",5★3#,★5#7,★5#3,5#3★,D,5#3★,"From SAVE = ★3#5: S = ★, A = 3, V = #, E = 5 (VASE = #3★5 confirms it). EVAS = 5 # 3 ★ = 5#3★.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20616,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"If the ratio of two numbers is 3:5 and their sum is 64, find the numbers","24, 40","20, 44","18, 46","16, 48",A,"24, 40","Let the numbers be 3x and 5x. Then 8x = 64, so x = 8 and the numbers are 24 and 40.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20617,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"If 5 @ 3 = 28 and 4 @ 2 = 18, then what is 6 @ 4?",40,52,64,76,A,40,a @ b = a² + b: 5² + 3 = 28 and 4² + 2 = 18. So 6 @ 4 = 36 + 4 = 40.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20618,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"Pointing to a girl, a man said, “She is the daughter of my mother’s only son.” How is the girl related to the man?",Daughter,Niece,Sister,Cousin,A,Daughter,The only son of the man’s mother is the man himself. So the girl is the man’s daughter.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20619,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"If P is the maternal uncle of Q, how is Q related to P’s sister?",Niece/Nephew,Cousin,Son,Cannot be determined,A,Niece/Nephew,"P is Q’s maternal uncle, so P is the brother of Q’s mother. SSC’s key treats P’s sister as another sister of P, whose niece or nephew Q is. Note: if the sister meant is Q’s own mother, Q would be her son or daughter. The question does not say which sister, so the key is arguable; we keep SSC’s answer.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20620,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Mathematical Operations,English,"After interchanging + & × and 3 & 9, which of the following equations will hold true?",(3+5)×9=48,(9+2)×3=10,(3+7)×9=60,(9+1)×3=15,A,(3+5)×9=48,"Swap + with × and 3 with 9 in each option. (a) (3+5)×9 becomes (9×5)+3 = 45 + 3 = 48, which is true. (b) gives (3×2)+9 = 15, not 10. (c) gives (9×7)+3 = 66, not 60. (d) gives (3×1)+9 = 12, not 15.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20621,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"If a % b = 37, where a % b = a + 2b, what is the value of a and b?","25,5","27, 5","16, 10","27, 10",B,"27, 5","Check a + 2b = 37: 25 + 10 = 35, 27 + 10 = 37 for (27, 5), 16 + 20 = 36, 27 + 20 = 47. Only a = 27, b = 5 works.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20622,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Mathematical Operations,English,"If + = ×, − = +, × = ÷; then 10 + 2 − 4 × 2 = ?",10,19,22,24,C,22,Replace the signs: 10 × 2 + 4 ÷ 2. Doing × and ÷ first: 20 + 2 = 22.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20623,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"In a tournament of 7 players, each player plays every other player once. How many matches are there?",21,42,36,28,A,21,"Each pair of players meets once, so the number of matches is 7C2 = 7 × 6/2 = 21.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20624,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"If 60% of A = 0.3 of B =1/6 of C, find A: B: C.",5 : 10 : 18,18 : 10 : 5,6 : 3 : 10,10 : 5 : 18,A,5 : 10 : 18,"Let 0.6A = 0.3B = C/6 = k. Then A = 5k/3, B = 10k/3, C = 6k. Multiplying by 3/k: A : B : C = 5 : 10 : 18.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20625,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,A car travels 0.875 km in 1 minute. How far does it travel in 1 hour 45 minutes?,91.875 km,94.576 km,95.444 km,92.582 km,A,91.875 km,1 hour 45 minutes = 105 minutes. Distance = 0.875 × 105 = 91.875 km.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20626,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,Simplify: (1/(7 + √2)) + (1/(7 − √2)) − (14/(49 − 2)),0,1,2,√2,A,0,1/(7 + √2) + 1/(7 − √2) = (7 − √2 + 7 + √2)/(49 − 2) = 14/47. Subtracting 14/47 leaves 0.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20627,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"The expenditure of a household on food, clothing, and entertainment is in the ratio 2 : 4 : 4. In the coming year, the cost of food is expected to fall by 10%, clothing to rise by 5%, and entertainment to fall by 15%. What is the percent change (increase or decrease) in the total household expenditure?",5% decrease,6% increase,6% decrease,5% increase,C,6% decrease,"Take spending as 2, 4 and 4 (total 10). New spending: food 2 × 0.9 = 1.8, clothing 4 × 1.05 = 4.2, entertainment 4 × 0.85 = 3.4, total 9.4. Change = −0.6/10 = 6% decrease.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20628,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A and B invested ₹1,20,000 and ₹1,60,000 respectively. A remained for 10 months and B for 7 months. What is the total profit if B's share is ₹16,800?","₹34,800","₹34,000","₹10,000","₹10,500",A,"₹34,800","Profit ratio = 1,20,000 × 10 : 1,60,000 × 7 = 12,00,000 : 11,20,000 = 15 : 14. B’s 14 parts = ₹16,800, so 1 part = ₹1,200 and total profit = 29 × 1,200 = ₹34,800.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20629,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,"Two individuals, A and B, have rented a field. A places 21 horses in the field for 6 months and 15 cows for 2 months. B adds 15 cows for 6 months and 40 sheep for 7.5 months. If 3 horses consume the same amount of food as 5 cows, and 6 cows eat as much as 10 sheep, what portion of the rent should A cover?",8/17,19/17,16/17,20/17,A,8/17,"Convert to cow-months (3 horses = 5 cows, so 1 horse = 5/3 cow; 6 cows = 10 sheep, so 1 sheep = 0.6 cow). A: 21 × 6 × 5/3 + 15 × 2 = 210 + 30 = 240. B: 15 × 6 + 40 × 7.5 × 0.6 = 90 + 180 = 270. A’s share = 240/510 = 8/17.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20630,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Ratio & Proportion,English,"Two individuals, A and B rent a pasture. A uses 16 cows for a duration of 3 months and 20 sheep for 4 months and B uses 30 sheep for 6 months. If 4 cows are equivalent to 8 sheep, determine A's portion of the rent.",44/89,54/89,64/89,74/89,A,44/89,"4 cows = 8 sheep, so 1 cow = 2 sheep. In sheep-months, A: 16 × 3 × 2 + 20 × 4 = 96 + 80 = 176; B: 30 × 6 = 180. A’s share = 176/356 = 44/89.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20631,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"Three groups of students have average ages 18, 20, and 22 respectively. If the number of students in the three groups is in the ratio 2:3:5, what is the overall average age?",19.6,20.6,15.6,14.6,B,20.6,Weighted average = (18 × 2 + 20 × 3 + 22 × 5)/(2 + 3 + 5) = (36 + 60 + 110)/10 = 20.6.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20632,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Average & Statistics,English,"The average of 11 numbers is 68. If the average of the first five is 63 and the average of the last five is 72, find the 6th number.",73,74,75,76,A,73,"Sum of 11 numbers = 11 × 68 = 748. First five = 5 × 63 = 315, last five = 5 × 72 = 360. 6th number = 748 − 315 − 360 = 73.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20633,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Simple & Compound Interest,English,What is the average of all integers between 300 and 450 that are exactly divisible by 13?,277,377,477,577,B,377,Multiples of 13 between 300 and 450 run from 312 (13 × 24) to 442 (13 × 34). Their average is (312 + 442)/2 = 377.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20634,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,Evaluate: 12½% of 560 km + 66⅔% of 240 km,140 km,230 km,320 km,450 km,B,230 km,12½% of 560 = 1/8 × 560 = 70 km and 66⅔% of 240 = 2/3 × 240 = 160 km. Total = 230 km.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20635,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"A vendor sells shirts at ₹500 each, earning a 2% commission, and ties at ₹150 each, with a 12% commission. If he sells 3 shirts and 4 ties per day, what will be his total commission earned in 30 days?",₹2850,₹3000,₹3060,₹3200,C,₹3060,"Daily commission: shirts 3 × 500 × 2% = ₹30; ties 4 × 150 × 12% = ₹72. Total ₹102 a day, so 30 days = ₹3,060.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20636,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,A fruit seller sells apples at a loss of 5% on the cost price but uses a weight that is 20% less than the actual weight. Find his total profit percentage.,20.62%,19.25%,16.28%,18.75%,D,18.75%,"Let 1 kg cost ₹1. He gives 0.8 kg (cost ₹0.80) but charges the price of 1 kg at a 5% loss, ₹0.95. Profit = 0.15/0.80 × 100 = 18.75%.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20637,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,The profit made on an item sold for ₹2200 is equal to the loss incurred when it is sold for ₹1800. What will be the profit or loss percentage if the item is sold for ₹2050?,Profit of 2.25%,Loss of 3.5%,Profit of 2.5%,Loss of 4.25%,C,Profit of 2.5%,"Equal profit and loss means CP is midway: (2200 + 1800)/2 = ₹2,000. At ₹2,050 the profit is 50/2000 = 2.5%.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20638,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A mobile phone retailer sells a phone for ₹P and earns a profit of 20%. For a special festive offer, he marks the same phone at ₹1.5P. At the offer, he provides a discount of 10%. What will be the percentage profit that he will make during the festive offer?",26%,56%,62%,60%,C,62%,CP = P/1.2. Festive price = 1.5P × 0.9 = 1.35P. Profit % = (1.35P ÷ P/1.2 − 1) × 100 = (1.62 − 1) × 100 = 62%.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20639,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A shopkeeper marked an item 25% above its cost price. During a sale, he offered a discount of 10%. What was his profit percentage?",10%,12.50%,15%,17.5%,B,12.50%,"On CP 100, MP = 125 and SP = 125 × 0.9 = 112.5. Profit = 12.5%.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20640,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A shopkeeper marks his goods at 60% above the cost price. He allows a discount of 25% on the marked price. If he also gives an additional cash discount of ₹150, and still makes a profit of 14% on the cost price, what is the cost price of the goods?",₹2000,₹2500,₹3000,₹3500,B,₹2500,"Let CP = x. SP = 1.6x × 0.75 − 150 = 1.2x − 150, which equals 1.14x. So 0.06x = 150 and x = ₹2,500.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20641,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,How many approximate kgs of sugar costing ₹45 per kg must be mixed with 25 kg of sugar costing ₹32 per kg so that a 15% gain may be obtained by selling the mixture at ₹43.70 per kg?,15 kg,25 kg,21 kg,18 kg,C,21 kg,"Cost of the mixture = 43.70/1.15 = ₹38 per kg. Let x kg at ₹45 be mixed: 45x + 32 × 25 = 38(x + 25), so 7x = 150 and x ≈ 21.4 kg ≈ 21 kg. (By alligation the ratio is (38 − 32) : (45 − 38) = 6 : 7.)",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20642,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,A right circular cone has a radius of 7 cm and height of 24 cm. What is the slant height?,25 cm,30 cm,35 cm,40 cm,A,25 cm,Slant height l = √(r² + h²) = √(49 + 576) = √625 = 25 cm.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20643,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A lent Rs. 5000 to B for a duration of 2 years and Rs. 3000 to C for a period of 4 years both at the same simple interest rate. In total, he received Rs. 2200 as interest from both borrowers. What is the rate of interest per annum?",10%,12%,15%,17%,A,10%,"SI = P × R × T/100. 5000 × 2 × R/100 + 3000 × 4 × R/100 = 220R = 2200, so R = 10% per annum.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20644,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,"A triangular prism has base area of 25 cm². If height is increased by 20%, what is the new volume (original height was 10 cm)?",250 cm³,275 cm³,300 cm³,225 cm³,C,300 cm³,"Volume of a prism = base area × height. New height = 10 × 1.2 = 12 cm, so volume = 25 × 12 = 300 cm³.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20645,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,A circular disc's radius is decreased by 10%. What is the percentage decrease in its area?,10%,19%,18%,15%,B,19%,"Area is proportional to r². New area = 0.9² = 0.81 of the old, a decrease of 19%.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20646,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A builder has 100 m of fencing wire. He can use this wire to enclose a circular garden or a square garden. If he wants to maximize the enclosed area, what is the approximate ratio of the area of the largest possible circular garden to the area of the largest possible square garden, using the entire 100 m of wire?",1:1,1.27:1,1.57:1,2:1,B,1.27:1,"Circle: 2πr = 100, so area = 100²/(4π) ≈ 795.8 m². Square: side 25 m, area 625 m². Ratio ≈ 795.8 : 625 ≈ 1.27 : 1 (exactly 4/π).",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20647,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,"A vertical cylindrical container is filled with oil. A solid hemispherical stone of radius 7 cm is immersed completely, and the oil level rises by 3 cm. What is the radius of the cylinder?",6.29 cm,7.43 cm,8.73 cm,11.41 cm,C,8.73 cm,The rise in oil equals the hemisphere’s volume: πR² × 3 = (2/3)π × 7³. So R² = 2 × 343/9 ≈ 76.2 and R ≈ 8.73 cm.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20648,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-12,Shift 3,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,A sector of a circle has a central angle of 120° and a radius of 7 cm. Another sector of the same circle has a central angle of 2π/3 radians. What is the ratio of the area of the first sector to the area of the second sector?,3:5,2:3,1:1,4:5,C,1:1,"120° = 2π/3 radians, so both sectors of the same circle have the same angle and the same area. Ratio = 1 : 1.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-12 Shift 3),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-12-september-shift-3/
