SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20670,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Direct & Indirect Speech,English,"A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech. Ravi said, “I like this pen.”",Ravi said he liked that pen.,Ravi said he like that pen.,Ravi said he liked this pen.,Ravi said he likes that pen.,A,Ravi said he liked that pen.,Said → past tense: “like” becomes “liked” and “this” becomes “that”. “Ravi said he liked that pen.”,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20671,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Direct & Indirect Speech,English,"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech. The judge said that justice must be served at any cost.","“Justice should be served at any cost,” said the judge.","“Justice must be served at any cost,” the judge said.","“We serve justice at any cost,” said the judge.","“One must serve justice,” the judge said.",B,"“Justice must be served at any cost,” the judge said.","In direct speech the judge's words are given as spoken: “Justice must be served at any cost,” the judge said.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20672,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,English Comprehension,Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles),English,"Rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph: 1. The rapid spread of misinformation and disinformation on social media platforms represents a major challenge to public discourse. 2. This method involves a systematic verification of facts, claims, and sources to provide a credible assessment of accuracy. 3. This phenomenon can erode public trust in news sources and undermine informed decision-making in a democratic society. 4. As a result, professional fact-checking organizations have emerged as a critical line of defense against the proliferation of false narratives.","2, 1, 4, 3","3, 1, 2, 4","1, 3, 4, 2","1, 4, 2, 3",C,"1, 3, 4, 2","Sentence 1 names the problem (misinformation) and 3 gives its effect. Sentence 4 brings in fact-checkers as the response, and 2 explains their method: 1, 3, 4, 2.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20673,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,History,English,Arrange the following sites in chronological order based on the stylistic development of Buddhist sculpture: a) Mathura b) Bharhut c) Sanchi Stupa–1,b-c-a,c-a-b,c-b-a,a-c-b,A,b-c-a,"Bharhut (c. 2nd century BCE) comes first. The gateways of Sanchi Stupa-1 (1st century BCE) come next, and Mathura sculpture (1st-3rd century CE) comes last: b-c-a.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20674,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,Which of the following statements about the Chithirai Festival of Madurai is correct?,The Chithirai Festival is celebrated in the tamil month of Margazhi,Lord Kallazhagar arrives on a golden horse,The festival is held exclusively in December,The festival ends with a game of bullfight,B,Lord Kallazhagar arrives on a golden horse,"At Madurai's Chithirai festival (April-May), Lord Kallazhagar comes to the Vaigai river on a golden horse. It is held in the Tamil month of Chithirai, not Margazhi or December.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20675,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,History,English,What is the term for a structured musical composition in Hindustani classical music?,Kriti,Bandish,Gamaka,Rasa,B,Bandish,In Hindustani music a bandish is a fixed composition set to a raga and tala. Kriti is the Carnatic term.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20676,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Consider the following statements regarding belt ranks and competition area in Judo: 1) A red-and-white belt is associated with judokas from Sixth dan to Eighth dan levels. 2) A shared safety zone of at least 1 meter must be maintained between adjoining competition areas. Which of the above statements is/are correct?,Only 1 is Correct,Only 2 is Correct,1 and 2 both are correct,Neither 1 nor 2 is Correct,A,Only 1 is Correct,"Statement 1 is true: 6th to 8th dan wear the red-and-white belt. Statement 2 is false: IJF rules require a shared safety area of at least 4 m between adjoining competition areas, not 1 m.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20677,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,"Who broke the 30-year-old Asian Games men’s 5,000m meet record in National Open Athletics Championships 2024?",Bahadur Singh,Gulveer Singh,Neeraj Chopra,Hima Das,B,Gulveer Singh,"At the 63rd National Open Athletics Championships (Bengaluru, August 2024), Asian Games medallist Gulveer Singh won the 5000 m in 13:54.70, breaking Bahadur Singh's 1994 meet record of 13:54.72. Note: the stem's “Asian Games” wording is loose. It was the National Open meet record.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20678,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,Chemistry,English,"Consider the following statements regarding BRICS Science, Technology and Innovation (STI) cooperation: 1) It is based on mutual benefit and public-good-driven innovation. 2) It is governed only through annual Heads of State Summits. Which of the statements is/are correct?",Only 1 is correct,Only 2 is correct,Both 1 and 2 are correct,Neither 1 nor 2 is correct,A,Only 1 is correct,"BRICS STI cooperation is based on mutual benefit and innovation for the public good. It is run through ministerial meetings and working groups, not only through annual summits, so only statement 1 is correct.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20679,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,"Fill in the blank: The inaugural Khelo India Para Games took place in _____, showcasing seven sporting disciplines across three venues in New Delhi.",March 2024,January 2023,December 2023,March 2025,C,December 2023,The first Khelo India Para Games were held in New Delhi on 10-17 December 2023: seven sports across three venues.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20680,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Read the below statements marked as Assertion (A) and Reason (R). Mark the correct options: Assertion (A): Last Man in Tower explores the moral and ethical conflicts faced by residents during rapid urban development and real estate pressures in Mumbai. Reason (R): The novel focuses on the historical evolution of Mumbai’s architecture and its colonial past.,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A.","Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A.","A is true, but R is false.","A is false, but R is true.",C,"A is true, but R is false.","Aravind Adiga's Last Man in Tower is about a Mumbai housing society under pressure from a builder. The assertion is true. The novel is not about the history of Mumbai's architecture, so the reason is false.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20681,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Choose the correctly matched cave feature and its formation:,Stalactite – Grows upward from cave floor,Stalagmite – Formed by dripping water from cave ceiling,Pillar – Hangs from the cave roof,Stalactite – Formed by upward mineral flow,B,Stalagmite – Formed by dripping water from cave ceiling,"Stalactites hang from the cave roof. Stalagmites rise from the floor, built up by mineral-rich water dripping from the ceiling. Option B is the only correct pairing.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20682,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,What is the primary function of the NVS-02 satellite launched aboard GSLV-F15?,It supports meteorological observations for cyclone prediction.,It enables satellite-based television broadcasting.,It boosts India's navigation system by offering precise position and timing data.,It conducts deep-space communication with planetary probes.,C,It boosts India's navigation system by offering precise position and timing data.,"NVS-02, launched on GSLV-F15 (ISRO's 100th launch from Sriharikota, January 2025), is a NavIC navigation satellite that provides position and timing data.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20683,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are given below. Choose the correct option: Assertion (A): Population growth can be measured in absolute numbers and percentage change per year. Reason (R): Measuring growth only in absolute numbers provides detailed insights into population trends over time.,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A","A is true, but R is false","A is false, but R is true",C,"A is true, but R is false","Population growth can be measured in absolute numbers and as a yearly percentage, so A is true. Absolute numbers alone do not give a full picture, which is why rates are used, so R is false.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20684,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,Indian Polity & Constitution,English,"Read the following statements regarding K. Sanjay Murthy's recent appointment as Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) of India: 1. He took office as the CAG in November 2024 after the term of Girish Chandra Murmu. 2. The CAG is a constitutional office, which is appointed by the President under Article 148 of the Indian Constitution. 3. The CAG's term is only five years and cannot be repeated. Which of the above is/are correct?",1 and 2 only,2 and 3 only,1 and 3 only,"1, 2 and 3 all are correct",A,1 and 2 only,"K. Sanjay Murthy became CAG in November 2024, succeeding Girish Chandra Murmu (1 is true). The CAG is appointed by the President under Article 148 (2 is true). The term is 6 years or until age 65, not 5 years (3 is false).",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20685,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,What is the primary function of the Golgi apparatus?,ATP production,Protein modification,Lipid synthesis,DNA replication,B,Protein modification,"The Golgi apparatus modifies, sorts and packages proteins (and lipids) for transport. ATP is made in mitochondria.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20686,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,Indian Polity & Constitution,English,"As per Article 279A of the Indian Constitution, the GST Council’s decisions require what kind of majority of the weighted votes of the members present and voting?",Simple majority,Three-fourths majority,Two-thirds majority,Half majority,B,Three-fourths majority,Article 279A(9): GST Council decisions need a three-fourths majority of the weighted votes of members present and voting.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20687,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,Indian Polity & Constitution,English,Which of the following correctly reflects the legal implication of Article 255 regarding presidential or governor’s assent to bills?,State law is void without written Governor assent.,Mention of assent is mandatory for validity.,Omission of prior recommendation doesn't invalidate law if assent is given.,President’s assent must precede legislative passage to be valid.,C,Omission of prior recommendation doesn't invalidate law if assent is given.,"Article 255: if the required assent is given, a law is not invalid merely because a prior recommendation or sanction was not obtained.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20688,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,Physics,English,"When light enters from air into a medium, its speed changes. Which of the following properties of light remains constant during this transition?",Wavelength,Frequency,Speed,Amplitude,B,Frequency,"When light passes into another medium, its speed and wavelength change but its frequency stays the same.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20689,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,The Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam(BSA) aims to align Indian evidence law with advancements in:,Forensic science and digital technology,Traditional agricultural practices,Ancient philosophical texts,Oral storytelling traditions,A,Forensic science and digital technology,"The Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023 replaced the Indian Evidence Act and recognises electronic and digital records and forensic evidence.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20690,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,Read the below statements marked as Assertion (A) and Reason (R). Mark the correct options: Assertion (A): Rashtriya Vigyan Puraskar is a civilian science award. Reason (R): It is conferred by Ministry of Culture.,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A","A is true, but R is false","A is false, but R is true",C,"A is true, but R is false","The Rashtriya Vigyan Puraskar is a national civilian award for science, so A is true. It is given by the Ministry of Science and Technology, not the Ministry of Culture, so R is false.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
