SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20692,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,Thang-Ta is a traditional martial dance associated with which northeastern state of India?,Assam,Nagaland,Manipur,Tripura,C,Manipur,"Thang-Ta, the “sword and spear” martial art, comes from Manipur.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20693,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,History,English,Which of the following industry pairs is correctly grouped as heavy industries?,Sewing machines and Paint brushes,Shipbuilding and Automobile,Electric bulbs and Fuse wires,Watches and Paint brushes,B,Shipbuilding and Automobile,"Shipbuilding and automobiles need heavy raw materials and large capital, so they are heavy industries. Sewing machines, bulbs and watches are light industries.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20694,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,Indian Polity & Constitution,English,"The President is elected by an electoral college, while the Governor is _____.",Directly elected,Appointed by the President,Nominated by Supreme Court,Chosen by State Assembly,B,Appointed by the President,The President is elected by an electoral college (Article 54). The Governor is appointed by the President (Article 155).,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20695,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,"The Western Ghats are a recognized biodiversity hotspot. Which of the following is currently considered the most significant threat to its endemic species, beyond general habitat loss?","Infrastructure development projects (e.g., roads, dams, mining).",Introduction of invasive alien species.,Forest fires due to climate change.,Human-wildlife conflict due to encroachment.,B,Introduction of invasive alien species.,"SSC keyed invasive alien species. Assessments of the Western Ghats do list invasive plants (such as Lantana and Acacia) as a major threat to endemic species. Infrastructure is also widely cited, but it is a form of habitat loss, which the question sets aside. The key is arguable, and the answer is kept as SSC keyed it.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20696,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,Indian Economy,English,NISAR’s orbit regime is?,GTO,GEO,Polar sun-sync,LEEO,C,Polar sun-sync,"NISAR (NASA-ISRO, launched July 2025 on GSLV-F16) flies in a sun-synchronous polar orbit at about 747 km.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20697,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Awareness,Indian Polity & Constitution,English,Consider the following statements: 1. The Governor can dissolve the State Legislative Assembly. 2. The President has no such power regarding the Lok Sabha. Which of the above is/are correct?,Only 1,Only 2,Both 1 and 2,Neither 1 nor 2,A,Only 1,"The Governor can dissolve the State Assembly (Article 174), so 1 is true. The President can dissolve the Lok Sabha (Article 85), so 2 is false.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20698,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,"In the following question, select the related word from the given alternatives. Architect : Design :: Chef : ?",Cook,Serve,Recipe,Food,D,Food,"An architect produces a design. A chef produces food. “Cook” is the chef's action and “recipe” is a plan, but the product, as with design, is food.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20699,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,"In the following question, select the related word from the given alternatives Utilitarianism : Consequence :: Deontology : ?",Virtue,Duty,Intention,Value,B,Duty,"Utilitarianism judges an act by its consequences. Deontology judges it by duty, i.e. whether the act follows a moral rule.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20700,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Select the letters from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series. K, M, O, ? , S, U, ? , Y","Q, X","Q, W","P, W","R, W",B,"Q, W","The letters skip one each time: K, M, O, Q, S, U, W, Y. The blanks are Q and W.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20701,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,"Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series. PQR, STU, VWX, ?",YZD,YVA,YZA,DFR,C,YZA,"Each group is three consecutive letters continuing from the last: PQR, STU, VWX, then YZA (wrapping from Z to A).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20702,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,"Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series. YMW , VJT , SGQ , PDN, ?",TYD,HGF,MJH,MAK,D,MAK,"Each letter moves back 3 every time: Y→V→S→P→M, M→J→G→D→A, W→T→Q→N→K. Next: MAK.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20703,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,"Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series: RBEH, RGOW, RLYL, RQIA, ?",RVSP,RVSH,RVHS,RSVP,A,RVSP,"The first letter stays R. The second letter moves +5 (B, G, L, Q, V), the third +10 (E, O, Y, I, S) and the fourth +15 (H, W, L, A, P). Next: RVSP.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20704,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,"Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series: C D E F, C K S A, C R G V, C Y U Q, ?",C E H K,C F H K,C F H L,C F I L,D,C F I L,"The first letter stays C. Second letters go +7 (D, K, R, Y, F), third +14 (E, S, G, U, I) and fourth −5 (F, A, V, Q, L). Next: C F I L.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20705,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"Complete the pattern: 120, 96, 76.8, 61.44, ?",60.27,78.91,47.89,49.152,D,49.152,Each term is 0.8 times the one before: 61.44 × 0.8 = 49.152.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20706,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,Each of the letters in the word CONTRAST is arranged in alphabetical order. How many letters are there in the English alphabetical series between the letter that is first from the left and the one that is fifth from the right in the new letter-cluster formed?,10,13,15,11,B,13,CONTRAST in alphabetical order: A C N O R S T T. First from the left is A. Fifth from the right is O (the 4th letter). Between A (1) and O (15) the alphabet has 13 letters.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20707,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Which of the following addresses are identical to each other: 1. S. Iyer 17-D, Coral Residency, Thiruvananthapuram , 695014 2. S. Iyer 17-D, Coral Residency, Thiruvananthapuram , 695014 3. S. Iyer 17-D Coral Residency, Thiruvananthapuram , 695014 4. S. Iyer 17-D Coral Residency, Thiruvananthapuram , 695013",1 and 2,1 and 3,2 and 4,3 and 4,A,1 and 2,"Addresses 1 and 2 match exactly. Address 3 has no comma after 17-D, and address 4 also has a different PIN (695013).",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20708,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Which of the following is/are identical to the address given: Sunil Kumar 21/4, Ashok Vihar, Delhi, 110052 1. Sunil Kumar 21/4, Ashok Vihar, Delhi, 1100522 2. Sunil Kumar 21/4, Ashok Vihar, Delhi, 110052 3. Sunil Kumar 21/4, Ashok Vihar, New Delhi, 110052 4. Sunil Kumar 21/4, Ashok Vihar, Delhi, 110053",1 Only,3 Only,2 Only,4 Only,C,2 Only,"Only address 2 matches. Address 1 has an extra digit in the PIN, 3 says New Delhi, and 4 has PIN 110053.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20709,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,Find the best option that best completes the analogy. CAB : EDF :: GIH : ?,JKL,KJI,ILL,JLI,C,ILL,"CAB → EDF is +2, +3, +4 (C→E, A→D, B→F). GIH: G+2 = I, I+3 = L, H+4 = L, giving ILL.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20710,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,Find the option that best completes the analogy. DP : XZ :: EN : ?,YZ,YB,ZB,YX,D,YX,"D → X is −6 (or +20) and P → Z is +10. For EN: E − 6 = Y and N + 10 = X, giving YX.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20711,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"Ten persons are sitting in two parallel rows containing five persons each, such that there is an equal distance between adjacent persons. Line 1: Five men (A-E) are seated and all of them are facing South. Line 2: Five women (M-Q) are seated and all of them are facing North. Based on the arrangement, answer the question: D is opposite to M. M is at one of the extreme ends of Line 2. O is at the center position of Line 2. Who is second to the right of M in Line 2 (facing North)?",O,M,A,N,A,O,"Line 2 faces North, so each woman's right is East. O is in the middle (3rd seat) and M is at one end. For anyone to be second to M's right, M must be at the West end (seat 1). Second to her right is seat 3, which is O.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20712,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,"In each of the following questions, a specific rearrangement pattern is applied to the first word to form the second. Identify the same pattern and apply it to the third word to determine the correct answer from the given alternatives. AROUND : RAUODN :: GROUND : ?",RGUODN,NDOOGR,OUNDGR,DNUURG,A,RGUODN,"AROUND → RAUODN swaps each pair of letters: AR→RA, OU→UO, ND→DN. GROUND: GR→RG, OU→UO, ND→DN, giving RGUODN.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20713,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,"In each of the following questions, the second group of letters is formed from the first using a specific alphabetical transformation. Apply the same pattern to the third group and find the correct option that completes the analogy. QDXM : SFYN :: UIOZ : ?",PAQM,LPWA,QNLA,WKPA,D,WKPA,"QDXM → SFYN is +2, +2, +1, +1. UIOZ: U+2 = W, I+2 = K, O+1 = P, Z+1 = A, giving WKPA.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20714,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Classification (Odd One Out),English,Choose the odd one:,"2, 4, 8","3, 9, 27","5, 25, 125","4, 16, 36",D,"4, 16, 36","Each group is a number, its square and its cube: 2, 4, 8; 3, 9, 27; 5, 25, 125. The group 4, 16, 36 breaks this, since 4³ = 64.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20715,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"In each of the following questions, a group of three numbers/symbols is given in each option. Identify the group that does NOT follow the same pattern as the others.",M13 : J10 : G7,Z26 : W23 : T20,D4 : A1 : X24,H8 : E6 : B4,D,H8 : E6 : B4,"The letter and number match (M13, J10, G7) and each step is −3. Option C wraps round the alphabet (A1 → X24). In H8 : E6 : B4, E is 5, not 6, so this group breaks the pattern.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20716,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"In each of the following questions, a group of three numbers/symbols is given in each option. Identify the group that does NOT follow the same pattern as the others.",Z1＄ : Y2# : X3@,W4% : V5^ : U6&,T7* : S8( : R9],Q10＄ : P11＄ : O12＄,D,Q10＄ : P11＄ : O12＄,"Each group has three different symbols with letters falling and numbers rising (Z1＄ : Y2# : X3@). In Q10＄ : P11＄ : O12＄ the same symbol repeats, so it is the odd one.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20717,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,B is the daughter of A. C is the husband of B. D is the son of C. How is A related to D?,Father,Grandfather,Grandmother,Cannot be determined,D,Cannot be determined,"B is A's daughter, C is B's husband and D is their son. A is D's grandparent, but A's gender is not given, so we cannot tell grandfather from grandmother.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20718,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Mathematical Operations,English,"If 'X' means '+', 'Y' means '−', 'Z' means '×', and 'W' means '÷' what is the value of the following expression? 15 W 3 X 2 Y 4=?",1,3,5,7,B,3,Replace the letters: 15 ÷ 3 + 2 − 4 = 5 + 2 − 4 = 3.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20719,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,A’s father’s wife’s only daughter is B. How is A related to B?,Nephew,Cousin,Sibling,Uncle,C,Sibling,"A's father's wife is A's mother, and her only daughter is B. So A and B are children of the same parents: A is B's sibling.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20720,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"Introducing a boy, a girl says, “He is the son of my mother’s only son.” Who is the boy to the girl?",Brother,Son,Nephew,Cousin,C,Nephew,The girl's mother's only son is the girl's brother. His son is her nephew.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20721,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,A is the wife of B. B is the brother of C. C is the father of D. How is A related to D?,Aunt,Mother,Sister-in-law,Grandmother,A,Aunt,"C is D's father and B is C's brother, so B is D's uncle. B's wife A is D's aunt.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20722,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Mathematical Operations,English,"If '+' means '−', '−' means '+', '×' means '÷', then 50 + 10 − 5 × 5 = ?",41,60,65,70,A,41,After swapping signs: 50 − 10 + 5 ÷ 5 = 50 − 10 + 1 = 41.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20723,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,What is the value of 4 + 44 + 444 + 4444 + 44444?,49380,42300,41300,45000,A,49380,4 + 44 + 444 + 4444 + 44444 = 49380.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20724,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,Simplify:(1 2/5 + 2.6) − 1 3/4,2.25,2.1,2.35,2.5,A,2.25,1⅖ = 1.4. (1.4 + 2.6) − 1.75 = 4 − 1.75 = 2.25.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20725,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Simple & Compound Interest,English,Evaluate the expression: 1/(3 − √8) − 1/(√8 − √7) + 1/(√7 − √6) − 1/(√6 − √5) + 1/(√5 − 2) = ?,5,3,2,0,A,5,"Rationalise each term: 1/(3 − √8) = 3 + √8, 1/(√8 − √7) = √8 + √7, and so on. With the alternating signs everything cancels except 3 + 2 = 5.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20726,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,Determine the ratio of the number of students who play Football to the number of students who play Basketball in a survey of 120 students from the following table: Category | Number Play Football and Basketball | 25 Play Football but not Basketball | 45 Play Basketball but not Football | 35 Play neither sport | 15,6:7,7:5,7:6,5:7,C,7:6,Football = 25 + 45 = 70. Basketball = 25 + 35 = 60. Ratio 70 : 60 = 7 : 6.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20727,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"Tina and Meera started a business with ₹1,00,000 and ₹80,000 respectively. After 6 months, Meera added ₹40,000 more. Tina withdrew ₹20,000 at the same time. What is the profit-sharing ratio at the end of 1 year?",9:10,5:6,7:4,2:3,A,9:10,"Tina: 1,00,000 × 6 + 80,000 × 6 = 10,80,000. Meera: 80,000 × 6 + 1,20,000 × 6 = 12,00,000. Ratio 108 : 120 = 9 : 10.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20728,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A invests ₹20,000, while B invests ₹30,000. A receives an additional 20% for management. The total profit is ₹60,000. What is A's share?","₹51,200","₹41,200","₹31,200","₹21,200",C,"₹31,200","A's management share = 20% of 60,000 = 12,000. The other 48,000 is split 2 : 3, so A gets 19,200 more. Total = ₹31,200.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20729,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Average & Statistics,English,"A batsman's average score for a certain number of innings is 44. If he scores 132 runs in the next innings, his average becomes 48. How many innings did he play earlier?",21,22,23,24,A,21,"44n + 132 = 48(n + 1), so 4n = 84 and n = 21.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20730,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"The average of 13 numbers is 70. The average of the first five numbers is 60. The average of the next five numbers is 25 % higher than the average of the first five numbers. The 11th number is 6 less than the 13th number, and the 12th number is 4 greater than the 13th number. What is the average of the 11th and 12th numbers?",78,77,76,74,A,78,"Total = 910. First five = 300; next five average 75, sum 375. The last three add to 235. If the 13th is t: (t − 6) + (t + 4) + t = 235, so t = 79. The 11th is 73 and the 12th is 83, average 78.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20731,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,"In an election, 80% of eligible voters cast their votes. Of these votes, 5% were declared invalid. If a winning candidate received 11,400 votes, which accounted for 60% of the total valid votes, what was the total number of eligible voters enrolled in that election?","20,000","22,500","25,000","27,500",C,"25,000","Valid votes = 0.8 × 0.95 × V and 60% of them is 11,400. So 0.456V = 11,400 and V = 25,000.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20732,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"The compound interest on a sum at 18 % p.a. for 1 ½ years, compounded yearly, is ₹2 862. Find the principal.","₹10,000",₹8 000,"₹2,000","₹4,000",A,"₹10,000","Compounded yearly for 1½ years: P × 1.18 × 1.09 = 1.2862P. CI = 0.2862P = 2862, so P = ₹10,000.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20733,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"If the compound interest on a certain sum at 16⅔% per annum for 3 years is ₹1270, find the simple interest on the same sum at the same rate and for the same period.",₹1080,₹1000,₹1500,₹2000,A,₹1080,"At 16⅔% (= 1/6), CI for 3 years = P[(7/6)³ − 1] = 127P/216 = 1270, so P = 2160. SI = 2160 × (1/6) × 3 = ₹1080.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20734,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A tea seller bought 15 kg of Darjeeling tea at ₹300 per kg and 25 kg of Assam tea at ₹240 per kg. He mixed them together. Due to a slight drop in market prices, he had to sell the entire mixture at ₹260 per kg. Calculate his total profit or loss.",Loss of ₹100,Profit of ₹100,Profit of ₹200,Profit of ₹200 (repeated on the official sheet),A,Loss of ₹100,"Cost = 15 × 300 + 25 × 240 = 4,500 + 6,000 = ₹10,500. Sale = 40 × 260 = ₹10,400. So there is a loss of ₹100 (option A, as per SSC's answer key). Note: on SSC's official sheet options C and D are both printed as 'Profit of ₹200'; option D is labelled as a repeat here so the two can be told apart.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20735,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"An antique dealer sold three items, A, B, and C, with their selling prices in the ratio 4:5:6. He suffered a loss of 10% on item A, made a profit of 50% on item B, and broke even (no profit, no loss) on item C. What was his approximate percentage gain or loss in the overall deal?",loss of 8.88%,profit of 8.88%,profit of 10.88%,loss of 10.88%,B,profit of 8.88%,"Take SPs as 4, 5, 6. CPs = 4/0.9 = 4.444, 5/1.5 = 3.333 and 6. Total CP = 13.778, SP = 15, profit ≈ 8.87%, about 8.88%.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20736,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Ratio & Proportion,English,"A 75-liter mixture contains milk and water in the ratio 3:2. If 15 liters of this mixture are removed and replaced with 10 liters of pure milk, what is the new ratio of milk to water in the mixture?",11:7,23:12,17:11,19:12,B,23:12,"Milk 45, water 30. Removing 15 L takes out 9 milk and 6 water, leaving 36 : 24. Adding 10 milk gives 46 : 24 = 23 : 12.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20737,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A wholesaler buys a batch of ceiling fans at a 50% markup over the factory's base cost ₹C. He then allows a 20% trade discount to the retailer. The retailer applies a 40% markup on his cost and offers a flat 10% discount to customers on the printed price. If a customer finally pays ₹18,144, what is the original base cost (₹C) of one ceiling fan from the factory?","₹12,000","₹11,500","₹10,800","₹10,000",A,"₹12,000","Wholesaler price = 1.5C × 0.8 = 1.2C. Customer pays 1.2C × 1.4 × 0.9 = 1.512C = 18,144, so C = ₹12,000.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20738,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A can lay railway track between two specified stations in 16 days, while B can complete the same task in 12 days. When C assists them, they manage to finish the job in just 4 days. How long would it take for C to complete the job on their own?",8 1/2 days,9 1/2 days,9 3/5 days,10 days,C,9 3/5 days,C's rate = 1/4 − 1/16 − 1/12 = (12 − 3 − 4)/48 = 5/48. C alone takes 48/5 = 9⅗ days.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20739,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"Three varieties of rice costing ₹40/kg, ₹50/kg, and a third unknown price are mixed in the ratio 2:3:5. If the resulting mixture is sold at ₹55/kg, making a profit of 10% on the cost price, what is the price of the third variety of rice per kg?",₹52.50,₹57.50,₹54.00,₹62.50,C,₹54.00,"Cost price = 55/1.1 = 50. (2 × 40 + 3 × 50 + 5x)/10 = 50, so 230 + 5x = 500 and x = ₹54.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20740,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,"Time, Work & Pipes",English,A can build up a wall in 8 days while B can break it in 3 days. A has worked for 4 days and then B joined to work with A for another 2 days only. In how many days will A alone build up the remaining part of the wall?,7 1/3 days,8 2/5 days,9 1/5 days,5 1/2 days,A,7 1/3 days,"A alone for 4 days builds 1/2. For 2 days together the net rate is 1/8 − 1/3 = −5/24, so 5/12 is pulled down and 1/12 is left. The remaining 11/12 at 1/8 a day takes 22/3 = 7⅓ days.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20741,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"An airplane travels a specific distance at a speed of 240 km/h over the course of 5 hours. To cover the same distance in just 1 hour, it needs to fly at a speed of:",1200 km/h,1500 km/h,1400 km/h,1600 km/h,A,1200 km/h,Distance = 240 × 5 = 1200 km. To do it in 1 hour needs 1200 km/h.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20742,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A person travels from city A to city B. If he travels at a speed of 50 km/h, he arrives 1 hour early. If he travels at a speed of 30 km/h, he arrives 1 hour late. What is the distance (in km) between city A and city B?",150 km,120 km,200 km,180 km,A,150 km,"The time difference between the two speeds is 2 hours: d/30 − d/50 = 2, so d = 150 km.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20743,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Geometry,English,A ring-shaped metallic sheet has outer and inner radii 10 cm and 6 cm. What percentage of the full circle's area is the ring?,36%,48%,64%,76%,C,64%,Ring area/circle area = (10² − 6²)/10² = 64/100 = 64%.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20744,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,"A circular pond is surrounded by a path 2 m wide. If the total area (pond + path) is 616 m² and the pond area is 452.16 m², what is the radius of the pond?",10 m,11 m,12 m,13 m,C,12 m,"Pond area 452.16 = 3.14 × r², so r² = 144 and r = 12 m. (Pond + path radius 14 m gives 616 m² with π = 22/7.)",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20745,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,"The ratio of the circumferences of two circular flower beds is 3:5. If the smaller flower bed has a radius of 9 m, what is the radius of the larger flower bed?",15 m,17 m,19 m,21m,A,15 m,"Circumferences are in the same ratio as the radii: 3 : 5 = 9 : r, so r = 15 m.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20746,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,"What is the equation of line through (0,3) with slope −1?",y = −x + 3,y = x − 3,y = −x − 3,y = x + 3,A,y = −x + 3,y = mx + c with m = −1 and c = 3 gives y = −x + 3.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20747,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-13,Shift 2,Quantitative Aptitude,Algebra,English,"Given, x + 1/x = 5, then determine the value of x² + 1/x².",25,24,26,23,D,23,x² + 1/x² = (x + 1/x)² − 2 = 25 − 2 = 23.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-13 Shift 2),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-13-september-shift-2/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20748,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Synonyms,English,Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: JUVENILE,Adult,Wise,Childish,Mature,C,Childish,"Juvenile means young or childish. Adult, wise and mature are opposites.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20749,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Idioms & Phrases,English,Choose the correct meaning of idiom: Bury the hatchet,To reconcile after a conflict,To deepen hostility,To run away,To forget someone's name,A,To reconcile after a conflict,“Bury the hatchet” means to make peace after a quarrel.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20750,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Antonyms,English,Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. Extirpate,Exterminate,Establish,Uproot,Eradicate,B,Establish,Extirpate means to root out completely. Its opposite is establish.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20751,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Spelling Correction,English,Identify the misspelt word,Embarrassment,Indispensible,Camouflage,Rendezvous,B,Indispensible,The correct spelling is “Indispensable”.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20752,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Spelling Correction,English,Spot the correct spelling of early film base compound.,Nitrocelulose,Nitrocellulose,Nitracellulose,Nitrocellullose,B,Nitrocellulose,"Nitrocellulose, used for early film stock, is the correct spelling.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20753,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,One Word Substitution,English,Choose the correct one-word substitute for: 'A person who eats excessively or greedily'.,Glutton,Gourmet,Epicure,Sybarite,A,Glutton,"A glutton eats excessively or greedily. A gourmet or epicure enjoys fine food, and a sybarite loves luxury.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20754,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,"Select the correct option: The finance minister’s statement was laden with caveats, none of ___ were explained.",that,them,which,whom,C,which,After “none of” the relative pronoun for things is “which”: “none of which were explained”.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20755,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Select the correct option: The philosopher’s stance was diametrically ___ to the prevailing orthodoxy.,adverse,averse,converse,opposed,D,opposed,“Diametrically opposed to” is the standard phrase for complete opposition.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20756,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Select the correct option: No sooner ___ the findings published than critics began questioning their legitimacy.,was,had,were,have,C,were,"After “No sooner” the auxiliary comes before the subject. The sentence needs a passive, “No sooner were the findings published than…” (“had the findings been published” would also work, but “been” is not in the sentence). Note: SSC's official key marks (B) “had”, which gives the ungrammatical “had the findings published”. Option (C) “were” is marked correct here.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20757,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Error Spotting,English,Find the part of the sentence that contains an error: The policy aims to neither penalise first-time offenders (1)/ nor those who may have violated norms (2)/ due to systemic ambiguity (3)/ rather than deliberate intent. (4),(1),(2),(3),(4),A,(1),“Neither … nor” must sit just before the parallel items: “aims to penalise neither first-time offenders nor those who…”. Part (1) places “neither” wrongly.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20758,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Error Spotting,English,"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error: It was not merely the fragmentation of administrative jurisdictions across sectors (1)/ that disrupted cohesive governance, but the inertia embedded in overlapping regulatory mandates (2)/ which, though designed to safeguard institutional autonomy, (3)/ ends up paralyzing inter-departmental responsiveness altogether. (4)",(1),(2),(3),(4),D,(4),"“Which” refers to the plural “overlapping regulatory mandates”, designed to safeguard autonomy, so the verb should be “end up”, not “ends up”.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20759,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Change the following from active to passive: The committee had been debating complex amendments when the bell rang.,Complex amendments had had been been debated by the committee when the bell rang.,Complex amendments had been being debated by the committee when the bell rang.,Complex amendments had be being debated by the committee when the bell rang.,Complex amendments had debated by the committee when the bell rang.,B,Complex amendments had been being debated by the committee when the bell rang.,Past perfect continuous active (had been debating) becomes the passive “had been being debated”.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20760,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word: The knight raised his ‘pauldron’ before mounting. (Highlighted word shown in quotes.),The blacksmith polished the steel pauldron until it gleamed.,The art historian admired the engraved pauldron of the effigy.,The biology student dissected the pauldron of the sea slug.,The museum displayed a 15th-century Italian pauldron.,C,The biology student dissected the pauldron of the sea slug.,"SSC keyed C. “Pauldron” means only shoulder armour, so no option has a true homonym. Option C (“pauldron of the sea slug”) is the only sentence where it cannot mean armour, which is how the key reads it. Arguable question. The answer is kept as SSC keyed it.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20761,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Active & Passive Voice,English,Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure: A letter is written to the editor by the citizen every week.,The editor writes a letter to the citizen every week.,The citizen writes a letter to the editor every week.,The editor wrote a letter every week.,The citizen has been writing letters to the editor weekly.,B,The citizen writes a letter to the editor every week.,Present passive “is written … by the citizen” becomes the active “The citizen writes a letter to the editor every week.”,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
