SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20765,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,What recent trend is encouraging in India's Olympic profile?,Reduced investment in cricket,Domination in hockey again,Emergence of multiple sports and women athletes,Decline of Western dominance,C,Emergence of multiple sports and women athletes,The heartening trend is the “diversification of sports” and the “rising representation and success of Indian women athletes”.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20766,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,What is implied about India’s Olympic aspirations?,They rely entirely on foreign coaching,They aim for consistent participation,They are growing but need sustained reforms,They are limited to traditional sports,C,They are growing but need sustained reforms,"The passage says India's Olympic identity is “still evolving” and that going from potential to podium needs long-term investment: growing, but in need of sustained reforms.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20767,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence: Had I known about the traffic, I ‘will leave early’. (Highlighted part shown in quotes.)",would have left earlier,would leave early,had left earlier,would left earlier,A,would have left earlier,A third conditional (“Had I known…”) takes “would have + past participle” in the main clause: “I would have left earlier”.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20768,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,English Grammar & Vocabulary,English,Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence: It is high time you ‘must change your habits’. (Highlighted part shown in quotes.),changed your habits,must have changed your habits,change your habit,will change the habit,A,changed your habits,“It is high time” is followed by the past tense: “It is high time you changed your habits.”,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20769,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Direct & Indirect Speech,English,"A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech. He said, “Do it right now.”",He said do it immediately.,He told to do it now.,He told me to do it at once.,He told me do it right now.,C,He told me to do it at once.,"An order is reported with “told + object + to-infinitive”, and “right now” becomes “at once”: “He told me to do it at once.”",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20770,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Direct & Indirect Speech,English,"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech. The professor remarked that students needed to submit their papers before Friday.","“Students need to submit their papers before Friday,” the professor remarked.","“Students needed to submit their papers before Friday,” said the professor.","“Submit your papers before Friday,” the professor instructed.","“You were to submit your papers before Friday,” said the professor.",A,"“Students need to submit their papers before Friday,” the professor remarked.","In direct speech the tense shifts back: “needed” becomes “need”. “Students need to submit their papers before Friday,” the professor remarked.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20771,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles),English,"Rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph: 1. This makes them ideal for tasks like image recognition, natural language processing, and medical diagnostics. 2. Machine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence that focuses on the creation of algorithms that can learn from data without explicit programming. 3. The algorithm improves its performance by analyzing vast amounts of input data and identifying underlying patterns. 4. Instead of being given a set of rules, a machine learning model is trained on examples.","2, 4, 3, 1","4, 3, 2, 1","3, 4, 2, 1","2, 3, 4, 1",A,"2, 4, 3, 1","Sentence 2 defines machine learning, 4 says it learns from examples, 3 says it improves by finding patterns and 1 gives the resulting uses: 2, 4, 3, 1.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-EN-EN-20772,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,English Comprehension,Sentence Rearrangement (Para Jumbles),English,"Rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph: 1. The primary purpose of this process is to ensure that the food we eat is safe and does not contain harmful bacteria or other contaminants. 2. Food processing is a series of methods used to transform raw ingredients into consumable products. 3. These methods can range from simple actions like cutting and grinding to more complex procedures such as pasteurization and fermentation. 4. Furthermore, it also helps to preserve food, extend its shelf life, and enhance its nutritional value.","2, 3, 1, 4","1, 2, 3, 4","3, 1, 4, 2","4, 2, 1, 3",A,"2, 3, 1, 4","Sentence 2 defines food processing, 3 gives its range of methods, 1 its main purpose (safety) and 4 its further benefits: 2, 3, 1, 4.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20773,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,Indian Polity & Constitution,English,"Read the below statement: 1. Solicitor General of India is appointed by the president of India. 2. A candidate contesting for the post of the President of India is required to make a security deposit of ₹15,000. Which of the above statements is/are correct?",Only statement 1,Only statement 2,Both statements 1 and 2,Neither statement 1 nor 2,B,Only statement 2,"The Solicitor General is a statutory law officer appointed by the Appointments Committee of the Cabinet. Only the Attorney General is appointed by the President (Article 76), so 1 is false. A presidential candidate must deposit ₹15,000, so 2 is true.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20774,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,Chemistry,English,Based on the given statements which option is correct: Statement I: Mathura art produced images for both Indian and non-Indian patrons. Statement II: Mathura art ignored nature-based themes in its sculptures.,Statement I and II both are Correct.,Only statement I is correct,Only Statement II is correct,Neither I nor II,B,Only statement I is correct,"The Mathura school made Buddhist, Jain and Brahmanical images, and under the Kushanas it served both Indian and foreign patrons (I is true). It often used nature motifs such as trees, yakshis and animals (II is false).",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20775,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,Which of the following statements about Hola Mohalla festival of Punjab is correct?,It is celebrated mainly by women through crafts and songs in Patiala.,"It showcases martial arts, langars, and Nihang mock battles at Anandpur Sahib.",It is a harvest festival observed in Punjab just before Diwali.,Hola Mohalla is celebrated on the same day as Holi.,B,"It showcases martial arts, langars, and Nihang mock battles at Anandpur Sahib.","Hola Mohalla, begun by Guru Gobind Singh, is held at Anandpur Sahib the day after Holi. It features martial displays, mock battles by Nihangs and langars.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20776,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,History,English,Mārgi Saṅgīta in ancient Indian music was rooted in:,Folk music,Vedic traditions,Courtly entertainment,Western-influence,B,Vedic traditions,"Margi sangita was the “classical” music rooted in Vedic chant and sacred ritual, as opposed to desi (regional) music.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20777,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,"In freestyle wrestling, which of the following actions can result in a technical point for the wrestler?",Running out of the mat deliberately,Holding the opponent’s singlet,Performing a successful takedown,Using an illegal headlock,C,Performing a successful takedown,"In freestyle wrestling a successful takedown earns technical points. Deliberately running out of the mat, grabbing the singlet and illegal holds are fouls.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20778,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,Vijender Singh defeated which player in the quarter-finals to secure India’s first Olympic boxing medal?,Emilio Correa,Carlos Góngora,Misha Aloyan,Vasyl Lomachenko,B,Carlos Góngora,"At Beijing 2008, Vijender Singh beat Ecuador's Carlos Góngora in the 75 kg quarter-final, which assured India's first Olympic boxing medal (bronze).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20779,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,Which mechanism did India operationalize in 2024 to strengthen regional financial resilience within SAARC?,SAARC Development Fund capital increase,SAARC Currency Swap Framework (2024–27),SAARC Trade Insurance Scheme,SAARC Sovereign Credit Pool,B,SAARC Currency Swap Framework (2024–27),"In June 2024 the RBI, with Government approval, put in place the SAARC Currency Swap Framework for 2024-27, offering swap support to SAARC central banks.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20780,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,"Fill in the blanks: Established in 1961 within the former Palace of the Maharaja of Patiala, the National Institute of Sports was later renamed as the Netaji Subhas National Institute of Sports (NSNIS) on _______.",15th August 1975,26th January 1972,23rd January 1973,7th May 1961,C,23rd January 1973,The National Institute of Sports (founded 7 May 1961 in Patiala's Moti Bagh palace) was renamed the Netaji Subhas National Institute of Sports on 23 January 1973.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20781,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Consider the following statements about “The Vine of Desire” by Chitra Banerjee Divakaruni: 1) Explores cultural conflicts in an Indian immigrant family across generations. 2) A historical account of India’s freedom struggle and politics. 3) A science fiction tale about identity and technology in future India. Which of the following is correct?,Only statement 1 is correct,Only statement 2 is correct,Statements 2 and 3 both are correct,"1, 2 and 3 all are correct",A,Only statement 1 is correct,"The Vine of Desire follows Anju and Sudha, Indian women in America, and the cultural strains of immigrant family life. It is neither a freedom-struggle history nor science fiction, so only statement 1 fits.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20782,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Which statements accurately describe water bodies in the Indian Desert? 1. Streams are perennial and flow year-round. 2. Most streams disappear into the sand.,Only 1,Only 2,1 and 2 both are correct,Neither 1 nor 2 are correct,B,Only 2,Streams in the Thar Desert are seasonal and most vanish into the sand (the Luni is the main exception). Only statement 2 is correct.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20783,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,General Knowledge,English,Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are given below. Choose the correct option: Assertion (A): Demographic statistics like birth and death rates rely on accurate reporting by households. Reason (R): Birth and death registration is mandatory and always accurately followed in all parts of India.,"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation","A is true, but R is false","A is false, but R is true",C,"A is true, but R is false","Birth and death rates depend on accurate reporting, so A is true. Registration is not always accurately followed everywhere in India, so R is false.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20784,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,"Art, Culture & Static GK",English,Which Padma awardees and fields is/are correctly paired? 1. Gokul Chandra Das – Folk Music 2. Dinesh Saini – Environment 3. Farooq Ahmad Mir – Literature 4. Geeta Devi – Agriculture,1 only,2 only,3 only,4 only,A,1 only,"Gokul Chandra Das, a dhak (folk drum) player from West Bengal, received the Padma Shri 2025 in Art: folk music fits. Farooq Ahmad Mir was awarded in Art (Kashmiri shawl weaving), not Literature, and the other two pairings do not match any 2025 awardee.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20785,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,Current Affairs & Schemes,English,"Which of the following accurately reflects the critical technological outcome of ISRO’s RLV-LEX3 mission conducted on June 23, 2024?",In-flight fuel transfer at hypersonic speeds,Autonomous high-speed landing under tough cross-range & wind,Launch abort test for crewed reusable launchers,Orbital deployment via dual-mode scramjet propulsion,B,Autonomous high-speed landing under tough cross-range & wind,"RLV-LEX-03 (23 June 2024, Chitradurga) showed autonomous landing of the Pushpak winged vehicle from a harder release point, with more cross-range and stronger winds, at landing speeds above 320 km/h.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
