SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GA-EN-20787,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Awareness,Indian Polity & Constitution,English,How are Money Bills handled in both Houses of Parliament and State Legislatures with bicameralism under the Constitution?,Rajya Sabha must approve Money Bills within 14 days,"In States, the Legislative Council can amend a Money Bill within 14 days",Both Rajya Sabha and Legislative Councils have equal powers on Money Bills,Rajya Sabha and Legislative Councils can only make recommendations within 14 days,D,Rajya Sabha and Legislative Councils can only make recommendations within 14 days,"A Money Bill can be introduced only in the Lok Sabha (or the Legislative Assembly). The Rajya Sabha or Legislative Council can only make recommendations within 14 days, which the lower House may accept or reject.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
