SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20803,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,"Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series: TDGJ, TGMS, TJSB, TMYK, ?",TEFY,TESD,TESO,TPET,D,TPET,"The first letter stays T. The second letter moves +3 (D, G, J, M, P), the third +6 (G, M, S, Y, E) and the fourth +9 (J, S, B, K, T). Next: TPET.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20804,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,"Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series: D A F H, D D K O, D G P V, D J U C, ?",DMKA,DJSH,DMNS,DMZJ,D,DMZJ,"The first letter stays D. The second moves +3 (A, D, G, J, M), the third +5 (F, K, P, U, Z) and the fourth +7 (H, O, V, C, J). Next: DMZJ.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20805,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"What comes next: 3, 7, 16, 35, 74, ?",153,156,151,152,A,153,"Each term is double the previous one plus 1, 2, 3, 4, 5: 3×2+1 = 7, 7×2+2 = 16, 16×2+3 = 35, 35×2+4 = 74, 74×2+5 = 153.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20806,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,Each of the letters in the word FRIENDLY is arranged in alphabetical order. How many letters are there in the English alphabetical series between the letter that is third from the left and the one that is second from the right in the new letter-cluster formed?,2,4,13,11,D,11,FRIENDLY in alphabetical order: D E F I L N R Y. Third from the left is F (6) and second from the right is R (18). Between them the alphabet has 11 letters.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20807,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Which of the following addresses are identical to each other: 1. Amitabh S 112/44 Block-B, Indira Nagar, Lucknow, 226016 2. Amitabh S. 112/44 Block-B, Indira Nagar, Lucknow , 226016 3. Amitabh S. 112/44 Block-B, Indira Nagar, Lucknow , 226016 4. Amitabh S. 112/44 Block B, Indira Nagar, Lucknow , 226016",1 and 2,2 and 3,2 and 4,3 and 4,B,2 and 3,"Addresses 2 and 3 match exactly. Address 1 has “S” without a full stop, and address 4 has “Block B” without the hyphen.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20808,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"Which of the following addresses are identical to each other: 1. Dr Ruchi Jain 4/88, Skyline Residency, Jaipur, 302001 2. Dr. Ruchi Jain 4/88, Skyline Residency, Jaipur , 302001 3. Dr. Ruchi Jain 4/88, Skyline Residency, Jaipur , 302001 4. Dr Ruchi Jain 4/88, Skyline Residency, Jaipur , 302001",1 and 2,2 and 3,2 and 4,3 and 4,B,2 and 3,"Addresses 2 and 3 match exactly. Addresses 1 and 4 have “Dr” without a full stop, and 1 also has no space before the comma.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20809,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Alphabetical & Letter Series,English,Find the group of letters that best completes the analogy. Use alphabetical positions and reverse position logic where necessary. DINS : WRMH :: EKPT : ?,VJOG,VJNF,VPKG,VJOF,C,VPKG,"Each letter is replaced by its reverse-alphabet partner (position 27 − n): D↔W, I↔R, N↔M, S↔H. For EKPT: E↔V, K↔P, P↔K, T↔G, giving VPKG.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20810,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"In the following question, a pair of letters is given, followed by its corresponding product of alphabetical positions (A = 1, B = 2, ..., Z = 26). A second pair of letters is given without its product. Identify the correct product for the second pair that maintains the same relationship as the first. AxE : 1×5 :: DxK : ?",3×9,4×11,5×10,4×12,B,4×11,The pair is written as the product of its positions: A×E = 1×5. D×K = 4×11.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20811,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,There are 40 students in a line. Rahul is 13th from the left and Kunal is 17th from the right. How many students are there between them?,7,9,10,12,C,10,"Kunal is 17th from the right, i.e. 40 − 17 + 1 = 24th from the left. Between the 13th and the 24th there are 24 − 13 − 1 = 10 students.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20812,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,"In each of the following questions, a specific rearrangement pattern has been applied to the first word to form the second. Apply the same rearrangement to the third word and choose the correct answer from the given alternatives. PRINTING : RPNIITGN :: PROTOCOL : ?",RPTOCOOL,RPOTCOLO,PRTOOCOL,RPTOCOLO,D,RPTOCOLO,"PRINTING → RPNIITGN swaps each pair of letters: PR→RP, IN→NI, TI→IT, NG→GN. PROTOCOL: PR→RP, OT→TO, OC→CO, OL→LO, giving RPTOCOLO.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20813,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Analogy & Classification,English,"In each of the following questions, a word is transformed into another using a specific alphabetic pattern (such as letter shifting or substitution). Apply the same transformation to the third word to determine the correct answer from the given options. HOUSE : GNTRD :: ? : KHFGS",SIGHT,FIGHT,MIGHT,LIGHT,D,LIGHT,"HOUSE → GNTRD moves each letter back 1. Reversing this, KHFGS moves forward 1 to give LIGHT.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20814,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"A said to B, “Your father’s wife’s son is my brother.” How is B related to A?",Cousin,Sibling,Uncle,Nephew,B,Sibling,"B's father's wife is B's mother, and her son is B's brother, who is also A's brother. So A and B are siblings.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20815,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Number & Letter Series,English,"Find the missing number: 1, 4, 9, 16, ?, 36",20,25,30,27,B,25,"The squares 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36. The missing number is 25.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20816,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,Identify the number which does not satisfy: Sum of digits is a divisor of the number,21,30,36,39,D,39,"For 39 the digit sum is 12, and 39 is not divisible by 12. For 21 (3), 30 (3) and 36 (9) the digit sum divides the number.",Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20817,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"In each of the following questions, a group of three numbers/symbols is given in each option. Identify the group that does NOT follow the same pattern as the others.",A1 : D5 : G9,B2 : E6 : H10,C3 : F7 : I11,D4 : G8 : K13,D,D4 : G8 : K13,"In each group the letters move +3 and the numbers +4: A1 : D5 : G9, B2 : E6 : H10, C3 : F7 : I11. In D4 : G8 : K13, G→K is +4 and 8→13 is +5, so it is the odd one.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20818,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Logical Reasoning,English,"In each of the following questions, a group of three numbers/symbols is given in each option. Identify the group that does NOT follow the same pattern as the others.",A1@ : D4# : G7＄,B2% : E5^ : H8&,C3* : F6( : I9),D4_ : G8@ : K13＄,D,D4_ : G8@ : K13＄,"Elsewhere the letter matches its number and both move +3 (A1, D4, G7), with three different symbols. D4_ : G8@ : K13＄ breaks this (G is 7, not 8, and K13 is +5).",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20819,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,A said to B: “The woman I met yesterday at the park was the only daughter of the father of your brother.” How is the woman related to B?,Sister,Cousin,Mother,Aunt,A,Sister,"The father of B's brother is B's father, and his only daughter is B's sister.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20820,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"A man says, “My son’s mother is the only daughter of your father.” How is the man related to the person being spoken to?",Brother,Husband,Son-in-law,Son,B,Husband,"The only daughter of the listener's father is the listener's sister (or the listener herself). She is the mother of the man's son, so the man is her husband.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20821,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Blood Relations,English,"Introducing a man, Shruti said, “He is the husband of the granddaughter of the only son of my grandfather.” How is the man related to Shruti?",Son-in-law,Husband,Son,Cousin,A,Son-in-law,"The only son of Shruti's grandfather is Shruti's father. His granddaughter is Shruti's daughter, and her husband is Shruti's son-in-law.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-GI-EN-20822,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,General Intelligence & Reasoning,Mathematical Operations,English,"If + = ×, − = +, × = ÷; then 6 + 3 − 2 × 1 = ?",20,21,19,24,A,20,After replacing the signs: 6 × 3 + 2 ÷ 1 = 18 + 2 = 20.,Easy,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20823,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,Find the product: 1.2 × 2 2/5 × 3/4,2.4,2.5,2.16,2.1,C,2.16,1.2 × 2.4 × 0.75 = 2.16.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20824,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,What is the value of (0.1×0.1×0.1+0.03×0.03×0.03)/(0.3×0.3×0.3+0.09×0.09×0.09).,0.027,0.009,0.729,0.037,D,0.037,"Take a = 0.1, b = 0.03. The numerator is a³ + b³, and the denominator is (3a)³ + (3b)³ = 27(a³ + b³). The value is 1/27 ≈ 0.037.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20825,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,The number of students in two sections A and B having different heights is shown in the table given below: Height (in metres) | Section A | Section B 1.55 | 5 | 4 1.60 | 9 | 8 1.62 | 11 | 13 1.65 | 14 | 10 1.68 | 6 | 7 1.71 | 7 | 5 1.75 | 4 | 3 What is the ratio of the total number of students in Section A whose height is less than 1.65 metres to the total number of students in Section B whose height is less than 1.65 metres?,25:26,1:1,26:25,25:25,B,1:1,"Below 1.65 m: Section A = 5 + 9 + 11 = 25, Section B = 4 + 8 + 13 = 25, so the ratio is 1 : 1. Note: option D (25 : 25) is the same ratio unsimplified, so two options are equal in value. SSC keyed 1 : 1, its lowest-terms form, and the answer is kept as keyed.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20826,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A, B, and C invest ₹40,000, ₹60,000, and ₹80,000 respectively for 1 year. What is B’s share in a ₹55,000 profit?","₹18,333.33","₹20,333.33","₹21,333.33","₹22,333.33",A,"₹18,333.33","Ratio 40 : 60 : 80 = 2 : 3 : 4. B's share = 3/9 × 55,000 = ₹18,333.33.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20827,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A and B invest ₹60,000 and ₹90,000 respectively, in a business. After one year, the profit is distributed, including simple interest at 10% per annum on the capital. Total profit, including interest, is ₹25,000. What is A’s share?","₹7,000","₹10,500","₹10,000","₹8,500",C,"₹10,000","Interest at 10%: A 6,000, B 9,000, together 15,000. The remaining 10,000 is split 60 : 90 = 2 : 3, so A gets 4,000 more. A's total = ₹10,000.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20828,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Average & Statistics,English,Table – Units Sold of 3 Products Product | Jan | Feb | Mar A | 100 | 120 | 110 B | 90 | 85 | 95 C | 150 | 160 | 155 Q: Which product had the highest average units sold?,A & C both,B,A,C,D,C,"Averages: A = 110, B = 90, C = 155. C sold the most on average.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20829,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"Three numbers are such that when the average of any two of them is added to the third, the results obtained are 180, 168, and 150, respectively. What is the average of the original three numbers?",83,84,85,86,A,83,"If the sum is S, then “average of two + third” for third number c is (S − c)/2 + c = (S + c)/2 = 180, so S + c = 360. Likewise S + b = 336 and S + a = 300. Adding gives 4S = 996, so S = 249 and the average is 83.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20830,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,A school organized a field trip for 100 students and 10 chaperones. Each student was given a snack pack containing items equal to 15% of the total number of students. Each chaperone received a snack pack with items equal to 25% of the total number of students. How many snack items were distributed in total?,1750,2000,2250,2500,A,1750,Students: 100 × 15 (15% of 100) = 1500. Chaperones: 10 × 25 (25% of 100) = 250. Total 1750.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20831,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"Find the compound interest on ₹10,000 at 10% per annum for 2 years 6 months, compounded annually.","₹2,000","₹2,705","₹2,700","₹2,500",B,"₹2,705","Compounded annually for 2½ years: 10,000 × 1.1 × 1.1 × 1.05 = 12,705. CI = ₹2,705.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20832,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A certain amount invested at compound interest of 12% per annum, compounded annually, amounts to ₹3,136 in 2 years. What is 140% of the amount invested?","₹3,600","₹3,800","₹3,500","₹3,000",C,"₹3,500","P × 1.12² = 3136, so P = 3136/1.2544 = 2500. 140% of 2500 = ₹3,500.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20833,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"One type of pulses is sold for ₹72 per kg at a 20% profit. Another type is sold for ₹60 per kg at a 25% profit. If these two varieties are mixed in the ratio of 2:1 (first variety to second variety) and the mixture is sold at ₹70 per kg, what is the overall profit or loss percentage?",Profit of 50%,Loss of 25%,Profit of 25%,Loss of 50%,C,Profit of 25%,CPs: 72/1.2 = 60 and 60/1.25 = 48. Mixed 2 : 1: CP = (120 + 48)/3 = 56. Selling at 70 gives a profit of 14/56 = 25%.,Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20834,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A clothing store sold three dresses, D1, D2, and D3, whose selling prices were in the ratio 5:6:7. They made a profit of 20% on D1, a loss of 10% on D2, and a profit of 30% on D3. What was their approximate total profit or loss percentage for the entire sale?",profit of 12.25%,loss of 10.98%,profit of 10.98%,loss of 12.25%,C,profit of 10.98%,"Take SPs as 5, 6, 7. CPs = 5/1.2 = 4.167, 6/0.9 = 6.667 and 7/1.3 = 5.385, total 16.218. SP = 18, so there is a profit of 1.782/16.218 ≈ 10.98%. Note: SSC's official key marks (B) “loss of 10.98%”. The figure is right but the direction is wrong: it is a profit, so (C) is marked correct here.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20835,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A wholesaler marks up the price of a microwave oven by 60% above its cost price. He gives a 15% trade discount to a retailer. The retailer, in turn, marks up the price by 25% above his purchase price and offers a 10% festival discount to the customer. If the customer finally pays ₹14,490 for the microwave, what is the original approximate cost price of the oven to the wholesaler?","₹9,471","₹9,500","₹10,000","₹10,500",A,"₹9,471","Retailer's cost = 1.6C × 0.85 = 1.36C. Customer price = 1.36C × 1.25 × 0.9 = 1.53C = 14,490, so C ≈ ₹9,471.",Hard,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20836,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Percentage,English,A 60-litres solution of alcohol and water has 20% water. How many litres of alcohol must be added to the solution to make the water content 15%?,10 litres,20 litres,30 litres,40 litres,B,20 litres,"Water = 12 L. For water to be 15%, the total must be 12/0.15 = 80 L, so 20 L of alcohol is added.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20837,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Time, Work & Pipes",English,A can do a work in 8 days and B in 12 days. They work together for 3 days. What part of the work is left?,1/4,5/8,3/8,7/24,C,3/8,In 3 days together they do 3(1/8 + 1/12) = 3 × 5/24 = 5/8. Work left = 3/8.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20838,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A grocer mixes 40 kg of lentils costing ₹65 per kg with a certain quantity of lentils costing ₹80 per kg. If he sells the mixture at ₹75 per kg, making a 10% profit, what quantity of the second type of lentils did he mix?",25.98 kg,10.77 kg,35 kg,40 kg,B,10.77 kg,"CP of the mixture = 75/1.1 = 68.18. By alligation, (68.18 − 65) : (80 − 68.18) = second : first, so second = 40 × 3.18/11.82 ≈ 10.77 kg.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20839,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A and B can complete a task together in 12 days, while B and C can finish it in 16 days. After A works on it for 5 days and B for 7 days, C takes the remaining 13 days to finish the work. How many days would it take for C to complete the work alone?",24 days,16 days,20 days,18 days,A,24 days,5A + 7B + 13C = 1 can be written as 5(A + B) + 2(B + C) + 11C = 5/12 + 1/8 + 11C = 1. So 11C = 11/24 and C = 1/24: 24 days.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20840,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,"Profit, Loss & Discount",English,"A cyclist travels from City A to City B at an average speed of 20 km/h and takes 4 hours. If they want to complete the same journey in 2.5 hours, by what amount (in km/h) should they increase their average speed?",12 km/h,10 km/h,15 km/h,8 km/h,A,12 km/h,"Distance = 20 × 4 = 80 km. In 2.5 h the speed must be 32 km/h, an increase of 12 km/h.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20841,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,A train leaves Station A at 6:00 AM and travels towards Station B at a constant speed of 60 km/h. Another train leaves Station B at 8:00 AM and travels towards Station A at a constant speed of 90 km/h. The distance between the two stations is 540 km. At what time will the two trains meet?,9:48 AM,10:48 AM,11:45 AM,12:45 PM,B,10:48 AM,"By 8:00 AM the first train has gone 120 km, leaving 420 km. Closing speed 150 km/h, so 2.8 h = 2 h 48 min. They meet at 10:48 AM.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20842,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Mensuration,English,A circular garden having a diameter of 10 m is surrounded by a concrete path that is 1 m wide. Calculate the percentage increase in area resulting from the addition of the path.,18%,20%,44%,54%,C,44%,Radius goes from 5 m to 6 m. Area increase = (36 − 25)/25 = 44%.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20843,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,A sector of a circle having a radius 14 cm has area 154 cm². Find the angle of the sector.,90°,120°,150°,180°,A,90°,"Area = (θ/360) × (22/7) × 14² = (θ/360) × 616 = 154, so θ = 90°.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20844,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Trigonometry & Heights,English,"A circular signboard has a radius of 2 m. If painting costs ₹60 per m² and 10% of the board is left unpainted, what is the total painting cost?",₹658.2,₹678.6,₹630.4,₹681.9,B,₹678.6,Area = π × 2² ≈ 12.566 m². Painted 90% = 11.31 m². Cost = 11.31 × 60 ≈ ₹678.6.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20845,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Arithmetic & Quantitative,English,Find y-intercept of 4x + 5y = 20.,3,4,5,6,B,4,"At x = 0, 5y = 20 and y = 4.",Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
SSC-CGL-2025-T1-QA-EN-20846,SSC CGL,2025,Tier 1,2025-09-14,Shift 1,Quantitative Aptitude,Algebra,English,"Given, x + 1/x = 4 find the value of x³ + 1/x³.",55,57,52,50,C,52,x³ + 1/x³ = (x + 1/x)³ − 3(x + 1/x) = 64 − 12 = 52.,Medium,Verified,Verified (Official Response Sheet Key),2025 Tier 1 (2025-09-14 Shift 1),https://www.bookofexams.in/pyp/ssc-cgl/ssc-cgl-2025-tier-1-question-paper-14-september-shift-1/
